  ('zcrm_1579374000165907006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165907001', 'Christian Childs', NULL, '5-29-25 Christian Childs is 48 next month. Referred by Craig Schkade and some other female member of mine whose name he didn''t mention. Craig connected us first and via email. Christian worked for the same large company for the past 25 years. But he''s working for a new non-profit now and he''s offered benefits for $20 a month with a high $5K ded for him only, not for his family. His wife is 51, son 22, daughter 13. Son is looking for a job and he''s expecting him to get his own ins. But, I let him know the price is the same for 1 or more kids. He might as well add his son. Christian lost quite a bit of weight over the last few months. He''s working with a psychiatric nurse practitioner and taking Mounjaro for weight and he has sleep apnea. I told him it''s best to keep him on his company ins and put his wife and kids onto MPB. His wife get migraines and takes Nurtec 75 mg as needed. Could be related to cycle but not really clear. She''s hitting peri-menopause and I let him know that will be pre-x. She is being told to take HRT but she''s shying away from doing so. Their daughter is healthy and same for son. Christian watched the video, paused and repeated sections to really understand. He will share it with his wife.  He''s going to give his company 60 day notice but he''s guessing they may limit it to 30 or less. So, he might need July 1st or Aug. 1st benefits. Premium HSA is best and $1000/$676 $125/$25. His wife is a full time teacher in their school district. She may retire June 2026. Sounds like her benefits are expensive if they choose that path. She has a cottage bakery permit and does a side business for self-employment. Qualifies for MEC.  Sent Premium HSA Overview.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-30 14:04:10', '2025-05-30 14:04:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165741028', 'Steve Winter', NULL, '5-28-25 Steve was referred by Lady Fuller bc she was saying how happy she is with her membership. He was surprised to hear that. He''s 57 and is the owner of Matchstick Productions! They''ve won the most ski film awards in the industry! He started the biz in 1992.  He was in a helicopter crash when they were filming in Chile. He has rod in his back and partial paralysis in his left leg from the accident in 1997. He hasn''t had any problems of any kind that ''97. He just wears a brace on his leg which he pays for. He learned the value on self-pay back in the 90''s. He needed a wheel chair at the time and the price with ins was $6K. He asked for the cash price and it was $1200. He paid the cash price instead. This was a scam for this long!  Steve is interested in Premium Care or Premium HSA. Leaning towards Premium Care $299/$1000. He did a colonoscopy 5 years ago and it was fine. He''s not super interested in funding an HSA. Doesn''t really do the rest of the wellness visit but open to it. He also may share this with his company employees to join on their own if they wish.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 13:45:35', '2025-06-02 12:48:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165741008', 'Jill Kosdrosky', NULL, '5-28-25 Jill is 50 and husband is 54. They are only paying about $300 a month and then paying for all of their annual wellness screenings on their own. She figures they pay about $7000-$7500 per year for their membership with Medishare and all of their wellness screenings. So, she''s curious if they can get more for their money by including wellness in a membership. They are both self-employed. They also has a $12K AUA! They are coming from major corporate insurance prior to Medishare. He used to work for Bank of America and is now retired. They''ll get benefits once he turns 65. She used to work for a big corporation as well. They are used to full coverage with ins before Medishare. Jill had a minor hernia repair surgery in the past year or so. Otherwise, no pre-x, no meds, no smoking/tobacco etc. She also learned the value of self-pay! She was erroneously billed via insurance recently at $38K!  Once she corrected them and told them she was self-pay the new bill was $4200! Holy smokes. Yet one more example of the corruption of the insurance system.  She''s open to Premium Care or Premium HSA but will need to run the numbers.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 11:37:55', '2025-05-28 11:37:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165642008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165642003', 'Isabella Allegrezza', NULL, '5-27-25 Isabella is 33 and Michael is 34 and live in Longmont, CO. She''s transitioning into a role w/o benefits. She was referred by Jessica Muniz who is training her for her new position right now. She has UHC now and looked at individual plans and saw that they are crappy. Her husband has a job with benefits and he''s paying $50 a month on his own but to add her it''s $700 a month or per paycheck with a high $7K ded or close to that. They are healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco/smoking, no meds. They are looking to get pregnant in the next year or two but don''t really want to have the 6 month waiting period. They do wellness but just the very basic stuff like labs and sometimes pap screening. Not old enough for mammo or colonoscopy. With Premium Care it includes well child immunizations. She''s leaning towards Premium Care $1000/$603 MS possible Aug. 1st start date and knows July 18th deadline. I read some of the maternity section and she knows it twice her chosen IUA. Therefore, better to keep $1000 IUA over $1500. She watched the video. I will send her the overview now as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-27 11:48:46', '2025-05-27 11:48:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165458240', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165458230', 'Martha Gomez', NULL, '5-23-25 Jane says LifeX won''t work for 65+ unless already enrolled. LHS is not possible without Medicare Part A and B. ACA won''t work without citizenship and will be WAY too expensive for 78 year old. I left Martha a vm and let her know my findings. Not sure how else to help.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-23 16:39:24', '2025-05-23 16:39:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165458235', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165458230', 'Martha Gomez', NULL, '5-23-25 Martha Gomez recently became a US Citizen from Colombia. She''s trying to help her mom who is 78 gain citizenship as well. She has to show that they are not relying on government benefits for health ins. She''s trying to find out what she can buy for coverage for her mom. Her budget is $200-$300. She won''t qualify for C4 or any traditional option or most health shares. Her mom is in good health and just has osteoporosis. I let her know she may be able to get meds affordably but likely not health ins. I''m inquiring about LifeX as the only possibly option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-23 16:07:28', '2025-05-23 16:07:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165338078', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000124530031', 'Patti Owens', NULL, '5-20-25 Patti watched the video and is 59. Her son Josiah Owens enrolled in the past as well. He joined Secure HSA. She however does not do mammograms, colonoscopies, vax. So, Care+ is more up her alley. She sees a Functional Medicine Dr. and just spent $500 at Function Health to do a full lab panel for her knowledge. She''s a nutrition coach! She used Medishare many years ago and liked how they worked. She has a growth in her breast that they are watching. But, nothing has changed for all 3 years and it''s NOT cancer. They just check it every year to be safe.  She has a thyroid issue and Hashimotos for 25 years.  Nothing has changed and just lives a healthy lifestyle. Apparently has emphysema. She was diagnosed in about 2015 and nobody told her. Therefore, she''s not worried about it at all. I explained the pre-x clause thoroughly. She also heard it in the video. She does her own screenings which are much more comprehensive than ACA labs. She wants to maintain her freedom to choose her drs. and possible alternative treatments if ever needed. She uses a chiropractor for wellness as well. She likes CARE+ $352/$1000 and $125/$25. She cancelled her regular ins for May 31st and will be ok without ins for one month. She can''t make a decision that fast since she just started diving into this today. She will make a decision this week and call me when she''s ready.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-20 17:29:55', '2025-05-20 17:29:55'),
