  ('zcrm_1579374000158861115', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000158933001', 'Cheryl Branson', NULL, '2-5-25 Cheryl called again and is getting nervous without having ins since her job ended. She wants something for March 1st. No pre-x, single, 63 and turning 64 soon. We will talk on Tuesday, Feb. 11th, 9:00 am.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-05 15:59:14', '2025-02-05 15:59:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158354085', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000158357235', 'Megan Price', NULL, '1-30-25 Megan was referred by Jennifer Cribbs who is the wife of Amos Shuman. Megan has a family of 4, 34, 36 (soon 37), 5 and 19 months. Kids are both girls. Megan is a nurse working part-time with benefits. But, she''s looking to change that. They are paying $550 now with employer paying the rest. They earn about $100K and still get a decent APTC. But, sounds like she''d rather not have to worry about their income. Husband has 2 genetic issues. One is a small vsd in heart. He no no observable symptoms. They only accidentally discovered it in 2019 and there''s nothing to do with it. He was also born blind in one eye and had his eye removed and replaced with prosthetic eye. I read and emailed the sharing guidelines to her for Premium Care and Care+ so she can read it herself. I included the pre-x clause stipulations in the email as well. Nobody take any ongoing meds, no tobacco, no other health issues within the family. Although she mentioned one minor item with her daughter which I can''t remember. I let her know that falls into the pre-x clause as well. She was fine with that. I think it was for Occupational Therapy that she inquired about.  She''s excited about HAB as well. Will use wellness screenings, gym, dental, vision for husband, mental health maybe, and skin checks.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-30 19:00:08', '2025-01-30 19:00:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158158063', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000158212001', 'Cynthia Weiner', NULL, '1-29-25 Cynthia lives in Indiana - IN and is 59 1/2. She came to me via Carolyn Tabak. She''s in the process of getting divorced and needs benefits March 1st ideally. She might choose Cobra for a month or two but that''s really expensive. On ACA she can get a bronze plan for $454 after APTC with $7500 ded, and $9200 mop in-network or $15K ded oon and $18K mop for out of network. I described Premium Care $1000/$285 and HAB $107, plus $125/$25. She says it sounds too good to be true. She will use ACA wellness screenings, mammogram, labs, vax, dental, vision, gym (pays personal trainer $60 week), mental health is interested in using possibly. She most concerned about a massive catastrophic scenario, so I brought up life ins with LB. I will discuss with Mara. DOB is 6/28/65. She just has osteoporosis and treats it with working out and by eating yogurt, etc. She has no debt, expenses about $10K per month which she has covered by her savings or disbursements for about 30 more years. Both her parents died at age 84 and 86. She does has family history of pancreatic cancer on both sides. Credit is 780-820! Probably just price out small LB her peace of mind for chronic, critical or terminal illness.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-29 10:20:17', '2025-01-29 10:20:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157962013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157506001', 'Lisa Bollman', NULL, '1-27-25 Lisa is very interested for her whole family. Matt 42 and wife 27 are hesitant bc they used to have her on ACA as single mom with 2 kids and huge APTC. But, now they are married and still want what they had. Lisa was paying 50% of the employer plan last year which was $1100 or so, I think. He''s nervous bc he''s never heard of it. Lisa was offering many what if scenarios without knowing enough about Matt''s situation. So, I told her I need to have a conversation with him to best answer the questions. I also encouraged his wife joins the call and we can figure out the best path for the entire family. She agreed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 10:32:11', '2025-01-27 10:32:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157634079', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157658001', 'Shadee Ardalan', NULL, '1-23-25 Shadee was laid off Dec. 4th but paid through Dec. 31st. Then she got a $21K severance Jan. 15th. Then she will lose her ins on Jan. 31st. So, we used the Jan. 31st date for her Life Change Event. She was denied Medicaid on Jan. 15th due to her severance pay. Cobra will likely be around $800 but she needs to check with HR. Her letter shows $418 but that''s like x2. Lives in 80015. She needs injections of Stelara and can use the generic version. Her Dr. are Dr. Mark Gerich, Dr. Ryan O''Leary, Dr. Jamie Gibbs. Only Anthem Pathway plans include all 3 drs. and med. Dr. Gerich was the tough one to find in network. She cannot use any Essentials plans if she wants to keep Gerich.  We''re looking at Anthem Silver Pathway 2800 $0 Select Drugs for $302.88 her cost or Anthem Bronze Pathway 6000 $0 Select Drugs for $146.45. She wants to review it over the weekend and we will talk on Monday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-23 12:29:04', '2025-01-23 12:29:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157503013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157506001', 'Lisa Bollman', NULL, '1-22-25 Lisa is Sara Brandenburg Bollman''s Mother in Law. Her son is Sara''s husband. They recommended to call me.  Lisa is 58 and husband is 61. They are business owners.  They currently have Anthem BC/BS since Anthem is the only company that will offer a plan for only 5 employees. They have 3 family members and 2 employees and somehow that''s allowed with Anthem. The price keeps going up 15% each year if they keep the same plan, ie. 30% increase in two years. She''s tired of paying this. It''s $640.18 for EO. Their ded is $1500 in-network and $3000 out of network, $3000 mop in-network and $6000 out of network. They have ages ranging from Matt 42 and wife 27, employee at 28, 58 and Lisa at 58 and husband at 61. I described Premium Care and HAB since they also currently have dental and vision and possibly want well checks for Matt''s baby with their own pediatrician.  Lisa''s company is currently paying 50% of the cost of EO. I suggested she pays a flat dollar amount for everyone. Then some folks will have almost their entire cost paid by the employee which will be a huge savings for them. It would mean an extra $3600 per year for EO.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-22 12:30:58', '2025-01-22 12:30:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157503003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131707093', 'Isaiah Taylor', NULL, '1-22-25 Jane enrolled Isaiah for March 1st. Their company is paying for Isaiah. They chose Premium Care $1000/$237. They joined via ASHI and I removed the $100 fee for them. Isaiah doesn''t have any pre-x. He''s all set to go!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-22 10:04:26', '2025-01-22 10:04:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157394013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157361286', 'Katrin Murray Bonham', NULL, '1-21-25 Katrin is turning 64 in April 2025 and looking to retire in May. Her husband Donald is 7/27/59, on Medicare and retiring in March.  She doesn''t know what they will be pulling from investments to live on. She''s guessing perhaps $30K but will figure that out. They will not pull SS until age 70. APTC shows at $1042. She wants to keep Dr. Patrick Strickland and Dr. Nicholas Heter. She was recently diagnosed with CHF and needs to see her cardiologist. She''s also taking brand med called Ernesto. Cigna looks to be her best option to keep her Drs. and includes Ernesto. She will get through as much of the treatments she needs now on her current insurance plan.  She has a huge CSR at $30K so the plan has $100 ded and $1225 mop. I let her know if her income is more, the ded and mop may dramatically increase. She understands.  If she chooses Cobra it will be $1800-$1900 a month! She''s only paying $80-$90 a month herself now. Employer is paying almost all of the cost. She will reach out in March or April.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-21 13:30:46', '2025-01-21 13:30:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157305016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157181240', 'Alyssa Childs', NULL, '1-14-25 and 1-20-25 Alyssa came to me via Bev. She and her family just lost Medicaid. She''s 31. I just called her back today bc I can''t find my notes. She apologized for not calling me back. Her case worker forgot to submit her information to be approved for Medicaid. So, they are approved and she''s all set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-20 11:58:47', '2025-01-20 11:59:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157241071', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000157220371', 'Nick Zurko', NULL, '10-8-24 Nick is 40 and came to me via Donna Baker. Lives in OH. He was on Medicaid and got stuck on it for 4 years bc of covid policies. Has a Dr. at Cleveland Clinic and psychiatrist. Has ADHD and takes Adderall 1x daily 20mg. He''s weary of an HMO bc in a small town and was with Oscar. Sounds like that caused trouble for him. No tobacco, no pre-x otherwise. Wellness he says yes to well checks, dental, mental health 1x per month, labs, flu shot. His boss is a nutrition counselor. Knows Donna through wellness via nutrient dense foods. Discussed Care+ $2500/$205 and HAB $107 = $312.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-17 22:15:18', '2025-01-17 22:15:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157241055', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156941238', 'Anahita Safavi', NULL, '1-17-25 Anahita called back to understand the pre-x clause with her husband on the phone. I re-read the Genetic Mutation section to her. She seemed a bit suck on what it means for her and her daughter. I explained the prosthetic leg will be at their expense and not shared. Then she revealed the other day the she needs to use catheters for her bladder issue. She''s gotten the catheters for a very discounted price before and wasn''t worried about that. Now she''s concerned again about her genetic issues. She will discuss it with her husband.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-17 16:29:15', '2025-01-17 16:29:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156942102', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156941238', 'Anahita Safavi', NULL, '1-15-25 Anahito came to me via Maureen Killough. She''s 60 and her daughter is 22 and husband is turning 65 in March, 24 2025. They live in Burlingame, CA. Therefore, they can only have Secure HSA. They currently have Anthem BC/BS and used to have Kaiser. They are totally done with supporting these companies and the crazy costs. They are paying $1400 for  a low bronze plan for all three of them. When her husband drops off she was looking at increasing the plan to a silver plan but it will cost $1600 for her and her daughter! Maureen speaks very highly of her membership and she had no idea that other options exist. She says they do have pre-x but it turns out they are genetic issues they were both born with. Her daughter has a prosthetic leg since. She has a kidney and bladder issue she was born with. She said there''s nothing she does to treat these. I will ask more questions tomorrow and review the sharing guidelines with her for genetic defects.
15. Genetic Mutation
Sharing requests resulting from a genetic mutation that existed prior to membership are
subject to the same limitations as other pre-membership medical conditions. If the member
did not receive a diagnosis, require treatment, present symptoms, or take medication for the
genetic mutation in the 24 months prior to membership, sharing requests related to the
condition may not be subject to pre-membership medical condition limitations.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-15 20:15:03', '2025-01-15 20:15:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156942013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131707093', 'Isaiah Taylor', NULL, '1-15-25 Jane Taylor, Isaiah''s mom called again to help sort out the best options for her son, his wife and soon to arrive baby. Isaiah had to wait 2 years to get reimbursed from Solidarity for when he had his appendix taken out unexpectedly. Isaiah is turning 29 on Feb. 25th. His wife has regular ins and is due to have their baby late March. So, Jane wanted pricing for all scenarios, ie. MO, MC, MF. I gave the rundown for Care+ and Premium Care. She''s choosing Premium Care bc of the additional benefits, more IUA levels, better pre-x clause moving forward, etc. They don''t seem to desire alternative care either. I think they''ll have a better member experience with Premium Care at this point as well. I sent her all of the prices for Premium Care for all ages once he turns 30 as well. We will revisit on Friday at 10:00 am to enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-15 11:42:38', '2025-01-15 11:42:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156759129', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156781359', 'Rachael Warner', NULL, '1-14-25 Rachael is 42 and lives in Boulder, CO 80301. She came to me via Shoshana Kressler. She watched the video. She lost Medicaid in Sept. and has been going without ins since then. She really just wants dental and vision. She said no to tobacco but she smokes pot 2x a day! So, MCS isn''t a good idea. Also her income turns out to be $46K once she plugged it into C4. At first she thought it was $30K-$40K. So, I ran the numbers at $35K. The cost was close to what she could afford bc false APTC of $328. But, when she filled it out correctly her APTC was about $184.70. Now the cheapest plans were about $250 for basically nothing until you spend $7K. So, she decided to continue to go without insurance and pay for her wellness visits on her own.  She couldn''t understand why the plans are so bad and why it''s not affordable contrary to what she''s told. She also wants dental and needs a periodontist. I shared 1Dental with her which she''s interested in. But, she''s in no rush to pay for it until she''s ready to move forward with a dentist. She will keep my link and let me know if/when she enrolls.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-14 19:30:47', '2025-01-14 19:30:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156759043', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156781131', 'Stacy Gladwell', NULL, '1-13-25 Stacy DOB 4/29/1974 and Robyn DOB 970-201-5335. No pre-x. Robyn is a truck driver and Stacy goes with him on the road sometimes. They want a plan that will work nationwide. Their expected income is $90K and can get a $502.60 APTC. So, lowest cost plans start at $404 for the two of them. BUT, they can''t really use it out of state or out of network other than ER. So, I showed the AC $5000 Gig Care PPO HSA for the nationwide network. She doesn''t know much about MCS, so I sent her the video to watch as well. For Gig Care $1,156.62 per Month for Employee + Spouse. They will decide and let me know ASAP. We lost our connection but I had already sent them everything to review and left them a vm. Oh, Stacy has scoliosis and that''s about it for pre-x.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-13 17:29:27', '2025-01-13 21:08:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156375146', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156399324', 'Shauna Monkman', NULL, '1-9-25 Shauna is 48 turning 49 in April. She came to me via Daniela Papi. She watched the 9 minute video. She has 2 health items to note. She has Lyme disease that is in remission bc working with a naturopath in WA to help her virtually. She has a fused spine which she treats naturally with yoga, stretching, castor oil, etc. No tobacco, no meds for a while. She in between TX and CA now and has a MediCal plan for $0. But, she''s paying everything on her own right now since nothing she does is covered by ins. She will be spending more time in TX and will claim as her primary residence. She likes HAB to be able to see her naturopath for wellness screenings. She also does dental, vision maybe, thermogram, gym, mental health maybe, skin maybe, nutrition probably not since had to educate herself long ago. We discussed Premium Care primarily since she''ll be turning 50 in 1 year and 4 months which incurs a large price increase. I read the alternative care section from the Sharing Guidelines for Sedera and the chiropractic care section. Those are the areas she may want to use. She''s going to think about it all and it could be many months before she makes a decision. She wants to make sure it will benefit her if she''s going to pay all of that money.  Quoted $1000/$285 + $107 or $1500/$254 + $107 and $125/$25.  She''s all set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-09 12:51:15', '2025-01-09 12:51:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156375087', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156166043', 'Jamie Gutthridge', NULL, '1-9-25 Jamie doesn''t qualify for AC plans bc of his back issues and he had a shoulder surgery within the past 5 years also. They are working with a broker named Emma. But, she''s hasn''t been as helpful as they wish.  He might like to change to my assistance but I don''t want to steal them away if she''s spent a bunch of time with them. Their accountant helped them realize they can input thei income from last year as a guide for 2025. I let him know it will have to be input at self employment income.  Beth has a little self employment income. So, they are getting a tax credit at the moment but would prefer to just pay if I found a good off exchange or MCS option. I let him know Beth could join MCS and he can keep his Anthem Essentials plan. His drs. were in the network for his plan in Dec. and should still be for 2025 with Boulder Medical Ctr.  He will discuss with Beth and get back to me.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-09 11:18:31', '2025-01-09 11:18:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156310067', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156330011', 'Rano Samadova', NULL, '1-8-25 Rano is 55 and asked her son Amir to help since she and her husband don''t speak english well. They just arrived in the US in 2024. They do not have health ins. They both have SS#''s. They want preventive screenings and co-pays for dr. visits and lowest cost. Their household income will be about $30K-$35K in 2025. Amir will follow my instructions to add their income into C4 and select me as their Agent. Then we will revisit on Tues. Jan. 14th to meet the deadline to get ins. for them for 2025.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 16:28:11', '2025-01-08 16:28:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156174082', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156166081', 'Scott Grubb', NULL, '1-7-25 Scott is turning 62 soon. He''s an ASHI member and the site link needs to be updated bc it''s not working anymore on ASHI. Scott is self-employed. Live in KS. He''s paying $369 now with a $6K ded and $20K MOP! He''s looking for something more comprehensive for the money. He has a prostate issue 10-15 years ago which is totally finenow. He''s done colonoscopies every 5 years now. He went about 2 years ago and they removed polyps, he believes. He''s had spots on his skin removed but nothing of concern recently. He thinks the one spot that was a concern and removed was over 3 years ago. He takes meds to control his blood pressure and cholesterol but he might go off of those soon bc he''s doing so well. No tobacco or smoking. He''s in no rush since he has ins already but would love something better. We discussed Premium Care since he''s 62 and I will send him HAB info to review as well, in case he''s interested in more than just colonoscopy. I let him know of the 6 month waiting period for preventive colonoscopy. He''s very interested.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-07 20:07:14', '2025-01-07 20:07:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156174042', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073533045', 'Donald Coy', NULL, '1-7-25 Don wanted to revisit his options for Linda and himself. He''s working with Andrea for Medicare and I just reiterated what we spoke about in May. Linda does has a knee issue but is not likely to do anything for it for many more years. So, he''s not worried about that for now. Linda will be 62 this year. She likes Cigna also and wants to keep her drs. But, they will have to pay far more for far less benefits, depending on their income for 2025. I told him to contact me in early March for April 1st effective. He turns 65 in July so there''s time for him as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-07 11:19:34', '2025-01-07 11:19:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156174018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000156166043', 'Jamie Gutthridge', NULL, '1-6-25 Jamie is 53 turning 54 in Feb. 2025, Beth is 55. They have been on corporate benefits for 20+ years with CVS/Aetna. They went onto C4 for Dec. But, now they don''t have any income to show and not enough investment income to show to get over the Medicaid threshold. They do NOT want Medicaid. They aren''t super comfortable putting in something not 100% accurate of course! They prefer to go outside of C4. They live in or near Boulder and are both active, no tobacco. Beth take meds for ADD called methyphenodate ie. ridulin, Zoloft and some for Raynaud''s. Jamie had a spinal fusion about 7 years ago. He''s had 3 surgeries. But, he''s doing well now and doesn''t foresee anything in the near future. He sees his GP 1x per year to check on general wellness. He had a colonoscopy 2 years ago and that checked out well also. He inquired about possibly paying for reg insurance for the year at least to protect himself for his back issues. Sounds like they have the money to protect themselves as well. He gets injections sometimes for his back. They can afford to pay cash for that if needed. He did one back in Sept. or Oct. They are leaning towards $1500 IUA / $507 + $200 HAB = $707. They see HAB as no brainer as well. They are active and have a gym membership and will use many of the wellness benefits. They will review everything and we are meeting again on Thursday, Jan. 9th.  All set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-06 16:09:16', '2025-01-06 16:09:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155122023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000153692106', 'Jack Ziemer', NULL, '12-18-24 Jack is deciding to go without any benefits for now. He''s paid for years and just want to roll the dice for now. He''s tired of wasting his money on healthcare that he never uses. But, he might change his mind. He''s also open to reminders down the road. So, I''ll keep him in Leads and communicate with him on  occasion.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-18 16:12:01', '2024-12-18 16:12:01'),
