  ('zcrm_1579374000153917069', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000153885368', 'Nick Medina', NULL, '12-15-24 Nick and his wife are both 59. Nick came to me via Mara Simoneau. He''s been with Kaiser for many years and they are threatening to cancel his plan for payment troubles. He was thinking of just putting his wife onto MCS bc he has rheumatoid arthritis. They have him taking an infusion 2x per year. They tried to charge his $4K and he refused. Then they discounted it to $2K but between that and paying $950 per month, it''s killing him financially. Plus he pays $750 for his wife. So, they''re paying $1700 per month and could be paying $733. He can save $1000 per month to help pay for the infusions. I found them on pharmacy checker for about $700-$750 per vial. He''s need to find a dr. to administer it. He understands the pre-x clause. But, saving $12K per year simply on the monthly payment could really help them. They live in San Diego, CA. Wife takes no meds, no tobacco and no health issues in past 24 months. He will watch the video with her and read the overview I will send now. He knows of the 20th of the month deadline for Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-05 20:28:12', '2024-12-05 20:28:12'),
