  ('zcrm_1579374000144226184', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144228275', 'Chris Weeks', NULL, '8-7-24 Chris is 37 and his wife (Amy?) is 37 also. I met them at a BSU dinner. They run the EE Systems in Boulder and moved here from CA. They prefer alternative, natural healing solutions. They aren''t interested in mainstream wellness. No pre-x, no tobacco, no meds, some supplements.  They currently pay $1700 for Cobra with BC/BS PPO with an $850 ded/$3900 MOP and 20% co-ins. They also have Delta Dental and VSP. He''s open to starting Sept. 1st instead of waiting until Cobra runs out in Feb. 2025. They are also wanting great maternity benefits which this has. Quoted him CARE+ $1000 / $450 and $125/$25. I mentioned the wellness stuff and cost. They would use dental, vision and gym. I''m not sure it'' worth it for them. I will also send them the Dental Discount Plan for possible bridge need for his wife.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-07 20:14:49', '2024-08-07 20:14:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144115081', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144154060', 'John Wessling', NULL, '8-2-24 Secondary email - johnwessling@sbcglobal.net.   John came to me via ASHI and is an inspector in Missouri. He''s 60, Katie, 54, daughters 25 and 22. His daughters might join other ins. Eldest is on an ACA plan for and she is pre-diabetic and has anxiety. Youngest has migraines and other issues that he will have his wife share with me bc he doesn''t know. He has metabolic syndrome which means he''s diabetic with blood pressure issues. However, he''s working towards weaning off all meds and he''s having success with it so far!  His endocrinologist is the one who is helping him to end meds while his other dr. just pushes the meds. I read the diabetes guidelines for Premium Care and let him know he''s responsible for his meds. He already went off of Trulicity for a few months and his levels didn''t change. So, he doesn''t think he''ll be using that again. He also takes metformin. His wife takes a blood pressure med as well. I quoted him Premium Care MF at $1000/$837 or $1500/$741 + $250 HAB = $1087 or $991. I also quoted him MS since he thinks the kids may be on their own $575/$1000 or $507/$1500 + $165 = $740 or $672. I also let him know of his $100 discount which makes it $25/$25 enrollment and annual renewal.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-02 11:54:32', '2024-08-02 11:54:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144115071', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144114255', 'Ray Baum', NULL, '8-1-24 Ben DiSalle (Financial Advisor) referred Ray to me regarding his wife. She is 61 now with her DOB on July 25th. She has high blood pressure which she has been lowering with her diet. She takes supplements as well such as magnesium. No hospitalizations for blood pressure and it''s very well managed. Ray lives in Broomfield and she lives in Pueblo. They they drive and meet up on the weekends. He is 66 1/2 and paying for Medicare. He wished there were a solution like this for folks his age. Discussed Premium Care $285/$1000 and HAB $107 = $392 and $125/$25. He knows regular ins will be much more expensive.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-01 16:36:43', '2024-08-01 16:36:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144115043', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144114236', 'Sara Cadwell', NULL, '7-30-24 Mike and Sara were sent to me via Chris Cadwell. Mike is 60 and Sara is 52.  His company let him go on Friday. Cobra will be $2600 for a family of 3 or 4. Daughter takes anti depressants. Mike takes meds for high blood pressure, cholesterol, testosterone, enlarged prostate. Sara takes lipitor, estradiol injections, progesterone, valtrax as needed. She had a TIA in the past and also takes a baby aspirin. Once they shared all of this and I pressed about their pre-x, they realized they don''t want MCS, but want C4HCO since there are no pre-x limitations. He will have a SEP for loss of coverage July 31st.  They want Dr. Mia Lynch and Dr. Jason Friedrich in Denver and Aurora. They daughter Sydney will remain on the plan and her DOB is 8/1/2002.  Select Health and Anthem are the carriers who accept their Drs.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-01 14:33:54', '2024-08-08 13:16:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144115003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144114001', 'David Pietsch', NULL, '7-31-24 David Pietsch is 62, wife 60, daughter 23 and twins at 21.  They have Anthem right now with his current job that he''s about to resign from. He has a new job without benefits. He''s looking for Sept. 1st start date. He was referred by Julie Oldham primarily but also Karen Pierson. I discussed Premium Care due to their ages and CARE+ due to a possible pre-x that he''s going to find out the date. It might be close to getting outside of the 2 year pre-x clause. David had A-fib around 2 years ago and they discovered sleep apnea. Now he uses a c-pap machine and no problems since. He can go onto Medicare to play it safe for up to 18 months. I suggested he goes onto Cobra for just himself and puts the rest of his family onto MCS. I gave him pricing for both memberships. He''s very interested in HAB as well and will use much of it. He wants to share the video with his wife and written information.  Premium Care MC $533/$1000 or MF $837/$1000 + HAB $200 or $250. CARE+ is $615/$1000 MC or $875/$1000 MF + HAB $200 or $250.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-01 11:31:47', '2024-08-01 11:31:47');

