  ('zcrm_1579374000140473078', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000140470156', 'Krystle Mulnix', NULL, '6-7-24 Krystle is an ASHI member and has a family of 4. They live in PA, so only CARE+ or Secure HSA as options. She will be 43 in Aug. 2024 and husband John is 42, kids 9 and 7. They pay $600 a month through large employer and employer paying the rest of the cost. They have a $2K ded and not sure of the mop. No pre-x, no tobacco. Only real health issue is migraines and very expensive med. I looked up Ubrelvy, Ajovy, Aimovig, Emgality and Qulipta which were all in the $1000''s. The final possible choice was Phenergen with the generic version promethazine which was only $7!  They do all of the typical wellness, dental, vision, gym for one daughter, no nutritional health needs and no mental health needs.  They take supplements sometimes as well.  I quoted CARE+ and HAB $1000/$635 and HAB $250 = $885 plus the $125/$25 with $100 waived as an ASHI member.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-09 23:11:21', '2024-06-09 23:11:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000140473073', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000140470146', 'Melissa Helman', NULL, '5-31-24 Melissa Helman 40 and Akbar Torshizad 52 have been off of any healthcare for 2 months now. Melissa has been a student for this past year and has Medicaid now. But, she''s about to start a new job as  a pre-school teacher in Aug. She will need something by then. She gets her pap screenings and mammos which she started doing at 38 years old.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-09 23:02:02', '2024-06-09 23:02:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139993028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000140002055', 'Sharon Jackson', NULL, '5-28-24 Sharon came to me via Carlene Frusteri! Sharon is 58, husband 54 and daughter 14. She has a PMA for her health and fitness instructor business. She didn''t have time to watch the 9-minute video yet. She currently paying nothing through ACA since not reporting income. But, she''d much prefer to remove herself from traditional ins. She prefers holistic care as well as acu and chiro. She likes to get some blood work done, EKG, skin check, thermogram and colonoscopies as her preventive visits. She also does dental cleanings, vision screenings and pap screenings and pays for gym or some form of it. She doesn''t need mental health benefits. She''s interested in CARE+ and HAB. Can''t do Premium Care since they live in NY!!  So, CARE+ $875/$1000 EF + HAB $165 ES (don''t really need it for daughter) = $1040.  This is perfectly in alignment with what she was hoping and expecting the price to be close to. However, she doesn''t need to focus on this until 2025! I will email CARE+ and HAB info.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-29 16:34:06', '2024-05-29 16:34:06'),
