  ('zcrm_1579374000139728003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000139726001', 'Anand Ghanvat', NULL, '5-23-24 Anand is 31 and wife Pooja is 29. They currently live with Santiago Mussi Tiscornia. They are planning to start a family soon. They are both healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco or smoking and no drinking. They watched the 9-minute video. The don''t do any wellness screenings at all, no dental cleanings, no skin checks, nothing. CARE+ is the best for their needs at $1000/$450 and $125/$25. Doesn''t make sense to put them on Premium memberships. They want to read the Maternity Guide and CARE+ Overview. We will talk again next week at noon on Tuesday, May 28th for a July 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-23 10:23:50', '2024-05-23 10:23:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139452104', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000139470004', 'Brett Rubenstein', NULL, '5-20-24 Brett''s DOB i 12/22/70 and wife Carolyn is 8/21/1977. Came to me via Kimberly Hirst and her husband Steve (?). I believe they came via Andrea Hinman. Brett is leaving his teaching position and needs insurance for himself and 2 kids for July 1st. He''s healthy, no meds other than using an albuterol inhaler periodically. He''s never been hospitalized for asthma. No other meds and no tobacco. He currently has an UHC Choice Plus Platinum plan that he only pays $300 towards every month.  It has a $500 ded indiv and $1000 per famiy with mop of $4500 indiv and $9000 (?) family. If he is added to his wife''s plan it will cost them an extra $2400!  Their household income will be about $120K in 2024. I shared with him the RMHP Bronze 0 bc it''s the only company that include all of their drs. Dr. Jonathan Aaron Smith, Dr. Emily Elizabeth Porternand Dr. Katelyn Marie Uhlemann.  I also shared the America''s Choice with him. Brett and 2 kids it will cost $629.  He''s nervous about the $500K cap. With C4 he may get a $386 APTC and his cost of the plans are in the $700''s. So, it''s reassonable comprared the the $2400. He will look it over and give me a call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-20 21:24:12', '2024-05-20 21:24:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139111163', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000136256074', 'Amy Hollander', NULL, '5-15-24 I reached Amy and she''s still fighting with Cigna to cover her. They might back date to May 1st. She''s uncovered at the moment if they don''t. She''s going on a river trip and nervous about that! MCS is possible but only with MEC to show proof of insurance. But, if she can qualify for America''s Choice that is a good option and for sure will qualify as health insurance for her Emgality med to be free for one year. She will also find out if they have a cash price for it direct from the manufacturer. She wants June 1st start date for sure and knows of 20th of the month deadline.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-15 16:53:42', '2024-05-15 16:53:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139111158', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000136256074', 'Amy Hollander', NULL, '5-15-24 Left vm to reschedule and deal with her challenges with C4 and no good option with Emgality at a reasonable cost. Also she''s in PT and getting PRP as self-pay. No surgery in her future. Possible America''s Choice instead but not certain with her pre-x. Emgality is for migraines.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-15 16:36:03', '2024-05-15 16:36:03'),
