  ('zcrm_1579374000137991107', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000137990230', 'Jay Leber', NULL, '4-25-24 Jay is on Medicaid right now but might not qualify once he figures out his taxes. He thinks he''ll show a negative balance. But, if not he''s curious about MCS and HAB. He wasn''t ready to jump into HAB so quickly and now seems more interested in MCS. We will connect upon my return. His business is Total Speed and he helps with all types of internet site and marketing needs 24/7/365 with some help with staff in Indonesia, not China or India. I met him at The One Business Connection networking event through Teresa at Sherpa''s.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-25 17:34:41', '2024-04-25 17:34:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000137764031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000137824039', 'Karen McKay', NULL, '4-23-24 Karen McKay lives in Louisville and was referred by her mental health counselor Jennifer Favell after Jennifer''s client used HAB. Jennifer shared it with Karen. Karen has employer coverage but the mental health benefits only kick in after she pays a $4K ded. She''s also exhausted the Marshall Fire donated hours from the counselors. She still needs help. She will think about whether or not she wants to join and let me know. She''s not ready to join for May 1st and knows I''ll be out of town until May 6th otherwise.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-23 16:34:44', '2024-04-23 16:34:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000137531011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000135095020', 'Emily Campbell', NULL, '4-18-24 Emily called and was ready to choose a Cigna with APTC if she could confirm that the MEC her company was offering didn''t qualify as creditable coverage. I asked Ann Eisenhart if she can get an APTC since her company is offering her an ACA compliant affordable MEC. She cannot get an APTC. So, now the price of everything is above her comfort level. Kaiser cheapest and worst plan is around $274. CARE+ is still too expensive. The only solution is direct to Sedera or Zion at this point or she will go without anything. I sent her the video to review to see if it resonates with her or not.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-18 16:10:26', '2024-04-18 16:10:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136995026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000136989014', 'Michelle Horton', NULL, '4-10-24 Michelle is 53 and husband is turning 58 soon. Husband was laid off last June and they joined ACA with an APTC and still pay just under $900 a month for UHC with a high ded of $8200. She watched the video. She has a thyroid issue and uses Armour Thyroid for about $30 a month. Husband has high blood pressure and pre-diabetes. He recently lost a ton of weight to help. She also was a user of Gastroenterology of the Rockies and was hit with an $8K bill! She knows the whoa''s of ins. They are considering CARE+ $1000/$615 + HAB $165 = $780 and no need for APTC as well. They are both retired.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-10 16:09:04', '2024-04-10 16:09:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136995003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000136989001', 'Dave Hasstedt', NULL, '4-10-24 Sent to me by Andrea Hinman. Dave is 61 and wife Carol is 58 this year. Dave is retired and his wife is retiring from Cherry Creek School System in May. Her benefits run out at the end of July. They are telling her she has to have something in place by the end of May which doesn''t make sense. They want medical, dental and vision. The do Not want Kaiser. They are also not interested in MCS. They are traditional. Dave is on Lexipro for anxiety. Otherwise, no pre-x, no tobacco and no other meds. PARA will be $1500 a month. Income is about $110K, so subsidy will be limited. We will talk again when he''s not at work.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-10 11:52:24', '2024-04-10 11:52:24'),
