  ('zcrm_1579374000136261023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000136256074', 'Amy Hollander', NULL, '3-29-24 Amy, 61 came to me via Robin Brenneise.  Amy got laid off and plans to retire. She needs PT for a lower back SI joint pain issue that won''t need surgery. It''s bc of one leg being shorter than the other. She''s working with a broker right now and needs April 1st start date. I told her to get the C4 plan which will cost her about $540 for now. She needs to do about 10 more sessions of PT which may be a few months. She also needs med called Emgality 120 mg pen and it''s a class 4 drug. She can get it cheap or free with a coupon if she shows commercial ACA compliant ins. We are going to revisit this in mid-May to see what options I have available at that time. She also takes HRT with progesterone and estradiol .025 mg patch, plus Lexapro. She wants to do the annual wellness visits as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-29 17:08:33', '2024-03-29 17:13:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136233006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000135324074', 'Christina Lanotte', NULL, '3-29-24 Tina was going to abort mission on all options since she was overwhelmed and the cost was going to be higher than they were comfortable with. So, I let her know that we can drop the wellness benefit and raise the IUA. I also gave her the 1Dental Discount plan as option for dental and vision. She chose to join for the family at $179 + $20 set up fee.  As for medical she was going to go without insurance or MCS altogether. Since Midnight Metals via Paula Chavez is paying half they don''t qualify for APTC and the low cost plans are pretty terrible. So, I suggested CARE+ for any new health issues to at least protect them on that front. She understands the pre-x clause means that anything related to Nathan''s previous cancer won''t be shared at all in the first year and then the tiered sharing after that. She said he was cleared of cancer in Jan. 2024.  She''s completing the app now and is calling Paula to get their payment information to complete the enrollment. Start date will be May 1st for CARE+. Dental might start right away. She looked and thinks it will start right away. We have to wait until Monday to complete the CARE+ enrollment since the HR or Billing person is not in the office today to provide the payment information. She will complete most of what we did already on her own and we''ll talk at 1:00 to finish it up. She also knows there''s no preventative care included in CARE+. But, she will get discounts on dental cleanings and eye exams with 1Dental. For CARE+ $1000 it will be $685 bc she''s a tobacco user under age 50. She knows that once she hits 50, we will need to find a new option since this will have serious limitations. That''s 4 years away.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-29 09:51:28', '2024-03-29 09:51:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136117046', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000135324074', 'Christina Lanotte', NULL, '3-27-24 Christina is 46 1-16-78 and tobacco user. Husband Nathan is 45 10-13-78 and daughter Emma is 8 4/9/2015. Live in CO Springs, 80922. They were referred to me by Andrea Hinman via Paula Chavez. Paula is their employer and will pay half of their cost. They recently got kicked off Medicaid Jan. 31st and ideally need ins. for April 1st. She''s super interested in MCS. Nathan just had non-invasive bladder cancer this past year and it''s showing as cleared in Jan. 2024. I told her MCS is not a good idea. So, we looked at Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 for $492.89 for Nathan with $9450 mop. Christina is willing to pay the extra $50 fee for tobacco use. We will have to find a new option for her once she turns 50. She''s ok with that. We discussed CARE+ for $450+$50/$1000 or $360+$50/$2500 and $125/$25. She interested in doing the stool test for colon cancer check and not colonoscopy. She does mammo every year and yes for dental cleaning and vision screening. No to gym membership or nutritional health. For HAB EC $200 mo. Total cost will be around $1000 split in half for employer and employee.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-27 15:56:39', '2024-03-27 15:56:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136117026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000135095020', 'Emily Campbell', NULL, '3-27-24 Emily sounds like she actually doesn''t qualify for an APTC. Her income i $36K and an affordable plan would be about $270 a month. She''s not sure if they offered her something for that price. The cheapest plan were terrible that she didn''t want. So, I explained CARE+ and she''s not really open to that at this point. It''s too different for her comfort level. She''s healthy and the generic med is topical and she''s not worried about it. But, she really wants to get the APTC. She will call her employer and see what she can learn or choose the cheapest C4 plan that she can find. I can''t login still since my email isn''t working to get the code.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-27 13:13:30', '2024-03-27 13:13:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136051008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000135324064', 'Sande Golubich', NULL, '3-26-24 Sande is looking for group insurance for a small group of 4-5 employees. There are 2 owners and possibly 2-3 technicians. The technicians might have ins from spouses. She has no idea at this point. But, they have a min of 2 owners and their families. The other owners just had a baby with many health complications at this point. So, they won''t be interested in MCS. Sande watched the video and said it would suit her family but likely not the others, so she wants to stick with reg. ins. They don''t need it until Jan. 2025. We will hold off on quoting until we have new pricing for 2025. She will call be before Nov. They own a restaurant and hospitality equipment repair company. They also might add 2 more technicians in year 2. She''s all set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-26 12:39:10', '2024-03-26 12:39:10'),
