  ('zcrm_1579374000134587276', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '3-4-24 Genevieve has tried to get the Cobra information from Swedish Medical where William works and they won''t give it to her yet. They are working on an offer to keep him or something along those lines. He''s not going to stay. We''ve set a time for March 18th to potentially enroll Genevieve and some or all kids. Olivia might be best served on Cobra with William. Once they have the numbers they can make an educated decision. He probably will work independently. One place might give him an allowance for medical which would work well for their needs. She will keep me posted. But, they are leaving on Friday for a family vacation until March 17th.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-04 15:25:02', '2024-03-04 15:25:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134587011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134593001', 'Kathy Morris', NULL, '3-4-24 Kathy Morris came to me via Linda Johnston and her husband Jim. They all go to church together. Kathy is a resident of TX and CO. She seems to live in or near Loveland/Berthoud when in CO. She''s not employed. She''s healthy, no real pre-x other than she takes hormones, she has restless legs and takes ambien for sleep. She''s already doing self-pay and sees the tremendous value in doing so. She got her mammo at Banner Imaging for $204 and her wellness lab work for $175 at Horizons Laboratory for her blood work. She''s able to pay only $18 a month for the YMCA nationwide bc she shows her W2 where she''s not employed now. She doesn''t have any ins now and see how broken the ACA system is. She really just wants to be protected for big health issues. She likely doesn''t want to include wellness but still wants to see the info about wellness. She wants to do her research and will ask Linda and Jim again about their experience with MCS and MPB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-04 11:15:16', '2024-03-04 11:15:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134197035', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '02-26-24 Andrea Hinman sent them to me via Dr. Brent Penman (?). William is a DR himself at Swedish Hospital. He''s ending his employment there on March 31st. They have 4 kids, 3 are out of state for school. They are 24, 22, 21 and 19. Dr. William has cardiac history with an open heart surgery in 2019 and sees a cardiologist 1x per year. They are less concerned about that and more concerned about his 4 meds for diabetes, Repatha 140 mg, Jardiance 25 mg, Rosuvastatin 20 mg and Mounjaro 5 mg. Willing to take generic versions. They get them every 90 days and 4 x year refills. Daughter Olivia has IBS problems and takes Ibsrela but that is super expensive $1700 month. They might press her to take Linzess 145 mg instead. All of these are covered by RMHP but Dr. Christopher Courtney is not in-network. They''d rather change drs. than mess with the medication coverage. Dr. William can accept Cobra if he wants. He''ll talk with his HR person to find out the cost for just him or him and Olivia. Yes, Genevieve did her first mammogram and had never heard of a thermogram. Her daughters do their pap screenings. They are interested in CARE+ $615 and HAS $200 = $815 plus Dr. William and Olivia''s plan. I sent them all scenarios. They are also originally from Canada. They do not qualify for any subsidy since their income is $1M.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-26 16:22:17', '2024-02-26 16:22:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133914062', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000133952095', 'Debbie Kilcullen', NULL, '2-21-24 Debbie is 52 and came to me via Judi Snyder. She quit her job last May from a job of 25 years. She currently has a huge APTC since she has very little income. She''s paying $125 for medical FL BC/BS and $25 for dental. She''s looking at a new part time job but is concerned about her benefits when she''s earning more. I explained CARE+ since she''s not self-employed. The entire process of MCS makes her super nervous. She doesn''t think it''s the right fit for her which is fine. But, she might change her mind once she sees her options. I told her I''d still send her the link again to the video to help her wrap her head around it, as well as the written overview and wellness benefit. CARE+ $350 and possibly wellness $107 = $457.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-21 20:33:12', '2024-02-21 20:33:12'),
