  ('zcrm_1579374000133343208', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000133325125', 'Donna Rempala', NULL, '2-13-24 Donna is turning 60 in April. She''s a retired nurse. Her husband is a pilot, employed at American Airlines for about 32 years. He now works 2 days a week. He possibly wants to retire soon but also says he''ll keep working as long as his mom is alive. She''s in her 90''s. He sees her every week when he has to go to work. She''s 4 1/2 hrs away but where he comes and goes for flying. They live in Northern WI. Donna does a little footcare for clients and it''s only about $300 a week. She doesn''t do the typical annual wellness visits. She''s careful about their diet. However, her husband does smoke a pipe a few times a week. So, he will need to stay with reg ins. He also has high blood pressure well managed with meds that he might not even need since it''s only borderline in needing anything. No other pre-x for either of them. She was totally understanding of the limitations for tobacco users. She found me from one of my podcasts that I did and it was a female host. So, I''m sure it was the Naturally Inspired podcast. She said she found it on Brigteon. Very cool! She was super intrigued and thrilled to learn of this solution so, her husband can retire peacefully when he''s ready. Their current ins is 80/20 and sounds like  a decent plan since it''s such a large employer group.  She''s not sure when they would want her to join. She''s going to discuss it all with her husband.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-13 12:14:49', '2024-02-13 12:16:06'),
