  ('zcrm_1579374000133108026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000133117001', 'Melinda Rochon', NULL, '2-8-24 Armour Thyroid is $226 via World MedRX. GoodRX is $185 for 90 day supply and 120 mg. So, GoodRX is better. But, will still want Concierge to price it out.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-08 15:05:24', '2024-02-08 15:05:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133108016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000133117001', 'Melinda Rochon', NULL, '2-8-24 Melinda is 48 and works for Steve Hakes. She was on Medicaid due to covid since she was laid off. She is working now as W2 only. So, she doesn''t qualify for SECURE and she just did All of her wellness visits including mammo, colonscopy, pap screening, eye check and dental cleaning.  So, she''s good for about a year. She has Hashimotos and hypothyroid. She takes Armour Thyroid which is expensive about $64 a month and Naltrexone 12 mg 1x daily. She cuts a 50 mg pill in 1/4 so they last a long time. No tobacco. She does  blood work a few times a year. CARE+ $1000/$265 is her best choice.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-08 12:47:21', '2024-02-08 12:47:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132923031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000132894049', 'Rick Hilliard', NULL, '2-6-24 Rick is 63 and wife is 62. He''s an ASHI member and is self-employed inspector. They are mostly healthy. He had a knee replacement about 2 years ago. He also had a thyroid gland removed on Jan. 10th, 2024. Everything checked out fine and benign. No problems! They removed it purely bc his calcium levels were high. Neither smoke or use tobacco. They both have high blood pressure meds and he also takes statin for high cholesterol. They are both well managed with meds and no hospital visits for these. Rick sees his Dr. every 3 months to check on his meds. They do not have an HSA. His wife''s company is being bought out in Feb. or not until July. So, they are prepping to make sure they have options if/when that happens.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-06 14:21:41', '2024-02-06 14:21:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132788006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000132304969', 'Alicia Ojeda', NULL, '2-2-24 Alicia is possibly interested in SECURE HSA at $405/$1000. Menla will pay for her up to $335 and she''ll pay the rest. She''s also interested in the better wellness benefits since everything she wants isn''t included in ACA compliant wellness. She wants heart check, better labs for all things, dexascan for osteoporsis, themogram, etc.  She also likes to you yoga, chiro, acupuncture, eats organic foods, takes supplements, etc. She''s extra proactive now since her dad just passed away and her mom is going through cancer treatments (I think that''s what she said.) She also wants dental and vision. Wellness benefit might solve all that she wants.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-02 15:44:33', '2024-02-02 15:50:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132623003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000132304969', 'Alicia Ojeda', NULL, '1-25-24 Alicia is 59 and had MVP ins with Manla (?) for 4-5 years in CA and NY. She uses Direct Labs sometimes and see the dramatic cost savings in doing so. She came to me via Lynn Schauwecker. She broke her arm 1 years ago and had a lypoma fatty cyst for 10 years. It was removed last year. She prefers preventative care with chiro and acu, instead of traditional. She was paying $300 every month and Manla was paying $300 every month. She self diagnosed Hashimotos many years ago and resolved it on her own with complete diet and lifestyle changes. She treated it naturally.  She''s a plant-based chef for 25 years now and has really taken control of her health in that journey.  She has done a thermogram in the past.  She also wants to review her NY Life ins policy which is for $100K and possibly wants dental/vision discount plan for $99 +$20. She rescheduled from Jan. 31st to Feb. 1st to enroll in CARE+. $350/$1000.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-31 14:24:22', '2024-02-02 15:41:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131978023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131987001', 'Ray Robinson', NULL, '1-18-24 Ray is 56, 9/13/67 and lives in Erie 80516. He used to live up the hill from me off S. Boulder Rd. He was referred by Jennifer Shedd. In March of 2023 he was laid off but his company allowed him to keep his employer plan, but not through Cobra. He''s just paying on his own $775 for an incredibly great platinum level plan. The company is based in AL. He finally got a new 1099 contract job for a company in eastern Europe. Income expected to be about $125K and he doesn''t qualify for a subsidy via C4. I shared the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $0 plan for $725.36 as one option. He also pays $119 for DPC Dr. Charles Tawa. Therefore, he qualifies for the DIRECT membership at $370 a month with MPB. That can save him about $2700 a year compared to the Cigna plan. His only concern that''s not really a concern to him is that in doing extra, non-necessary screenings they uncovered a dilated aorta. It could be normal for him. But, now they have a baseline to  review and compare it to. The Dr. isn''t concerned for him. But, since his grandfather died of an aneurysm, the Dr. suggested he does an echocardiogram 1x per year as a precautionary screening.  He knows this would have to be at his cost with either plan. I also suggested he speaks with his drs. about any risks or clean bill of health on his records. He also does 2x year skin checks and knows those aren''t ACA compliant annual screenings. Finally he does 4x dental cleanings per year since his gums are receding a bit. He has some hard decisions. He''s not sure if there''s any problem with him staying on his previous employer''s plan now that he has a new job. I suggested that he talks with their HR person and he said it''s the CEO or Founder he''ll talk with to double check. I likes having the super platinum plan for peace of mind since he''s had employer benefits since he was 40.  He knows of the deadlines. He has another screening in 3 weeks and that will let him know if there''s anything to be concerned about moving forward. He knows of the 60 days allowed since loss of coverage and of the 19th this month and 20th next month for the DIRECT membership. He also is interested in the dental discount plan and less interested in the HMA for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-18 15:40:38', '2024-01-18 15:40:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131699043', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131707093', 'Isaiah Taylor', NULL, '1-15-24 Tim Taylor and wife are looking at this for their son who''s 27 and wife is 26. They are with Solidarity right now at $208 for son with $6K AUA and then 80%/20%. His son is a W2 employee of his home inspector biz. So, I explained CARE+ since they are so young and don''t really need to pay so much for wellness to be included. CARE+ ES $425/$1000. Zip code is 61356 in IL. Taylor is an ASHI member, so make sure to enroll via the ASHI site and make sure $100 is waived. He''s also interested in the dental discount plan at $149 yr plus $20 enrollment fee which also includes vision.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-15 15:39:07', '2024-01-15 15:39:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131699028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131407021', 'Brett Hall', NULL, '1-15-24 Brett and I finally connected after crazy phone tag. He was referred by Colleen and I need to determine which Colleen. He''s 58, healthy mostly. He has diverticulitis which he mostly manages by himself. However he had a perforation in his colon last year. So, I explained the pre-x clause and made sure he understood it. He also watched the 9-minute video and did a bunch of reading and research before we talked. Colleen had sent him a bunch of info to read first. He''s self-employed and does his annual wellness screenings. He considering SECURE HSA or CARE+. He''s leaving for Mexico tomorrow and may not look at this until his return after the deadline. He''s fine to join later for March.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-15 14:51:56', '2024-01-15 14:51:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131397038', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131407031', 'Haley White', NULL, '1-9-24 Haley is 29 and pregnant. She''s due June 2nd, so looking at a July 1st start date. She has a 6 yr old as well. Looking potentially at SECURE HSA $1000/$530, $125/$25. She''s healthy. W2 pay now but might have self-employment by July. I shared CARE+ with her as well, in case she doesn''t self-employment. Lives in Brighton, CO. We have an appt set in June to revisit everything for possible July 1st start for EC.  She currently has ins through work at $800-$900.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-09 17:03:16', '2024-01-09 17:10:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131097031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130802007', 'Elijah Sensibar', NULL, '1-3-24 We are playing serious phone tag. But, I just reached him. He works for Doug Weller and is a W2 employee. So, he only qualifies for CARE+ which is better for his price point anyhow. He lives in CO and has a residential address in AZ. He does wellness sometimes but is ok to pay on his own for this part. He''s healthy, no tobacco, no meds, no pre-x other than a broken bone this year that is fully healed. He currently pays about $200 a month with a $5K ded and not sure of the mop. He''s considering $2500/$185 CARE+ EO. He is all set until March right now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-03 16:07:50', '2024-01-03 16:07:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131097003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130664073', 'David Buck', NULL, '1-3-23 David and Megan called to discuss the memberships. Megan is VERY skeptical and doesn''t want to pay for anything at this point after her terrible experience with their current insurance from HA called UHA. She had a skiing accident and got an ACL surgery done at Steadman''s Clinic. Now she''s owing about $20K in hospital bills since UHA won''t pay for most of it since she was out of network. She got pre-approval from them and now they are pushing back. She realizes the true cost was about $20K if she had just paid cash up front. They pay $1700 a month and have a super low ded and mop, but it didn''t matter since it was out of network in CO. David is still interested to do SECURE HSA to avoid this same problem in the future for the EF or EC. They have two kids as well. Megan is beside herself with how corrupt the ins world is and is having a hard time believing MCS is different after her terrible experience.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-03 10:35:05', '2024-01-03 10:35:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131035054', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131036104', 'Savanah Shea', NULL, '1-2-24 Savanah came to me via Savannah Lewis. She changed jobs in May 2023. She''s 28, no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds, healthy. She expects to make $55K-$60K this coming year. She doesn''t qualify for an APTC and lowest cost plan is $227 for a terrible plan. So, I quoted her CARE+ which she says is likely too expensive for her right now. I will still send her the info on C4 and CARE+.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-02 15:23:51', '2024-01-02 15:25:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130903033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130953001', 'Michaela Reynolds', NULL, '12-29-23 Michaela (sp?) just finished listening to the Naturally Inspired Podcast and called me right away. She''s super intrigued by what we offer. She prefers to remain outside of gov programs ie. ACA. She hasn''t had insurance in many years. She''s currently looking for a job as a caregiver in geriatric care as home care provider. She''s self-employed and licensed in CO. Lives in Lafayette, CO. She''s super healthy and is very interested in sharing this with a number of other people who she believes will appreciate our offerings. She sounds super nice! I sent her to my 9 min video and she will watch it and we will meet again next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-29 11:53:26', '2025-04-02 16:19:23'),
