  ('zcrm_1579374000130665038', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130664073', 'David Buck', NULL, '12-21-23 David is 49 turning 50 Feb. 2nd, 2024. I quoted him in the 50-65 age group. His wife is 45. They have two teenage daughters. They split their time between HA and CO. David is a realtor on Honolulu, but his wife and the girls all spend most of their time in CO now with school and such. They live in Aspen and ski, play basketball, etc. His wife blew out her knee skiing and just had surgery in May. They are still fighting to get it paid and next step is to go to arbitration. The ins is fighting it since they did the surgery out of network. They are trying to pay only $900 of the $20,000 surgery. She wasn''t mobile enough to fly back to HA for the surgery where it would have likely been even more expensive and worse care. They are paying $1600 a month and he thinks it will go up to $1700 in Jan. for crap benefits since everything will be out of network. David watched some of the video, so I explained the entire thing again. I told him to share it with his wife as well. They are so fed up with the trad ins world and see how corrupt it is! He understands the pre-x clause in relation to her ACL and his daughter sprained her ankle and is healing that now. She plays volleyball for school. They are all healthy otherwise, no tobacco. David takes phenosteride for hair loss which is about $12 a month and a cream for seriosis. His younger daughter takes an acne medication. He found me via James Benvenuto since their daughters go to school together and plan basketball together. He was asking about doing a colonoscopy soon, his wife did her mammo recently, and kids may need physicals for school. He''s never funded an HSA but is interested. I explained SECURE HSA $1000/$1005, $125/$25. Feb. 1st will work. We have another appt set for Jan. 3rd.  He also wants to see the dental discount plan.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor'