  ('zcrm_1579374000130665003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130664001', 'Juliane Rohs', NULL, '12-21-23 Juliane is 53, self-employed, psycho therapist, single mom. Her son is 21 and has a daughter too. I don''t know her age. She was referred to me by Christine Harvey. She hasn''t had ins since May since it''s so expensive. She was quoted $700+ for just her which is ridiculous. So, she''s learned how to navigate as a self-pay patient. She used to work at BCH and saw the billing system with ins and how much of a scam it is. She just learned that if she goes to Urgent Care as an "Established Patient" the price is $130 vs $250! She doesn''t necessarily want wellness and is possibly interested in funding the HSA. She does take a migraine med on occasion called sumatripten and pays $80 for it which lasts a very long time. She''s hoping maybe she can get it prescribed via the virtual healthcare app. I suggested she tries there first bc then it would be at no cost to her. If not, she might still have to go in person to get the prescription.  She''s most interested in SECURE HSA, but possibly CARE+ if she doesn''t fund the HSA. She''s also un-v. She has a cool foot bath that she learned about that naturopathic Drs. use to pull out metals. It helped a person that had too much lead in their body from time in China and the work he was doing. It can help with a ton of ailments. She''ll let me know when she finds out what it is called. I also gave her Dr. Pierre Kory''s name and site name for her son to help pull out v and Dr. Peter McCullough (she knew of him).', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-21 10:42:53', '2023-12-21 10:42:53'),
