  ('zcrm_1579374000130292003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130286011', 'Kiki Wiesen', NULL, '12-14-23 Kiki came to me via her mom Lisa Wiesen. Kiki is 26 and her company offers $200 towards ins that they offer but not on any plan. Kiki is borderline not working enough hours to gain this $200 benefit. If not, then she has to pay the full price of whatever she chooses. So, she''d rather get a C4 plan and she will want to keep her hours under the threshold to maintain her APTC which shows about $70 with $49K income for 2024. She can''t login to her account. She will get that squared away and we will review next week. Her plan auto renewed already and her cost is showing $183.44 but with her income set at $45K she thinks. So, we may want to adjust it moderately so she doesn''t owe more taxes at end of the year. She''ll let me know her availability for next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-15 11:52:58', '2023-12-15 11:52:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130219052', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000061379001', 'Tilio Lagatta', NULL, '12-14-23 Zion gave me access to the public data regarding the non-profit and assets available which I believe were about $13M. I saved the link on a doc and shared it with Tilio. He wanted more data but Zion wasn''t willing to give the additional details. They provided the public data.  Tilio decided to move forward. I re-explained how  a Need/Incident works again. He understands now. He also decided to add his daughter since she''s still a tax dependent and lives with him mostly. She''s 20. He was going to have her join separately but it only saves $10 a month and insteads means they have 3 separate Needs per year rather than 3 per household. So, it''s best to keep them together as EC. He enrolled in SECURE HSA $1000/$710.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-14 16:33:02', '2023-12-14 16:33:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130066023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130064021', 'Mignon Lagatta', NULL, '12-12-23 Mignon is 55 and x-wife of Tilio Lagatta (who is still looking into joining as well). Mignon sounds like filet mignon. She''s self-employed with and EIN. Lives in Reno, NV. Has blood pressure meds, no tobacco, yes for wellness visits and open to having an HSA. She also takes hormone replacement therapy progesterone which she''s taken for many years. Ok with self-pay. She''s ending a domestic partnership of 10 years now and just has to talk with him about her next steps before she joins. She''ll do so in the next week and she knows the deadlines. She ok if it''s not until Feb. 1st but ideally Jan. 1st if she can decide in time. But, she has crappy trad ins at the moment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-12 14:47:49', '2023-12-12 14:47:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130066003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000130064001', 'David Kindrachuk', NULL, '12-12-23 Found me on C4 bc they live in Louisville. David is 44 and his wife is 46 and they have two kids who are 11 (turning 12 in Jan.) and 15 turning 16 in June 2024. He earns about $300K or more from investments, businesses, real estate, commercial properties, etc. He has a business that he sold off the assets to but it''s still his business with an EIN that can also serve as eslf-employment. Plus he has an S-Corp.  He also is a partner in multiple businesses. He started the call by saying he wants a PPO. I let him know those aren''t available as individuals on or off C4. He''s on Cobra now for $1400 and doesn''t know when their renewal is. He joined in July 2023. It has  an $8500 ded and $16K mop with UHC. He''s had a questionable gall bladder for years and may want to do one more test to rule out any problems. It''s not changing and tolerable.  His wife has a meniscus knee problem that was repaired already and she did 3 injections of something more than just cortisone and it still has pain. So, they want to get that resolved. He''s thinking to get these issues handled while they have access to Cobra and then switch to SECURE HSA when Cobra runs out or they have no more concerns of pre-x. They also like to fund an HSA. David was given a Preferred status for life ins recently as well.  They are more traditional in their approach to medicine.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-12 11:53:36', '2023-12-12 11:53:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129968003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129727067', 'David Herkert', NULL, '12-11-23 David is making his final decision. The lowest cost plan through his employer benefits is about $400 as well but the plan has a $8K MOP and $7K Ded. He understands SECURE HSA doesn''t have co-pays for the small stuff but he''s better protected for the larger issues. He''s also talked with Holly Wiese and some others who have this membership and they are happy. He''ll let me know if he wants to move forward and he knows the deadlines.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-11 10:08:45', '2023-12-11 10:08:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129838074', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129840035', 'Wayne Harrick', NULL, '12-7-23 Wayne is 39 and lives in Santa Fe, NM but will also be working in CO a bunch this year. He does 1099 work. He mtn bike rides and just wants to protect himself in case of an accident and to keep up with aging. He doesn''t have any pre-x, no tobacco, just takes anxiety meds. Yes, he''d like to do his wellness visits and fund an HSA. He might want to start for Jan. 1st but isn''t certain. He''s looking at SECURE HSA $1000/$325 or $2500/$265.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-08 18:05:48', '2023-12-08 18:05:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129838053', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000061379001', 'Tilio Lagatta', NULL, '12-8-23 Tilio is 53 tomorrow, therefore DOB is 12.9.1970. He''s self-employed, healthy, he hasn''t done the traditional wellness and isn''t sure if he''s interested. He''d rather dig deeper and get better labs and such it sounds like. Yes, he''s open to funding an HSA. He did have 2 hip replacements 3 years ago. I explained the pre-x and made sure he understands if he has any symptoms still of anything in the past 24 months then it''s pre-x. I recommended he checks his record to make sure there''s nothing that could deem it pre-x. He understood. He''s paying $700 now for just him. He could join SECURE HSA for $405/$1000 and even add his 21 yr old at $710/$1000 for both of them. He really wants to see the financials. I''m not sure what I can get.  He wants to understand how it''s audited or who overseeing the funds? I''m asking Zion.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-08 17:48:45', '2023-12-08 17:48:45'),
