  ('zcrm_1579374000129733043', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129727067', 'David Herkert', NULL, '12-6-23 David is 59 and lives in Boulder County. He came to me via Holly Weise. He''s employed by someone who offers ins but he will still pay $600 (after his company contribution) a month for a plan with a high ded and mop. He moved here from WI where he was getting incredible ins with something called Badger Care. He flew back to WI last year for his visits bc it made more sense than to pay the crazy rates here. For items that didn''t make sense to do in WI, he paid cash for some labs here. When he did, it cost him $8! He then started seeing the insanity in ins. He''s already dabbled in self-pay.  He''s healthy. He did have a benign tumor removed out of his leg or called a nerve sheath in Dec. 2022. He doesn''t really do the wellness visits but he is interested in the HSA. He''s interested in SECURE HSA $405/$1000 for Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-06 14:20:03', '2023-12-06 14:20:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129733038', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129552001', 'Brooke Fowler', NULL, '12-1-23 Brooke is looking for something immediately which we don''t have in CO anymore since we don''t have short-term benefits. She''s in a tough spot. I''ll try to reach her again though.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-06 14:05:05', '2023-12-06 14:05:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129605003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129297033', 'Joe Jarriel', NULL, '12-4-23 Joe is quite combative and feeling like I was "pushing" the non-insurance solution which he''s very uninterested in. He thinks it sounds like a ponzi scheme. I sent him reg ins plan options as well in our initial communications. He doesn''t understand how I can help him vs him calling every ins company to do his own comparison. He thinks I''m being too vague in my questioning. So, I shared all of the questions that I''d ask him if he wants to work with me. I almost just let him go since I don''t need to work with someone who doesn''t value my knowledge or expertise. Once I shared with more all of the questions that are important in making an educated decision, he said he''ll think it over and talk with his wife. If he wants to move forward with me, he''ll call me back. Not holding my breathe. It''s probably best he does his own research, so he can''t place blame on me or anyone else down the road.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-04 09:55:41', '2023-12-04 10:18:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129511160', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129549093', 'Ann Weatherby', NULL, '12-1-23 Ann is 35 and engaged to her partner who''s 40. He''s with Kaiser and quite content but paying $400. She may show him that it works before he decides he wants to switch. For Ann, her C4 account is going up to $500 a month! She''s self-employed. She does her annual wellness and she likes to fund an HSA. She called someone at Zion to ask about maternity. They told her they are removing the 60 day waiting period. She has some modest shoulder and hip issues that she resolving with PT now and no surgery is on the forefront. She understands this is pre-x and she will have to pay for the PT. She''s currently going within the hospital and it costs $175 per hour!  She''s open to looking for  a private practice to pay a more affordable rate. She''s considering pregnancy soon. She engaged but they have no date set. They might elope or just go to the court. She wants the maternity guide that I''ll send. She has some generic meds, no tobacco. Her should MRI cost $800 with her insurance. I let her know the cash price is often even cheaper than that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-01 17:56:03', '2023-12-01 17:56:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129511140', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129549083', 'McKenzie Winebarger', NULL, '12-1-23 McKenzie is 42 and husband Brent is 46. She''s self-employed in bike sales. They are using US Health/Freedom Life right now for $830. Then she got onto Bright Health for herself for a hip surgery a few years ago. Her hip is good now. Her non-comparable plan on C4 for just her is going up to $400 this year for a Catastrophic Plan.  She''s also leery of C4 bc they had to pay back their APTC a few years ago. She did a home birth with her kids. She gets mammo and pap screening but Brent doesn''t do any of them. She prefers holistic, naturopathic solutions. She loves their virtual healthcare through Freedom Life right now. That''s what they use the most. They don''t have any other pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. Kids are 10 and 7. Live in Durango, CO Most interested in SECURE HSA to gain some wellness and HSA. Possibly CARE+ but seems to be leaning towards SECURE.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-01 17:43:41', '2023-12-01 17:43:41'),
