  ('zcrm_1579374000129469077', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129471073', 'Laura Kilty', NULL, '11-30-23 Laura is 60 and her husband is 61. Live in Arvada and they were referred by Dr. Carrie Ballas. Laura goes to Carrie for her wellness visits but Dr. Ballas doesn''t bill to ins. So, she will have to go somewhere else or pay cash and not get reimbursed for that part. Laura''s husband is looking to quit his job by the end of Dec. 2023. Laura just got a new job at Target and they may give her benefits. She''s not sure yet. Also, she does have a Shaklee Distribution business on the side with a 1099. So, they can qualify for SECURE HSA. Laura is healthy but takes thyroid meds and compounded meds for menopause. Those are $70 a month. She also went to an ENT who sent her to a TMJ Specialist which then determined she has sleep apnea. I read the Sleep Apnea section from the Sharing Guidelines to her. Her husband just had foot surgery 2 weeks ago to take out a bundle of nerves that were tangled. It''s basically a neuroma and it was minor. She understands the pre-x clause relative to all of the items she shared with me. Neither of them use tobacco. They do their annual wellness visits and would like to fund an HSA.  She was nervous about the major health event such as when their son was in and out of the hospital for 5 months once and the bills were insane. I suggested life ins with Living Benefits to protect for major health events  like that. She believes her has that with Thrivent. But, I recommended she looks closer at what''s really included.  She''s looking at SECURE HSA and Medishare as well as Christian Healthshare Ministry. She will let me know what they decide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-30 15:44:44', '2023-11-30 15:44:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129349173', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000127739001', 'Melissa Thornton', NULL, '11-28-23 Melissa is 44, divorced with 4 kids, 24, 22, 18 and 14. But, she only needs to cover the 14 year old. The eldest 2 are on their own ins and her x is covering the 18 yr old. She''s a realtor with her own S-Corp and going to determine the MAGI with her CPA called Zachster (?). Income is $80K-$90K but she thinks after expenses perhaps $20K-$40K.  She says she''s super loyal and has been with only 2 ins companies in her life time except what she had as a kid with her parents. But, she recently chose Freedom Health and has managed to spend $130K-$150K on everything the don''t cover!!!  She almost needed to file for bankruptcy but refused to do so. Instead she sold her house in Superior and moved to Longmont, which she doesn''t love. She''s a full time single working mom with no help from her x. She''s been paying most of her health expenses out of pocket. Neither of them have any pre-x from the past two years, no meds, no tobacco. She hasn''t been doing her annual wellness since covid but she does have an HSA that she finally opened. I''m having her watch the video and also get more exact numbers to give her a comparison with C4 options. She wants mental health benefits, no more than $5K ded and monthly around $500 with $600 max. She likes Anthem and prefers the big names and my opinion.  She grew up in VT in Morrisville, Stowe, Williston, etc. and went to UVM!  She most recently lived on 100 acres at the base of Mt Mansfield and loved the small town feel.  She found me via a photographer who told her to contact me. I need to find out who that is!  Also she''s been spending $500 a month mental health therapy for her 14 year old. So, that''s important to her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-28 15:48:55', '2023-11-28 15:48:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129289117', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000097262001', 'Alex Lovejoy', NULL, '11-27-23 Alex is now asking about insulin for her son. He needs Lantus and Novolog, plus Freestyle Libre 3 sensors and 2 a month.  She also thinks she enrolled in the Vision Plan B for herself. I have no record of that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-27 21:05:36', '2023-11-27 21:05:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129289077', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000127739001', 'Melissa Thornton', NULL, '11-27-23 I reached Melissa and she was driving. She asked me to send her a few times tomorrow afternoon to connect. We will do so.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-27 16:25:32', '2023-11-27 16:25:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129289039', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129297033', 'Joe Jarriel', NULL, '11-27-23 Joe is 55, 3/26/69 and Trudy soon to be 59, 12/2/64.  Joe is unemployed and his Cobra is ending by Jan. 1st 2024. They''ve had employer group coverage always. Trudy is retired for 10 years now. But, they do have some self-employment income to show such as rental income. They want to keep their drs. at BCH in Lafayette. Dr. Kara Choi and Dr. Mikyong Hand and both show up in the PHCS network. Trudy takes Estradiol. Yes, they want their ACA wellness visits. Joe hasn''t done them but is now starting to. They also looked at the C4 plans. They don''t have a C4 account yet. But, Cigna and Anthem are the only plans that cover both Drs. Cigna''s are more affordable, so I''m sending those samples to them to review. They don''t have pre-x, no tobacco and no meds except Estradiol. At $180K they can gain a $273 APTC to bring the cost to $1100-$1200. Full cost is $1400+, similar to what they are paying with Cobra.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-27 14:51:51', '2023-11-27 15:00:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128760062', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000128774061', 'Alana Beard', NULL, '11-15-23 From Alana, "Hi, thank you so much for reaching out… let’s hold off for right now but I will definitely be in touch later in 2024. My husband and I are both self employed and the last few years we have made enough annually so that we didn’t qualify for any assistance thru Obama (coverMe.gov) care- needless to say it was very expensive. But I just redid the numbers on our renewal application based on this past year’s income, because it was an in-between year for my husband’s building jobs, and it brought the monthly payment down significantly for this coming year. But in 2025 we expect a big income jump again when he finishes his current project so we will have some time to research the coop and reach out to you before then if not sooner. Diane seems to have have had a great experience. 

Alana"

