  ('zcrm_1579374000126058011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000123308001', 'Marguerite Richard', NULL, '10-5-23 Marguerite called to get a plan for Jan. 1st, 2024. I told her again we can''t start until Nov. 1st.  However, Dennis, her husband can start with Medicare now bc his DOB is Dec. 30, 2023 and turning 65. His job end Jan. 2nd and then Marnie can join Cobra if it''s affordable. She has many significant health issues with her heart and such. So, she wants good coverage but I don''t know what they can afford.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-05 16:10:49', '2023-10-05 16:10:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125691038', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000125618001', 'Paula Persons', NULL, '9-28-23 Paula watched the video and had a lot to share about her past experiences with insurance and Christian Healthshare Ministry. He husband is a pilot and can''t risk doing underwriting if they come back with something that will jeopardize his career. She''s familiar with the ACA where pre-x isn''t an issue and no underwriting. However the cost was in the $700''s for the two of them for crappy coverage. She really just wants catastrophic and no underwriting. So, MCS is possible but she had something rejected by Christian Healthshare Ministry considered pre-x that she never even knew existed and there were no records of. So, she''s discouraged by that experience. The items they are concerned about for now are that she had a double hip replacement in mid March of 2022 and husband had a hiatial hernia at end of April 2022. So, she wants to wait until those are past the pre-x clause. The only other concern is his asthma. He hasn''t been hospitalized for it. I was very clear with her that they will need to decide if they''re willing to take the risk of the pre-x clause, especially in the first year. They actually do not have ins at the moment and they''ve been going as self-pay patients. She understands how to advocate her them, ask questions and get the best cash price. They are using GoodRX for meds for her husband''s asthma. Paula is 53 and husband is 60. I explained the HMA to her as well and she wasn''t super thrilled since you have to wait a while to use it per the recommended within 1-3 years. She wants something immediate for all of the money spent. I explained the HMA 10,000 since she just wants to put money into a CD or money market acct for health events.  She became slightly more open minded to this as we talked.  They also don''t want to tie up their money in products where they can''t access their money. This is one hurdle of the HMA for them. 

She also brought up that her sister in law or niece in Ft Morgan had a pregnancy that is getting rejected by insurance since the hospital was  bought out 3 times since the start of the pregnancy. They had one set of bills for labs for $13K which was sent to CA at the beginning of the pregnancy. That''s only one of many bills trickling in. That bill is outside of the 270 days. But, the birth was 6 months ago, so they may qualify for the Hospital Debt Eraser. She''s guessing their household income is about $80K since the mom doesn''t work and husband works for Excel Energy. They are  a family of 5, so I believe they are likely to qualify for the program. I am waiting for Ali to send along anything to share with the potential client.  
Also, Paula was sent to me via Ben DiSalle, their Financial Advisor. He wants an update as we progress.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-09-28 13:22:08', '2023-09-28 13:26:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125617008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000125618001', 'Paula Persons', NULL, '9-26-23 Paula came to me via Ben DiSalle her Financial Advisor. Their family doesn''t currently have any  health ins. Her husband is a pilot and can''t have any underwriting that might put his career at risk. He had a hernia repair within the last 1-2 years and she is 1 1/2 yrs out from a hip replacement in April 2022 (I think).  She''s curious about adding their 23 yr old on as well. We have an appt set for this Thurs. and I just sent her the video to watch.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-09-26 17:01:33', '2023-09-26 17:01:33'),
