  ('zcrm_1579374000124014057', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000124012054', 'Debbie Steinbock', NULL, '8-23-23 Both Debbie and Roy have hypothyroidism which they take meds for and they do labs every 6-9 months. Mia is their daughter turning 13 soon. They asked about the cost of labs and I looked them up on JasonHealth.com and gave them an idea of the cost and no need for a separate dr. prescription. They were interested in thyroid tests, vitamin D, iron and possibly hormone tests. Roy is a pediatrician, so he typically writes the prescriptions for them but it''s a moot point for this purpose. They are currently paying $1200+ a month with a $7500 Ded and $14K MOP. They do their annual wellness visits. They are currently on a group plan and it ends Nov. 1st. So, they''re looking to potentially move to this for Nov. 1st start date.  They use mostly alternative healthcare providers. They will keep me posted as we approach Nov. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-23 17:18:06', '2023-08-23 17:18:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124014052', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000124012054', 'Debbie Steinbock', NULL, '8-23-23 Debbie is 46 and Roy is 51 and they have a 12 year old turning 13 in Sept.  Their background - 

