  ('zcrm_1579374000122060097', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000122049100', 'Jewell Aline', NULL, '7-17-23 Jewell is helping her family look at options. One daughter Eileen Fagan is already a member under Tupac. Jewell looking to help her other daughter Carolyn 5/20/64 and son in law, John who is born 4/19/62.  They are currently on Medishare and have a $10K deductible and paying $700+.  I sent her the video to sent to Carolyn and John to review. It has my contact information for them to reach me as well. They all live in OR.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 18:22:58', '2023-07-17 18:23:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060092', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000122049090', 'Frasier Block', NULL, '7-17-23 Frasier is 40 and super healthy, no pre-x, yes she does her annual wellness visit as well as hormone blood test etc. She''s self-employed and lives in Charleston SC. She''s not super familiar with HSA''s. I explained it. She''s pondering the higher IUA for lower monthly cost. Curious about SECURE and CARE+. I forgot to get her email address and I promised to send her the overview emails and video! I just sent her a text to ask her for it. She''s in no rush bc she''s traveling soon and can''t focus on completing this now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 18:16:29', '2023-07-17 18:16:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000122060074', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000122049080', 'Mark Wagoner', NULL, '7-17-23 Mark and wife are currently with Christian Healthshare Ministry and paying $520 for $1000 AUA per member. They are both 62 or he will be in Aug. actually. Yes, they do their annual wellness and blood work but they pay for it on their own right now. He got a colonoscopy 6 years ago and shouldn''t need another one until he on Medicare. They don''t have pre-x, no tobacco and no meds. His wife did have kidney stone this past year and got it resolved. He assumed that wouldn''t be pre-x. I explained it''s up to the dr. and how they determine if a new one comes whether or not it''s considered pre-x. Not up to us. He talked for a long time since he''s frustrated with our broker healthcare system. He wants to retire but he was hoping for cheaper rates since they rarely use the membership. However the $30-$40K kidney stone scenario was lowered to $16K-$17K with cash pay and then he had to spend a ton of time getting all of the bills with the CPT codes to submit. He doesn''t want to have to fight to get all of the docs and then still wait 90 days for reimbursement. This is his major frustration with Christian Healthshare. If ours was even a few dollars cheaper, he''d try it but it''s $5 more expensive. So, he''s going to ponder with his wife and let me know. He''ll probably stay put. I will send email and video to share with her.  He''s looking at all of the healthshare options including One Share and may avoid LHS. I told him One Share had concerns for me in the Guidelines.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-17 18:02:24', '2023-07-17 18:04:19'),
