  ('zcrm_1579374000121971086', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121972082', 'Dylan Darnulc', NULL, '7-14-23 Dylan is 25 turning 26 in Nov. He''s working on leaving his current employment and going to do contract work for next year or more. He has a 1099 already that he can show. He lives in TN. He watched the video and understands it. His only health issue is that he takes meds for sweating. Takes Drisdol and that''s super cheap ($2-$12) as well as Oxybutynin that''s super cheap ($2-$14), both show for less than what he''s paying now at $9 and $15.  He wants dental and vision as well. He might like to join SECURE for the HSA tax benefits. He''s talking with his accountant next week to run it by him/her. So, he''s deciding between SECURE or CARE+ at the $1000 level. He is also non tobacco.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-14 14:29:34', '2023-07-14 14:30:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121902013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121904004', 'Lisyuri Gallardo', NULL, '7-13-23 Lisyuri is 31 and works as a counselor at an elementary school. She''s from Colombia!  She''s leaving on Monday, June 17th and gone until Aug. 10th. She wants a Sept. 1st start date. We''re meeting on the 16th at 4:00 to enroll in CARE+. She''s super healthy, no meds, no tobacco. She does all of her wellness visits back home in Colombia when she goes. Her school is paying $200 now for her health ins plan which she never uses. If she opts out, her school with give her a $400 stipend. So, she can pay for CARE+ from that money and be ahead of the game since CARE+ is not insurance! She watched the video and understood it well. She just wanted to know what the difference is between health sharing organizations. I let her know the biggest difference is the Guidelines for each membership. She''s psyched to move forward and came to me via Jennika Wildau.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-13 12:25:44', '2023-07-13 12:25:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121881003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121880023', 'Nicholas Song Candea', NULL, '7-13-23 Iris Kelly is looking for an option for her 29 year old son. He''s living in ID and is a big kayaker at the moment. So, he''s super healthy, no meds, no tobacco, no wellness visits. He''s doing seasonal work now. This is a perfect solution for him with his young, active lifestyle. Iris will pay for it and is psyched about CARE+ probably at $1000/$215. She will discuss it with Nicholas and have him watch the video. We have an enrollment meeting on Tuesday. She''s been looking/thinking about MCS for 30 years. She knows of folks happy with LHS.  I will send video and written overview for them to review.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-13 10:30:47', '2023-07-13 10:30:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121789066', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121788049', 'Kate Yu Cheng', NULL, '7-12-23 Lynn Schauwecker sent Kate to me. Kate is looking at this for her 35 year old son. They are living at a Buddhist Retreat Center for now and likely the rest of the year. Her son isn''t earning much and can probably qualify for Medicaid. They live in WA state. But, he may not stay there long term. I suggested Essentials to help for the basic items for Virtual Healthcare, Life Care and Concierge Team, especially if he doesn''t qualify for Medicaid. He files his taxes in WA for now. Used to live in CA. She will see if he qualifies for Medicaid and ponder Essentials. She''ll let me know if they want to enroll in that. Sounds like she might pay for it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-12 15:30:11', '2023-07-12 15:30:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000121789008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121788004', 'Labrew Solomon', NULL, '7-11-23 Julie sent Labrew to me. He''s 29 and currently W2 but working towards own biz. He''s paying $360 through his W2 employment now. He had asthma but hasn''t had any symptoms in 10+ years now. He keeps an inhaler just in case he needs it for an emergency. He doesn''t have an HSA. He hasn''t done his wellness visits for perhaps 18 months or so. I explained CARE+ vs SECURE. CARE+ initially until he has his own self-employment. I gave him rate for CARE+ $1000 and $2500. Then at the end of the call I asked him how he was referred to MPB. I should have asked at the beginning!  He found MPB through an article from HSA America. So, I explained to Labrew that he might need to work with my teammate moving forward. I immediately called Wiley Long to sort it out. I haven''t heard back from Wiley yet. But, this should have been sent to him initially.  I will send follow up email today 7-12-23, so Labrew isn''t waiting any longer.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-07-12 09:50:22', '2023-07-12 09:50:22'),
