  ('zcrm_1579374000121221090', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000121247021', 'Wendy Thomas', NULL, '6-29-23 Wendy watched the video. She''s self-employed and has been uninsured for many years. She was previously married to Schaana Wetzelberger''s brother. They divorced many years ago and he''s now remarried for almost 4 years. Her current husband is 66 on Medicare. She has Friday Health right now with a $9100 ded. She did all of the wellness visits, got the vaccines, mammo, colonoscopy, etc. She did her mammo at age 60 and they prefer she gets routine checks since her mom died at age 60 of breast cancer. She also did a colonoscopy recently and it looked good except there was a polyp too close to something internally. So, they want her to go back in 3-6 months. She''s set for an appt on Sept. 26th to check it again. She''s not on any meds, no tobacco and has been super healthy. She will work to get a letter from her dr. regarding the request for additional mammos purely bc of family history, not bc they''ve found anything of concern. Assuming her colonoscopy goes well, she will request a similar note from Dr. stating they she is clear of any issues. We have a next appt early Oct once she is past this next colonoscopy. He goal is to sign up for a Nov. 1st start date.  Super nice. SECURE is the best option for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-29 15:44:37', '2023-06-29 15:46:48'),
