  ('zcrm_1579374000120540008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000120541001', 'Michael Echery', NULL, '6-8-23 Michael Echery is Brandy Echery''s brother. Mike is 51 and lives in Louisville now. However, he recognized my name from when I lived in Steamboat! Brandy is just about my age. Mike use to race then switched to snowboarding. Mike is working towards leaving his job and becoming self-employed with his own benefits. His income year to date is about $40K and his wife''s is $40K to equal $80K for potential APTC. Therefore, likely more than $80K for 2023.  But, he mentioned he''s made up to $400K in the past. So, to avoid tax penalties he''s happy to avoid ACA. He sees the ridiculous costs associated. When their son was born they needed flight for life and the entire bills for everything was $296K!  He knows the prices are completely inflated.  He has been diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis 12-13 years ago and a kidney disease around the same time. The kidney disease is well managed with 1 dr. visit per year and a med. He likely doesn''t even need that one visit but he complies. For the arthritis he goes 4x per year and gets blood drawn sometimes and take meds to manage it. He hasn''t had any problems and he''s not worried about it. I explained the pre-x clause first and foremost before I explained the full membership. He''s fine paying for those visits and he''s not concerned about any bigger problems stemming for them. He does his annual wellness visits and has an FSA now but is familiar with an HSA as well. He will likely want an Aug. 1st start date.  He will call me when it''s closer and he knows of the 20th of the month deadline.  Looking at SECURE $325/$1000 and $125/$25.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-06-08 16:53:55', '2023-06-08 16:54:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120370053', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000120299005', 'Byron West', NULL, 'I contacted Byron on Friday, June 2,2023 before the lead was entered. He came from a Sales IQ chat. Left him a voicemail message. Tried him back again today, voicemail again. Sent email for him to contact me.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-06-05 14:16:54', '2023-06-05 14:16:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120324001', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000120299005', 'Byron West', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 3092 Question : Who do you use for telemedicine? We have had terrible experiences with Teladoc of recent which is who our current cost sharing plan partners with which is causing me to consider other cost sharing options. I’d be interested in learning more about your program so long as it does not lock us in with Teladoc.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-06-02 12:22:02', '2023-06-02 12:22:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120227028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000120224022', 'Jeremy Green Up Pest Control', NULL, 'Left voicemail message for Jeremy to call me back.', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', 'Jeffrey Bursteen', '2023-06-01 09:24:50', '2023-06-01 09:24:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000120235003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000120224022', 'Jeremy Green Up Pest Control', NULL, 'Met Jeremy at a restaurant. Had previously inquired about MediShare through a Christian radio station. Was unable to get any accurate information when he called the company. Currently has Blue Cross Blue Shield and feels like he is overpaying. Healthy with no Pre-X. Owns his own biz and would be perfect for Secure. Expecting a call from our sales dept.', 'Julia Avalon', 'Julia Avalon', '2023-06-01 08:12:58', '2023-06-01 08:12:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119981003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000119553011', 'Patrick Hester', NULL, '5-25-23 Patrick called back and he''s going to meet with his accountant and one other person to determine income. He thinks they can keep it low enough for this year to benefit from the $300 cost to them. Then he''s thinking of making a change for the new year when his income might be higher moving forward. He''ll let me know if/when that happens.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-25 13:16:51', '2023-05-25 13:16:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000119552044', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000119553011', 'Patrick Hester', NULL, '5-17-23 Hester is an ASHI member!  He already signed up for ins via Healthcare.gov and is paying only $300+ a month for his family. However they are nervous since his wife is  a nurse and she''s offered the option for benefits but she opted about. Otherwise, they deduct her pay by $6.75 an hour to help pay for benefits. So, they are worried they will have to pay back all or part of their APTC. They also have a high ded of $7500 and higher mop with $50 co-pay PCP and $100 specialist. He wished he thought of ASHI before they went down the traditional ins path. Kids are 13 soon, 10 and 6 while Patrick is 38 and wife is 35. They are healthy. However I forgot to mention the Pre-X clause! I''ll call him back..... I called him back and explained it and he''s not concerned. He had a swollen throat back in Nov. 2022 and had a hard time swallowing and some acid reflux. He had an endoscopy (I think). He couldn''t remember the name of it. Then he had surgery to stretch his throat. He now takes a medication to control is. It''s $6 for a 30 day supply. He understands if he has any more problems in the first year of membership that it''s his responsibility to pay for. Nobody uses tobacco and no other meds. No other pre-x. They are getting dental through Healthcare.gov and VSP. I told him to keep those for now and I''ll show him the HMA account. They are paying $140 for dental and about $40 for VSP. After a year they can drop those and maintain the $140 HMA to gain them $10K to use on medical, dental, vision, etc. He''s interested in understanding it better.  They definitely do all of their dental cleanings and such.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-17 15:47:25', '2023-05-17 15:47:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118787016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000118790001', 'Ernie Noh', NULL, '5-3-23 Ernie is 47, Dana 43, kids, 12, 10 and 6. They run a business together and have an EIN. I explained the entire membership to them and they will watch the video as well to really understand it all. Live in CA, so must have SECURE.  Family is healthy, no meds, no tobacco. Paying full price to Anthem $1606. They also have 2 employees they might share this with. They aren''t sure if they''d pay any portion or not. They already have an HSA.  Ernie is newly on the board with WWSRA this year and realized he should look into their own benefits!  He''s also curious how much utilization from WWSRA members and I let him know it''s some but not a ton, we need better communication and marketing to let members know. I need to make sure I give them the $100 discount. Very nice couple and they asked many great questions to wrap their heads around it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-03 12:07:50', '2023-05-03 12:07:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118668003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000118020034', 'Jaffe Rissman', NULL, '5-2-23 Jaffe just wants to make sure the vaccines for children will be properly covered. Her $1400 bill does have a Z code on it and is labeled as wellness. But, she wants to call them to make sure all of the items on that bill are coded as wellness and covered by the ACA. This will help her to be confident that these will be covered in the future moving forward, since they weren''t covered by her current ins. The billing Dept is tough to reach but she''s looking for a June 1st start date, so she has time to get a response. She''ll let me know when she talks with them to better understand the CPT and ICD codes.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-05-02 10:20:35', '2023-05-02 10:21:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118384049', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000118020034', 'Jaffe Rissman', NULL, '4-26-23 I called Jaffe to update her about RBP per our training with Steve Schone. He stated to function legally as a MEC, Planstin has to cover the ACA wellness at no cost with no balance billing. There still remains the issue with preventative vs diagnostic per the dr. records, but they can''t balance bill on the ACA compliant immunizations like what happened to them previously. I even asked that very question in the recorded training call. She wants to talk more tomorrow when she has time since she was leaving to pick up her daughter now. Super interested in SECURE.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-26 16:56:04', '2023-04-26 16:56:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118060026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000118020047', 'Paolo Bonetti', NULL, '4-19-23 Paolo 56, wife, 53 and son 21. He works for Madhava Foods which sells Cocomels. Came to me via Nancy Gentry. He has a terrible Anthem EPO Pathway 28 with a $5K ded and $12K mop. He reached the ded two years in a row bs his son Mario broke his wrist 1 time and had a concussion the next time as separate incidents.  The network is terrible. Son is a skier, etc. Paolo has since learned the power of self-pay in a number of circumstances now and sees how terribly broken our ins system is. He wants to be done with it. His company is actually paying $1225 of his plan and he''s paying $306. He thought they were only paying for him and he was paying for the rest of the family. That''s not the case. They are paying 3/4 of the monthly fee. But, they could pay the full cost of $915/$1000 and save $300 while he also saves $300 a month. He really wants to present this to Madhava Foods to get them on board. He will share the video and any information I send to him now. He wants me to follow up with him in Sept. so I made a note in my calendar to do so. He''s learned to pay wellness on his own bc his plan doesn''t cover anything. His wife is self-employed in case he wants to switch before their annual renewal for company. But, going from $306 to $915 isn''t appealing right now, of course. He learned that self-pay can be 10X cheaper than paying with ins. But, then it doesn''t get applied to his ded. It''s such a racket. His wife has a scheduled surgery for May 9th to have a polyp removed by her uterus. So, they can''t move to MCS at this time.   He wants brochures to present to HR. He''s also interested in the HMA and possibly dental discount plan. I''ll send it all via email now. He''s paying about $122 for dental and vision now for family. So, I explained the HMA 10000 as an option and to use 1Dental in year one while he waits for it to build. He likes all of those ideas.  Other than the above health cirsumstances, the rest of the family is super healthy and no other issues, no tobacco.  Paolo''s company has about 15 employees. He''s not the decision maker. But, he wants to share everything with HR.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-19 15:14:30', '2023-04-19 15:52:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000118060013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000118020034', 'Jaffe Rissman', NULL, '4-19-23 Jaffe is 42 and daughter is 5. Came to me via Rachel Brisson. They live in Glenwood Springs area. She watched the video. She''s looking at One Share and Medishare as well. She said many drs. stopped taking the PHCS network and are now taking it again. Her most recent visit to pediatrician for her daughter was for her wellness visit and a bunch of vaccines, 4 I believe. The bill was $1400 even though they are part of the childhood vax schedule. She has a Cigna PPO plan that basically covered almost none of the cost. They paid $50 per vax but not the $300 administration fee for each. So crooked! She''s a non-smoker. She takes lethartan (sp?) for high blood pressure. It''s well controlled with meds.  She was also looking at the Zion site and prices! I tried to help her understand the prices she was looking at don''t include all of the other benefits. She will call her new doctor''s office to see if 150%-180% of Medicare reimbursement rate will appease them for an ACA compliant annual wellness visit.  If so, she''ll be more comfortable knowing she won''t have to front a huge bill like what just happened.  She wants a May 1st start date but is willing to wait until June if need be.  She is self-employed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-04-19 14:59:36', '2023-04-19 15:00:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000115003001', 'Jill Laughlin', NULL, '3-1-23 Jill is turning 58 this year and husband is turning 55 in Sept. They both work for University of WI. Husband coaches the women''s hockey team and has done so for 20 years! He''s considering a new job or retiring soon. Their current plan costs $2300 a month!!! BUT, the state of WI pays for all of the cost except $250. But, when they retire the funds will be pulled from a holding account to fund the plan until the $ runs out. So, they are trying to explore their options moving forward. They might not want to change until Oct. of 2023, but it''s all up in the air right now. She likes the sounds of SECURE if they can qualify. She gets a 1099R as a pension payment from the University. She has two other PT jobs and those are both W2. Husband is paid as W2 employee as well. They''ve done their colonoscopies the first time around and Jill is 3 years away from needing her next one and husband is 6 years away from needing his. So, they could go with CARE+ is they can''t qualify for SECURE.  They don''t have any pre-x other than she had some skin spots on her face that were biopsied and turned out fine. I told her to check her records to make sure there''s nothing on there that could become a problem. She also is thinking it would be good to join when they haven''t seen a dr. for anything in 24 months. She will share this with her husband and continue determining their next steps towards retirement or another job.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 12:35:57', '2023-03-01 12:35:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114997003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000114761004', 'Bryce Halverson', NULL, '3-1-23 Bryce 39 and wife 35 are both healthy, no pre-x, no meds other than birth control, no tobacco and wellness on occasion. They are financially well and really want to protect against a big incident. They currently have a plan through a friend of a friend that uses an out of state address to get them a more affordable plan. He thinks it might be an AZ address but he can''t remember. He signed up for it 2 years ago and has to make sure he can get out of it as well. The prices in the Aspen Valley area are so high that they got creative to access better pricing. However, when he needed an MRI his ins was rejected. So, he paid $900 cash for the MRI and recognized that was way cheaper than running it through ins. I forgot to ask what the MRI was for and what the results were. He doesn''t want dental or vision since those seem to be a waste of money. He likes SECURE at $1000/$525. He will discuss it with his wife and let me know if they want to move forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-03-01 11:42:56', '2023-03-01 11:46:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114226018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000114228001', 'Debbie Huttner', NULL, '2-20-23 Debbie is 52, kids 16 and 15. She''s divorced and now on Anthem Pathway X plan for $1000+ a month with terrible benefits. She''s self-employed and does wealth management, estate planning, tax planning, etc. She knows Helen Gemmill and Carrie Van Hyst and Peter Johnson. She knows Carrie and Helen through the work she does. She also came to Boulder 19 years ago and taught meditation and yoga. 10 years ago she got back to her educational skills with wealth management. She has many degrees. Works with clients who have $1M - $190M net worth. These are not clients affected by covid to benefit from ERC. However, works with inheritors, more women, lawyers, folks in the tech industry, etc. Her business is PearlWealth.net. She has no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. Son has special needs and goes to Greenwood School in Putney, VT which is sort of associated with the Putney School.  She''s interested in SECURE and HMA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-20 12:57:22', '2023-02-20 12:57:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114226013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000114123038', 'Timothy Moss', NULL, '2-20-23 TJ cancelled his appt today bc they aren''t ready to decide. Not sure what their concern is but they are pondering now...', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-20 12:47:30', '2023-02-20 12:47:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000114125003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000114123038', 'Timothy Moss', NULL, '2-17-23 TJ is born in ''81 and wife in ''88. They are family planning and they know to wait 60 days! They are currently only paying $250 with Covered CA for Sharp Health. They don''t like the current healthcare system. They see all that''s wrong with it. Totally open to being own advocate. They are healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. Self-employed and open to funding an HSA for tax benes and future use. Perfect type of client for MCS. Prefers alternative and preventive care (but not necessarily in traditional sense).', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-17 09:59:04', '2023-02-17 09:59:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113494028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000113482031', 'David Panter', NULL, '1-10-23 David was let go from his job at the beginning of Jan and his benefits ended Jan. 31st. Came to me from Big Wave Lead system. His wife is a stay at home mom and is 40, son is 11. His severance was a one time payout of $75K. He''s looking at a new job that is a big pay cut but would allow him to work from home and not move. Most other jobs will require him to move. If he chooses this job it will pay about $150K, plus his $75K he will not qualify for much or any APTC. They are all healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. The new job won''t offer benefits either. So, I looked at the full cost for a C4 plan that might suffice. The Cigna $0 Ded plan will be $1045.56. He will not qualify for SECURE. No other income now or future intention for self-employment, all W2. So, I quoted him CARE+ at $1000/$580. He won''t do a colonoscopy this year and let him know if wide needs mammo it will still be cheaper than paying for one month of Cigna at $1045.56. He understands wellness will not be reimbursed but savings significant. He watched the video and will share it with his wife. He will also meet with me on Tuesday at 10:00 am.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-10 14:54:58', '2023-02-10 14:54:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000113104108', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000113151030', 'Chelsea Ariew', NULL, '2-6-23 Chelsea is 52 and husband is 36 and step-dad to son Cyrus 17. Came to me via Andre Simoneau. They are both self-employed. Sons birth dad lives with them too! They prefer naturopathic/holistic solutions. They never do their annual wellness visits and didn''t know about HSAs. They are paying $900 now for their ins with a high ded of $5K or more. Their son has testicular torsion which the surgery wasn''t done correctly last year. So, they have to do it again right away. Once complete, they want to switch to CARE+ at $780/$1000 or $630/$2500.  They are all healthy otherwise, no meds. She knows of the deadlines and hopes to be able to switch for March 1st if possible, or April 1st otherwise.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-06 13:15:42', '2023-02-06 13:15:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112922031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000112556008', 'Sean Snyder', NULL, '2-2-23 Sean is 36, wife 31 and daughter will be 2 in April. Sean got laid off and his wife is a stay at home mom. Sean does some music recording on the side as self-employment income. He''s looking for a new W2 job and has his 2nd interview coming up. He might get the job. His benefits last until March 21st and with Cobra after that he''ll pay $1700 a month. We will ask about the benefits as he progresses with the interview. If his cost is $1200 for example, then he likes the SECURE idea and will skip the employee benefits. If the cost is close then he''ll likely choose traditional. But, he gets it and sees the value in SECURE. He takes generic of Prozac 10mg which is about $4 and Adderrall XR 20mg in am about $30 plus Adderrall 5 mg immediate release in afternoon for about $20 on GoodRX. He''s paying about $40-$50 now and it looks like he''d pay about the same with SECURE or better once it''s shopped around.  He wanted to make it clear that they are non-denominational or agnostic and wanted to make sure that''s ok. I let him know that all are welcome. His wife was misdiagnosed with ulcerative colitis and then the diagnosis was removed when she saw another doctor at a later date. They now believe it was simple stressed induced.  Once she quit work and became stay at home mom all symptoms went away.  If he joins, he''s thinking to do so before March 20th for April 1st start date. This way he''ll know more about the potential job situation if that''s going to happen or not. He watched the video and had good questions. SECURE will be $715/$1000 EF 30-49.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-02-02 14:42:57', '2023-02-02 14:42:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000112570003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000112556008', 'Sean Snyder', NULL, '1-30-23 Sean is Judi Snyder''s son. He just got laid off, he''s buying a house and he has a ton on his plate. So, we have rescheduled for Thursday at 2:00 MST for his 1st appt and he will watch the video in advance.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-30 12:16:30', '2023-01-30 12:16:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111868041', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000111864063', 'Anna Thea Davis', NULL, '1-17-23 Thea has some inheritance that she''s been using for her health journey and she doesn''t have much left. She wanted to put some into a retirement account but only has about $30K left last we talked a month or two ago. She''s been going to Roots and Branches with Dr. Dorninger and they are super expensive and treating her for mold that she likely got when in WA. But, she has no income at the moment and will qualify for Medicaid. But, Roots and Branches is telling her they won''t accept her as a patient if she''s on Medicaid. I don''t know how that''s possible. But, she considering going down a different path. I recommended the Sound Clinic and I''ll get Billie''s # from Shelley to possibly help her. She''s dealing with Lyme, menopause, SIRS (Sp?), MCA, etc. Billie might be great. Thea doesn''t really know anyone here yet since she lives remotely on a farm. I let her know she missed the deadline for trad ins but it''s a moot point. She will qualify for Medicaid now and she can get some bills retroactively paid for.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-17 17:17:11', '2023-01-17 19:34:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111397060', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000111365015', 'Carol Prendergast', NULL, '1-10-22 Carol came to me via Suzanne Cote. She had created her C4 account but the plans are more expensive than she can afford. She put her income in at $44K but will try to find more deductions to bring it down so she can afford a plan. We looked at Friday Copay Bronze but her dr. isn''t in the network. Anthem and Ciga ok for Broomfield Family Practice with Dr. Michelle Levine and Dr. Shannon Hill. Friday is not showing up. So, I recommended the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0. She thinks she needs a echo cardiogram and can''t afford the insurance full price. She learned as cash pay her EKG or ultrasound was $40 instead of $250! She currently has flu and laryngitis. She will see if she can change her income and possibly afford a plan that will actually help her, not hinder her ability to pay. She lives in Jefferson County in Westminster. She will call me tomorrow or in the next few days once she decides and I''ll choose the plan for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-10 16:49:24', '2023-01-10 16:49:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000111190067', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000110777030', 'Melinda Cabot', NULL, '1-9-22 They might join with the absolute cheapest plan for a few months. Rylie''s father is court ordered to pay for health ins for Rylie. They think she''s covered by her mother. So, they want the cheapest option. They think they can find something cheaper than what I shared with them. But, I even looked up Anthem''s options off-mkt and nothing is cheaper. So, I doubt they''ll find anything that will appease the court order for cheaper. She also wants to make sure they can cancel it as soon as she''s in school which they can.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-09 15:11:59', '2023-01-09 15:11:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110939033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000110901012', 'Kristy Vollrath', NULL, '1-5-22 Kristy is 42 and lives in OH. Her company ins will cost her $90 a week, therefore $360+ a month. She absolutely can''t afford that. Her dental is $18 a month which she will keep. Sounds like she wants the price to be around $100+ per month. So, this may not work for her but she won''t find anything this affordable with so many benefits. She''s healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. She did land in the ER once after taking an allergy pill that she had a bad reaction to. It increased her blood pressure or heart rate. I forget what she said. But, the bill was $10K and she was not insured. Due to her income level at the time, they lowered the cost to $1K and she was clear. So, she''s seen the corruption in the system. She does want her annual wellness visits and hasn''t been since she doesn''t have ins. She wants a pap screening and possibly mammo. She might like Feb. 1st start date but doesn''t want to rush. I let her know the deadline for both trad ins and for MCS. She wants to take her time and research all options. She tries to be as natural as can be, especially after her experience with pharma drugs. She used to live in CO for 10 years and misses it after talking with me. :-)', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-05 16:04:27', '2023-01-05 16:04:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000110772051', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000110777030', 'Melinda Cabot', NULL, '1-3-22 Melinda Cabot called to help Rylie her step daughter (I think). Rylie is 17 and going to school in WA DC in July with great ins. Melinda is retired. Rylie''s father is working and gets ins through work. He didn''t know her mom wasn''t covering her until just now. So, they want the highest ded catastrophic plan possible to get her through to July 1st. Cost was more in Frederick 80530 vs 80023 Broomfield in Adams County. Rylie is still a dependent, so using the 80023 zip. She doesn''t care about doctors, just lowest price.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-01-03 17:25:42', '2023-01-03 17:25:42'),
