  ('zcrm_1579374000106555028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000106614001', 'Lora Moody', NULL, '11-8-22 Lora Moody is 52 and husband Brian Wagner is 50 and their two daughters will soon be 10 and 12. They just moved to Breckenridge to from WI. Husband has been in corporate world his entire career with ins. They have ins until Jan. 15th. They are figuring out their employment moving forward. Lora quit corporate world once she had their kids and does some side work as self-employment. Husband isn''t sure yet. But, they are super healthy and rarely go to the doctor. They are doing their well child check but seriously disenchanted by our healthcare system now. She''s afraid they will try to force vax upon kids and not interested in that. They are free of covid vax and believe much more in acupuncture and naturopathic care. No real pre-x except husband has high cholesterol managed by atorvastatin. Can get that for $4-$15 easily. Lora is a runner and had bursitis back in Feb and still working to heal that 100%. She asked if she blows out that knee will the bursitis deem that pre-x. I told her it''s best to ask her doctor that question, since it will be up to however the doctor writes up the notes. She understands. She totally dialed in with her own body and with her girls as to when there''s anything wrong, and not needing to be reliant on the current system in the way it''s functioning.  They are focused on CARE+ for $780/$1000 which is $1620 savings to pay for any well checks they choose to do. She will not do a mammogram again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-08 15:16:48', '2022-11-08 15:16:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000106167042', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000106218001', 'Kimberly Elliott', NULL, '11-3-22 Kimberly Elliott, CEO with Fashion Flooring (Trade Name) is looking for ins for the first time in 28 years for their employees.  They have about 7-8 employees, 2 are Medicare, 4-5 need insurance. They want to pay most of cost and include spouses and dependents. They are already paying monthly fee for Peak Med at $70 per adult and $60 per child. They want a more catastrophic plan to protect them for the big stuff and even willing to self-fund for the high deductible, if need be. No tobacco users. Ages 1 U30, 1 in 40''s and 2 in 50''s, other 2 Medicare age.  She doesn''t think she wants alternative, but might change her mind when she sees the prices for 2023. She had a quote from Kaiser earlier in the year. So, I will include Kaiser in this quote.  She wants Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-11-03 15:18:04', '2022-11-03 15:18:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105646023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000105661023', 'Erin Whitney', NULL, '10-25-22 Erin is 62 and Jon is on Medicare already, so he''s all set. She''s paying Bright Health $860 a month now!  Earns too much for APTC. Self-employed. She was diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis 15-20 years ago but she''s treated with diet and exercise and hasn''t seen a dr and hasn''t had any symptoms for about 15 years. She''s had dry eye syndrome but nothing really to do for that. She takes Singulair/montelukast for allergies and GoodRX shows price at $3-$6. Finally she''s taking uvafem for menopause support and already pays cash for that. She''s not worried about any of those. Only potential issue is that she had a Leap procedure donein Feb. of 2021 for pre-cancerous cells. She''s had 2 paps since then showing all is clear! I suggested she gets her records and I''ll find out if they deem it pre-x or not.  If yes, she''ll wait until March 1st to start. If not, she''ll start Dec. 1st. She''s thrilled that this exists! She wants to share it with her network as well and is also excited for the $100 referral fee. She''d like me to present to her people. :-)', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-25 11:54:36', '2022-10-25 11:54:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000105160071', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000105221001', 'Kira Kearsey', NULL, '10-18-22 Kira is 48 and will be 49 in April 2023, husband is 49 and will be 50 in May, 2023. Kids are 16 and almost 19. They only have accident insurance at the moment. Love in Carbondale, CO and would like to go to All Valley Women''s Care with Dr. Nagel. It''s still not showing in network. Neither is Dr. Glode showing up.  BUT, Grand River Health in Rifle is showing that they accept Multi-Plan/PHCS where Dr. Glode practices. I told Kira to call in advance and make sure. 
 They are looking towards Dec. 1st start date since her husband is in Canada right for for week or two. Her husband is a realtor on his own. Kira isn''t employed, but is working as a care taker for her elderly parents. No meds for family except husband uses acyclovir for cold sores on occasion. They are healthy, active. I explained the tobacco clause once 50+ bc husband uses it on occasion. I let her know it may show up in a blood test and needs wouldn''t be shared if false information is provided by client. She understood. I let her know it''s a great incentive for him to quit 100%. Otherwise, they are great candidates. I also let her know the network might be removed very soon which will eliminate that challenge. They definitely partake in the well checks annually and are reaching the age of needing a colonoscopy.  SECURE is what we discussed at $715/$1000 for now and $915/$1000 in May at husband''s 50th BDay. She''s ok with that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-18 22:15:31', '2022-10-18 22:19:30'),
