  ('zcrm_1579374000104870018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000104884001', 'Sherri Stroh', NULL, '9-28 and 10-7-22 Sherri is going to be 63 in Jan 2023. Andrea is helping her husband Steve already with Medicare which they are thankful for. She came to me via Beth Fredericksmeyer via Cory Nickerson. Beth isn''t a member, but Cory is. Sherri is in the mortgage industry and W2 income but looking to transition out since market is slowing down and coming to a halt. Her income will likely decrease significantly. She''s not sure what her plan is or when she''ll make a change. But, she''s planning for the future right now to see what''s possible. Her current ins that she pays for semi monthly through her company is $21.09 dental, $60.84 medical and $3.57 vision. She understands I won''t be able to offer her it at such a low price. I described the SECURE membership at $1000/$325. She has med-high blood pressure and it''s well managed on mild meds which she pays $13.39 for 90 day supply. Yes, she does her annual wellness visits. As for showing self-employment, she can have Steve pay her as 1099 or some other way since she helps him with his business. That''s no problem to do to show self-employment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-07 15:34:39', '2022-10-07 15:34:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000104799020', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000104708165', 'Sean McRoy?', NULL, '10-6-22 Sean came to me via Terry Talley. He said she referred him to me long ago and he''s now wanting to look at insurance for his employees. He''s with Kaiser and doesn''t want to switch. He has 3 employees who are all single. Eric is 45 and x military so he also has VA. Steve is about 65, so Medicare. Michelle is 52-54 and isn''t super healthy, so maybe not a good candidate. He''s like to pay all of some of cost for employees. They were driving and asked me to send info. I sent the link to the video to begin. He will take a look and see if it''s a good fit for them.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-10-06 11:49:01', '2022-10-06 11:49:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000104399013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000104398043', 'Malle Gambuti', NULL, '9-29-22 Malle ios 37 and husband Leandro 39, kids 1 and 3.  Paying $1500-$1600 now through Ski Co as ski instructor. Leandro hurt knee last winter with a sprain and has been doing PT. I let her know about the pre-x clause for his knee and she understands. No other health issues in family, no meds and no tobacco. Malle is self-employed. We discussed SECURE and CARE+ since network is crappy. She understands that she''d pay cash and not get reimbursed for wellness visits, if they choose CARE+. Her ob/gyn, All Valley Women''s Care isn''t in the network. I also let her know they might remove the network limitations as of Jan. 1st, 2023 which would be ideal. She will talk with Leandro who''s stuck in the hurricane in FL right now, so she can''t reach him. They paid for the full year through June of 2023 for their current insurance. She didn''t realize that can cancel and get reimbursed if they want to switch. She also asked about Maternity and I let her know about the 60 day waiting period. So, if they want to start getting pregnant, she will want to join the membership sooner than later. She understands.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-09-29 12:45:59', '2022-09-29 12:45:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102932003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000102917021', 'Gabriela Pereyra', NULL, '9-13-22 Gabi is 54 and Hernan Vespa is 51. He''s self-employed. She''s looking for a new job and doesn''t get Cobra. She was laid off in late July.  I suggested they look at short-term medical in NJ if they think it will be soon to get a job and not need it for husband either. She has hypothyroidism and takes levothyroxine. She pays $30 for 90 vs she could get it for $10 for 90 through MPB resources. She also has endometriosis but doesn''t really do anything for that at this point. She had a surgery in 2019. She also get a colonoscopy every 3 years and I explained that will likely be considered diagnostic and would have to pay the $1000 IUA. She wants vision for both of them  and possibly interested in the HMA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-09-13 11:49:31', '2022-09-13 11:49:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102228020', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000051439001', 'Anne-Laure Peaucelle', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 2204 Question : Hi! I''m wondering what the process is to become a provider for the WholeHealth Living Choices program. I''m a yoga therapist and offer in-person and online services that would fit really well with what you offer.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2022-09-03 22:39:28', '2022-09-03 22:39:28'),
