  ('zcrm_1579374000098342003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000098334034', 'Margot DeVita', NULL, '7-18-22 Margot is looking at this for her 38 yr old son. Margot is retired and all set for herself. But, son hasn''t had health ins in many years and it makes her super nervous. She will pay for it if he refuses to. He''s closing on a house today and totally panicked by the closing costs and everything else. He''s a welder and she thinks he''s paid as W2 but she''s been trying to get him to set up an LLC. If so, he''ll qualify for SECURE. If not, he can choose CARE+. She''s thrilled to be able to watch the video and share it with him. He makes about $40K per year. Used to live in CA and got covered CA and has herniated disc at the time which showed as costing $200K at the time. Sounds like that was many years ago.  I''ll need to ask him about any pre-x for now. He currently just pays as self-pay. He did have stitches recently and cost him $800 for stitches.  Margot was referred to me by Joy Lanzano. Sounds like Joy had a Need recently and was happy with how it worked and how much she paid.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-07-18 12:26:08', '2022-07-18 12:26:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000098001018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000098018001', 'Jessica Van Antwerp', NULL, '7-13-22 Jessica is self-employed massage therapist. She has health insurance for $113 and it''s not ACA compliant and doesn''t cover much. She liked when Mary told her this includes mental health visits. She''s healthy, no meds, yes supplements. She chooses massage, chiro, acupuncture, etc. I forgot to let her know that she can seek alt care for accident, injuries, illnesses, etc. She thinks she wants wellness and is uncertain about funding HSA. She''s also looking at something called Go Forward in Denver that helps with preventative care, health screening and such. But, she doesn''t know much about it yet. She believes it doesn''t protect for major health issues, only preventative solutions to set you on a good path. Wants to read over SECURE and CARE+. Doesn''t know when she would want to start since just exploring now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-07-13 12:55:01', '2022-07-13 12:55:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000097228013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000097262001', 'Alex Lovejoy', NULL, '7-5-22 Alex is 53 and husband 54. They listened to my presentation at BSU and are considering changing from their current insurance plan to SECURE. They''re paying $1000 now for family of 5! They must have super high ded and mop, but she has to look it up. I suggested $1000 or $2500 IUA. She''s leaning towards $2500/$765 to get their monthly cost down. I explained the price is the same for 1 vs 3 kids. So, even if one drops off, price will remain. 19 year old son was recently diagnosed with late Type 1 diabetes. I read the exemption clause to her straight from the guidelines. She was happy it''s not an issue. He''s never been hospitalized or anything from it. Family has no other health issues, no meds, no tobacco. She''s paid for her current insuranace on June 11th. Knows earliest to join now is Aug. 1st.  Yes, they do their annual wellness visits and yes they have an HSA. Alex is self employed and does QHHT sessions past life work and PTSD clearing sessions.  They are also moving suddenly but just 15 minutes away. She wants to possibly join for Aug. 1st after she looks it over.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-07-05 16:34:15', '2022-07-05 16:34:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000096563008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000096555033', 'Ben Fillmore', NULL, '6-24-22 Ben is looking at this to help his clients. Ben was referred to me by Andre Simoneau since Ben is working with Five Rings as well in OR. His current clients are facing paying $1200 per the rest of the family to join the employee benefit. Employee is free and rest of family is $1200! So, Ben has a reasonable understanding of the membership after watching the video. I''ll send him the email as well. I answered his few questions. He shared it with his clients and they usually decide quickly. He expects to hear back any day this week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-06-27 15:04:13', '2022-06-27 15:04:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000096030013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000094440021', 'Ryan Castillo', NULL, '6-21-22 I reached Monica just now and she let me know some things have changed in their world all of the sudden. They are waiting for some paperwork to go through in the next few weeks. So, they aren''t ready to enroll quite yet. But, they will let me know if/when they want to enroll in the near future. They are ASHI members, so I need to use the ASHI link if they enroll. Super nice.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-06-21 11:12:51', '2022-06-21 11:12:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000094689011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000094688010', 'Chris Marseilles', NULL, '6-1-22 Moved to Denver, CO 2 years ago and he took a break from working. He was forced into Medicaid bc no income. He wasn''t looking for a Free option, he just wanted a subsidy but it wasn''t allowed. Now his income is coming in again and best estimate as realtor is $60K. It could be much higher, he really has no idea. He''s 55, mostly healthy with 1 med for general anxiety, 1 for slightly high cholesterol, no tobacco. He does have diverticulitis which flairs up from time to time. He has a colonoscopy at age 50 and again at 53. So, he doesn''t think he needs another one for a few more years. He did get stuck with the $2800 colonoscopy bill because they coded it as diagnostic. He was told if they put on the form that the screening was looking for polyps that it would been covered at no cost, but since they didn''t indicate that they were looking for polyps in the screening, but found and removed them, it''s then charged as diagnostic and the dr. had no control after the fact. This is slightly different from what I''ve been told. But, either way it was his bill to pay. Chris seems to understand pre-x and is also looking at traditional ins through C4 which I will help him with as well. With diverticulitis, he needs to determine the risk for SECURE vs C4 plans. He was diagnosed with arthritis in his neck many years ago. But, he hasn''t had any issues, treatment or any new diagnosis in many years on that front.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-06-01 12:03:14', '2022-06-01 12:03:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000094689003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000094440021', 'Ryan Castillo', NULL, '6-1-22 Ryan called to understand how payment works. I let him know of my trip June 3-17. So, he will talk with Monica tonight and see if she''s ready to enroll tomorrow. If not, we have an appt late on Monday, June 20th to enroll for July 1st. This is still contingent on her employer coverage and leaving her current job. So, he''ll talk with her right away.   They are interested in SECURE. He is an ASHI member. Use the ASHI link to enroll!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-06-01 11:11:14', '2022-06-01 11:11:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000094575036', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000091124105', 'Colin Fogerty', NULL, '5-31-22 Colin thought he was booted off of Medicaid but he logged into Medicaid and sees his account is still active. He will reach out to them to see what''s up.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-05-31 16:20:20', '2022-05-31 16:20:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000094575031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000092927033', 'Walker Teekell', NULL, '5-31-22 Ryan Morin says they can''t give an exact price for anesthesia until they know exactly what is necessary for his exact surgery. He will look into the Dr. Justin Michael King and also his aunt is looking into some insurance options that include his current doctor. I have no idea how she''s able to find something but we will see. He knows the deadline of June 20th and my leaving June 3rd-17th. He might have some more answers tomorrow or Thursday and will let me know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-05-31 14:49:17', '2022-05-31 14:49:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000094413018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000094440021', 'Ryan Castillo', NULL, '5-27-22 Monica and Ryan called bc Ryan just discovered MPB through ASHI''s website and they are thrilled. Monica is changing jobs and the new benefits are at no cost to her but 3x their current cost now for Ryan!  So, they are exploring this and like SECURE since he is self-employed, does his annual wellness visits and might possibly fund the HSA. They never understood the HSA before.  Ryan is super healthy and gets the best blood work and such from his wellness visits. They watched the video already and they might want July 1st start date. He should be all set for June with her current employer.  He typically chooses traditional medicine since he''s never had the option for alternative. So, he was intrigued about that. He understands it''s best practice to call the Concierge if her ever needs anything beyond the wellness visits to get help for highest quality care at the best price and for labs, meds, etc. They really seem to understand and are psyched to learn of this option. We will talk next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-05-27 17:13:47', '2022-05-27 17:13:47'),
