  ('zcrm_1579374000090792023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000090810021', 'Tim Duffy', NULL, '4-13-22 Tim is 45 and wife born in 1989, he thinks 32. They used LHS in the past but had a bad experience in getting reimbursed as they degraded and for the birth of their first child. They wound up needing to ask the local hospital for aid which they gave them. They are forever grateful for that. Then they went onto ACA for second child which was nice until he earned way too much money last year and now owes $17K back to gov!  Full cost I think is around $1666 but he blocked out the cost bc it''s so egregious. He thinks part of the problem is from Trump removing the penalty to prices increased too much. Also he has diabetes, Type 1 and required insulin which the costs are high. With his insurance now it costs $135 per month for insulin and products but his dr wants him to switch to newest solution in which I''m asking to price out via Reid for both options. There may not be good options which I let him know. He may have to remain on his ins and put rest of family on SECURE. They are all healthy with no pre-x.  Gaia and Wayne used to be business partners with Tim. Tim bought them out last week after having a banner year but that also bumped him into a much higher income level. He''s expecting another good year this year too. SECURE for family is $715/$1000 and also email information about VSP for wife.  Kids go to wellness every year and he goes every 2 years to get his boat captains license. Goes to endo 1x per year. For meds he''s using Express Scripts now with home delivery. He needs home delivery for this since lives in the sticks of AK.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-13 17:05:44', '2022-04-13 17:05:44'),
