  ('zcrm_1579374000088330003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000088286223', 'Alissa TBD', NULL, '3-8-22 Sandra Coulson came to me via Shelley bc she''s her orofacial myologist (myofacial therapist). Dr. Sandy is all set with health insurance for herself and sounds older than 65 with plenty of health issues with  a completed hip replacement and upcoming surgery on ear for hearing ruined by previous surgery. They will be putting implants in next. But, Alissa her Office Manager is interested and watched the video. She''s 29 and paying $212 for catastrophic plan with $8K ded and mop. She likes the idea for herself. They were thinking of trying to share this with their patients but it''s not ideal bc of the pre-x clause. Most clients have been referred in and need immediate care which is typically 8-12 sessions and an avg. of $1100. They may still share this with clients if there''s a good fit. I also shared the HMA concept with them and that might be a good option as well, especially the higher cost plans and can use the money for medical, dental, vision, hearing, etc. So, it solves a number of challenges. The higher HMA levels have  a much shorter waiting period to grow the account. I will send them all info about CARE+ (best for Alissa bc doesn''t do wellness) and SECURE to understand for business, plus HMA info.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-08 10:18:01', '2022-03-08 10:18:01'),
