  ('zcrm_1579374000081750033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000081767046', 'Lisa Spalding', NULL, '12-10-21 Lisa is 68 and husband is 81 and they lived internationally, Japan and England for most of life. They don''t qualify for Medicare. They already had their Kaiser auto renewed. But, husband needs neuro surgery done and they don''t want to use Kaiser''s surgeons for that. If the neuro surgeon they want will bill to Kaiser they will stay put. Otherwise, they''re looking to change their policy. Husband had a ruptured aneuryism recently and was in the hospital for 2 weeks. They currently have KP CO Bronze 6500/35%/HSA for $1,532.94 with APTC $1,322.23. But, this income won''t be accurate for 2022. She wants to see options but system won''t allow her to since already renewed. Due to age system won''t allow review on outside of account either. I''m not sure how to help... But, she''ll call me back when she knows more.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-12-10 16:49:22', '2021-12-10 16:49:22'),
