  ('zcrm_1579374000080957042', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000080958013', 'Traci Hagie', NULL, '11-30-21 Traci is a BSU member and saw my post. She works at BVSD and wants to leave but was most afraid to give up her health ins. Priced out reg ins and the lowest price started at $657.88 for Friday with $8700 Ded/Mop and $17,400 Group. She''s super healthy. But, just can''t breathe through a mask all day. No meds. Take B12 shots once a month, chiro and acu all as preventative. Dr. tried to help her with mask mandate to become exempt. So, she will check her records and make sure record is clear for pre-x. She has no problems, just a normal human who needs fresh air. Her step sister is with LHS but otherwise knew nothing of these. She wants Dr. Berger who''s in the Centura system. He doesn''t show up but Centura shows they accept PHCS/Multiplan. Husband has S-Corp and she has LLC for her mental health counseling business which she will try to do full time if she quits at BVSD. SECURE $1000/$500 best option for them. They do their annual wellness visits and she wasn''t really familiar with HSA.  Best guess at income $120K, $70K husband and hers $50-$60K or hopefully more.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-30 18:03:32', '2021-11-30 18:03:32'),
