  ('zcrm_1579374000079391018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000079390035', 'Chad Follmer', NULL, '11-10-21 Chad is 50 and lives in Louisville, self-employed and earns too much for an APTC. Healthy, no meds, no tobacco. He''s on Cobra now ''til next Sept. if he chooses. He''s paying $450 with an HSA. He did have a back muscle spasm in Jan or Feb of 2020 and got an MRI. He had a bruised facet(?) or fascia on vertebrae. He couldn''t remember diagnosis. He did few PT sessions and then it healed on its own and no problems since.  I told him to pull his records to determine last PT visit and clear bill of health. He can then join after the 24 months have passed which is around March 1st, 2022.  He will read over it all and better understand it. Originally he didn''t understand why it''s not listed on C4HCO. I explained and I think he understands the value of NOT being insurance. Discussed SECURE $1000/$275.  Also, Dr. Randy Pinto is in the PHCS network at Avista Hospital.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-11-10 15:32:34', '2021-11-10 15:35:05'),
