  ('zcrm_1579374000074411018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000074428001', 'Kelly McDonald', NULL, '8-27-21 Kelly is 47 and 12 yr old son. Son does not currently have insurance but plays sports and no pre-x. Kelly has controlled diabetes type II with affordable meds and she is willing to change to generic if need be as well. Currently paying $50 through ins. Typically sees a specialist 2x year and PCP 2x year for meds and blood work.  She also has hyperthyroid and anxiety meds. Seeks psychiatric care. She will pay $505 plus about $275 (estimate) for her an son = $780-$350, her cost is $430 estimated. With OPD it''s $544 +$40 and $584 - $350 and $234 a month at the $1000 IUA level. She''s in central Orlando. She also needs these labs done - CMP, lipids, hemoglobin A1-C, CBC, TSH, T4, D3, UA. She wants price comparison and send her the video to listen to. She will ponder switching to OPD after long conversation. She understands paying cash bc she''s done that for her son plenty of times.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-27 15:28:55', '2021-08-27 15:28:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074240003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000074235009', 'Heriangie Acabeo-Arroyo', NULL, '8-25-21  Candy is an employee of Primary Partners. She is 41 and healthy, only pre-x is seasonal allergies but no meds and no hospitalization. Just takes vitamin D. Wants to keep their pediatrician Dr. Mohammed Afzal. New price with BC/BS will be $397.40 vs OPD $299. She''s interested in cost for whole family as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-25 21:32:39', '2021-08-25 21:32:39'),
