  ('zcrm_1579374000073854035', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073533045', 'Donald Coy', NULL, '8-18-21 Don hadn''t watched the video yet. I told him to watch or I''d explain it. He said he''d watch and then proceeded to ask me questions. CARE+ is likely best for daughter but they probably don''t need it until Nov. 1st. So, he has plenty of time. He will also think about this for his wife for when he turns 65 and she needs something to protect her.  Sounds like daughter takes some $5 medication as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-18 15:14:42', '2021-08-18 15:14:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073600038', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073598072', 'Susan Mueller', NULL, '8-13-21 Susan is 59 and twins 25 who are both in CA. One can get ins through employer and the other can go onto Medicaid. Twins both have asthma and she wants them to start doing allergy shot treatments. She also had a colonoscopy 6 years ago with polyps removed. She was told all future colonoscopies will be considered diagnostic bc she had polyps removed 6 years ago. I told her to get a 2nd opinion on that. I haven''t heard that. Zip 80238 in Stapleton area in Denver.  She can get Cobra for $1200-$1300 for her and the kids. A Bright Health plan Bronze $0 would be $1088 (I think) with 2 kids and $620.96 for just her alone on plan. She will review what HR department can offer to her and call me next week. She has life change event so open enrollment ending is irrelevant.  Has UHC now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-13 15:44:51', '2021-08-13 15:44:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073600011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073598017', 'Chris Rowe', NULL, '8-13-21 Chris Rowe and his wife are both 53 (I think) and kids are 24 and 20. They are on his wife''s insurance with Anthem through her work right now. But, she will quit her job if they can find good ins. He doesn''t know what they pay right now, but not super relevant. They also pay for a separate cancer policy to cover all costs if someone gets cancer. They are all healthy, no tobacco. Chris takes doxycycline for acne and that''s it for family.  Live in VA. 
