  ('zcrm_1579374000073524031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073533045', 'Donald Coy', NULL, '8-10-21 Donald Coy was referred by brother (I believe) Mike Coy. Donald needs to find a solution for his daughter who''s turning 26 in Oct. They have Cigna now. He doesn''t want Medicaid for her due to lack of drs. who accept Medicaid. He thinks she''ll earn about $10K this year, therefore can''t qualify for subsidy either. So, MCS may be best option. I think she''s W2 employee as well. So, perhaps CARE+ can work.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-12 15:35:46', '2021-08-12 15:35:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073524008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073533001', 'Russell Duke', NULL, '8-12-21 Russell, wife and 2 kids under age 26. Russell has great insurance now through his employer who pays the full cost of the insurance. But, he''s leaving that job and choosing to become a Home Inspector and is newly an ASHI member. He''s researching many options but likes this the best so far. Except only hurdle is wife has mild asthma and daughter has mild asthma and Hoshimotos. Only use inhaler in rare circumstances. Daughter doesn''t take any meds for Hoshimotos. He will talk this over with his wife to make sure they''re comfortable with this. Have not been hospitalized from what I understand.  No tobacco and all healthy otherwise. He''s interested in VSP and HMA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-12 12:03:03', '2021-08-12 12:03:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073043008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000073037006', 'Laura Edwards', NULL, '8-5-21 Laura is currently on Medicaid for what she thinks is this year and next? But, she''s possibly starting a new job and wants to know what the future holds when she''s earning enough money. She''s most interested in CARE+ but she does do all of her annual wellness visits and is age 56. But, her doc IS in the network, Dr. Karlynn Sievers. She was thrilled about that so then leaning towards SECURE depending on job situation. She recently had a knee replacement and will be doing PT into September. She also had domestic violence trauma she''s been dealing with and Dr. Sievers was a god send through that. The Life Care may be very beneficial to her. She will not be enrolling any time soon!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-05 12:08:53', '2021-08-05 12:09:04'),
