  ('zcrm_1579374000071404008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000042338063', 'Josh Latham', NULL, 'NOTE:  Josh is on his own plan under:  Joshua Latham !!!   See that file!!!   Josh called looking for a certificate of membership for his child going off to college.  Did warm transfer to Kaleen at Liberty after verifying she is in the correct department to help him.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-07-06 12:15:24', '2021-07-06 12:24:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000071169023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000071186001', 'Ryan Robinson', NULL, '7-1-21 Ryan left a vm and I left one back. He''s a CPA and was referred to me by Dr. Drostan Baker. He''s wanting to learn about this for himself, his clients and possibly his employees. He''d like to learn about options with DPC and possibly the other options as well to best suit everyone he has in mind. He''s in Spokane Valley, WA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-07-01 15:30:16', '2021-07-01 15:30:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000070920021', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000070944001', 'Jamie Stein', NULL, '6-28-21 Jamie is turning 26 on 7/13/21 but can stay with parents ins ''til end of July. She''s 1099 contract worker and will make $45K per year. Therefore, not eligible for APTC. Wants to keep Dr. Emily Aaron and Dr. Beth Roland. No pre-x, no tobacco and just takes birth control. Yes, does her annual wellness visits. Open to MCS but wants to share with parents to get their opinion. I told her to share video and all docs with them as well as insurance options I will send over.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-28 15:57:04', '2021-06-28 15:57:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000070135003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069635001', 'Ashley Wilson', NULL, '6-16-21 Still deciding between MCS vs Anthem or RMHP. Sent her better version of trad ins. plans to review. Their pre-x are allergies and thyroid issues. Cost with trad ins will be twice MCS. So, may easily be able to pay for doctor visits on own and do MCS as long as son''s allergies aren''t a threat of possible hospitalization. The Buy Out with Biz is in negotiations with lawyers now, so that''s up in the air. They both each have their own business licenses to show proof of self-employment.  She feels like she has enough information now to make a decision. Dr. Robert McDermott and Dr. Carey Levin are both in network for RMHP and Anthem. Dr. Rebecca Percy is in PHCS and is partner of Dr. Levin. Suspect it will work for MCS as well. Told her to call them and ask. Dr. McDermott is specialist, so not relevant to the network for wellness.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-16 15:22:10', '2021-06-16 15:22:10'),
