  ('zcrm_1579374000069850013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069856009', 'Charlie Tarver', NULL, '6-11-21 Charlie, 58 is quite the jokester! He''s looking at this for his uninsured friends and maybe himself but he''s feeling skeptical for himself since he''s paying $1100 a month! He''s a skier and breaks bones but nothing else. No smoking, no meds. He had his shoulder rebuilt this past year. He understands if any problems arise with that it''s on him to pay. He brought Velvet onto the call. Charlie and Velvet both listened to the audio. Velvet is 45, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. John is 50, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. Asked him to listen to audio later so I could answer Charlie''s questions and not repeat everything they already heard. John is W2 but possibly adding 1099 work. Velvet is student and possibly adding 1099 work on summer. Charlie is retired, so CARE+ only for him. They know the deadlines for July 1st start date. Charlie will share this with his uninsured friends next. They want the link to the VSP information. Told them dental ins is waste of money and described HMA and sounded interested in that as well. I will send them both. Discussed CARE+ and SECURE.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-11 16:51:50', '2021-06-11 16:52:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069688138', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069816001', 'Arielle Wildau', NULL, '6-10-21 Arie is Jennika Wildau''s sister. Lives in Lafayette. She''s leaving her employment and benefits end Aug. 1st. She will qualify for Medicaid without a job. But, has epilepsy and takes meds for it that they are tweaking. She also has nerve damage in foot that she''s trying to resolve. The best orhto''s don''t seem to accept Medicaid. Told her to find out cash price. Traditional C4 she will pay full cost and $0 ded plans are $304 Oscar and $307 Bright Health and both have $100 Specialist visits. But, paying the premium may not benefit her unless she thinks she will need surgery.  She''s planning to take a few months off, travel and possibly get a new job in Oct. She''ll call me back when she has a better idea.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-10 12:23:57', '2021-06-10 12:23:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069637016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069635017', 'Kacy Popovich', NULL, '6-8-21 Kacy Popovich is the HR person that Jim Harper told me to talk with about health insurance. I was sent to Jim via Chadd Ziegler.  Jim said they are always looking for more affordable solutions. Currently they are about to offer Anthem and possible avg. is $400 per person plus $45 for gap insurance with a $7900 Ded and Gap insurance covering ded except for $2000. Some employees opt out for unknown reasons, others on spouse''s insurance and some on Medicaid. Totally open to offering this as an alternative solution or at least share the information but not necessarily paying for it through PSI. Their open enrollment is in July. She is happy to listen to audio and read SECURE membership info. If folks join outside of PSI then might only be able to offer CARE+ depending on if any 1099 work. Kacy''s husband is an electrician and she looked at health sharing for him in the past.  So, she has a basic understanding and is open to it. It may be a good option for her husband at the very least. Totally nice and open!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-08 12:12:20', '2021-06-08 12:19:44'),
