  ('zcrm_1579374000069637003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069635001', 'Ashley Wilson', NULL, '6-8-21 Ashley and Steve are both 40 and Nolan 4 1/2 and Landon 1 1/2. Mostly healthy. Currently employed through company that is offering a buy-out. They will research Cobra option to find out cost. They don''t necessarily know their income moving forward. Steve will probably take time off and Ashley is looking to start own biz but no idea how that will pan out.  They do have their children get their annual wellness visits, ie. want the MEC. Ashley takes Synthroid for Hashimotos. Priced  Synthroid 125mcg x 90tabs $66.12 + $9.95 shipping - $25.36 a month cheaper than paying $45 with their current insurance. Current insurance has a $6500 Family Ded. Steve is currently taking allergy shots $25 per shot and occasionally needs serum for $350. She expects no more than $1000 per year. Paying it on own already because will never reach ded. His allergies are seasonal to trees, pollen, grasses, etc.  Expect 1 more year of the shots. Want to keep Dr. Robert McDermott for allergy stuff. Son has allergies to nuts which they''ve managed very well! But, there is a risk and they will ponder that.  Also looking at traditional options for $1000-$1800 per month w/o any APTC. Might get some APTC with Cobra now too.  They aren''t quite sure if they will need a July 1st start date yet, since they need to decide if they will take the Buy-Out option and how fast. They were just offered this yesterday after it had been dropped for a while.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-08 11:17:04', '2021-06-08 11:22:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069034008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000069045001', 'Greg Thomas', NULL, '5-27-21 Greg lives in CA and considering quitting his current W2 employment to move to 1099 contract work. Wife has Epstein Barr which they are currently paying out of pocket entirely for with naturopaths right now. They used Samaritan Ministries years ago so they understand how this works. He listened to my audio. Wife also had a chiropractor do some neurological MRI and nothing showed up. So, just uses supplements to deal with it now. He understands the pre-x clause and caps moving forward.  
My Question in Slack - 
"Greg had non-Hodgkins lymphoma 7 years ago. Diagnosed in Feb. 2014. His last treatment was July 24th of 2014. He was given a clean bill of health at that time. They required blood panels every year for another 3 years. After that he chose on his own to continue to get the blood panels every year for simple peace of mind. He''s had no treatment, no scans or anything else required. Will Zion deem this as a pre-x or is he clear?"
Response from Dr. Jeff Lee with Zion, "If it is regarded as cured and did not require treatment or present symptoms for 24 months prior to membership it would not be pre-existing. We would need the record or at least a letter from his oncologist that the condition is cured."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-27 12:39:41', '2021-05-27 12:39:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000068428018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000068443001', 'Courtney Kieffer', NULL, '5-19-21 Courtney is on Medicaid now and earning $900 in child support. We didn''t count that in income of $75K for Benjamin. Ben is in end stage renal disease. Nephrologist is Dr. Michael Allen Rocklin. I saved  estimated Cigna plans on external drive including most important 4 meds. She will ask doctors how they categorize the meds or call Cigna since he''s currently on his employer plan  plus Medicare. She will do her homework and then we can revisit.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-19 11:38:15', '2021-05-19 11:38:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067853003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000067849001', 'Eileen Seeley', NULL, '5-11-21 Eileen is Luke Seaman''s mom. She realized when listening that this may be a much better choice for her and their 19 yr old child. They are paying a ton through her husband''s employer. She said he has a pre-x and probably needs to keep employer coverage. She has some super small 1099 income that she''s making sure she receives a 1099 for or other proof. This will give her the option for SECURE. If not, CARE+ is still viable option especially if saving so much, she can pay for her mammogram on own. She will explore. She thought she was locked in for remainder of year. I told her she can cancel whenever she chooses . She''s exploring this option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-11 12:26:25', '2021-05-11 12:26:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067367102', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000067483038', 'Dallas Blaney', NULL, '5-5-21 Dallas owns and operates Challenge America which is a non-profit to help vets around the country.  Based out of Basalt, CO. Currently just Dallas and 1 employee, Maggie Tolan who referred him to me. His biz was initially established in Denver, so they''ve been jumping through hoops to keep their grandfathered group plan and not switch address to Basalt to incur crazy high costs for healthcare. He wants to attract and keep great talent. He''s looking to grow the business. Maggie just had a baby and no known other health issues according to Dallas. Dallas has a hypo thyroid that he takes meds for. That''s it that he knows of. Nobody uses tobacco. He would like to chat with a current client that has had to use the membership for something big. I will have to find someone willing to chat with him.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-05 15:48:19', '2021-05-05 15:48:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067038008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000067089001', 'Robert White', NULL, '4-29-21 Robert is 58 12/29/1962 and had health ins a few years ago but got pissed bc somehow his policy lapsed without his knowledge and broker wasn''t helpful. When he declined a X-mas party invite it all went downhill...  He got frustrated and quit paying for health ins. He now has a knee problem that swells from time to time. He got stuck in a cattle fence. Works on a working cattle ranch and doesn''t have a computer. He''s working on getting one now and he''s working on getting an email address first and foremost. He used to rely on a friend when he needed to get online. He''s a hunter and outdoorsman. His income is about $50K which gives him a $501 APTC. He hasn''t seen a doctor for a few years now. He had a hernia surgery 8 years ago in Vail and through Medicaid he thinks. Now looking at Anthem he can get lowest cost plan for $140 with $8550 ded and mop. But, I should recommend Anthem Bronze Mountain Enhanced X HMO 7000 for HSA at $202 and gain the tax benefits and lower his out of pocket by $1500. He will call me as soon as he has an email address set up.  Super appreciative of my help!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-04-29 11:02:02', '2021-04-29 11:30:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000066446035', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000066329020', 'Cindy Kalmarx', NULL, '4-13-21 Realized that perhaps she can join DIRECT to deal with her pre-x and not have to worry about her income and # of hours she''s working through her employer plan, since they may cancel her benefits if her hours drop below 30 hrs. I recommended Nextera or Harmony Health $99 or $80 plus $245. They can help her manage sleep apnea and asthma. I''m finding out cost for Alvesco which is her inhaler for asthma that she needs. Says she at a good weight and everything else is good.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-04-13 16:57:28', '2021-04-13 16:57:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000066330011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000066329020', 'Cindy Kalmarx', NULL, '4-12-21 Cindy is 64 turning 65 in Jan. 2022. The full cost of a Temp Agency employer coverage is $548 and they pay $151, she pays the rest. She was trying to decide if she wanted that or not. She will have to be kicked off of their plan to gain C4 plan with a $435 APTC, if her hours drop low enough. She believes they will avg about 30 hrs per week at $35 per hour.  But, the group plan sounds better than the individual plans I reviewed for her. MCS isn''t ideal since she''s aging out and she has asthma and a c-pap machine for sleep apnea. She talks with her doctor about 1x per month! So, I''m setting  her free unless she gets put onto Cobra at some point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-04-12 16:51:54', '2021-04-12 16:51:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065893003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000065880001', 'Michele McDonald', NULL, '4-1-21 Missy is a personal trainer, massage therapist and her hours were cut significantly so she lost her benefits as of April 1st. They can join Cobra for $1700 or ACA for $1100! They mtn bike, raft, ski, back country ski etc.! Missy has blown out her knee 3x. She had a partial tear in 2013 and then fully blew it out in 2015 and never had it repaired. Hasn''t had issues since 2015. David is self-employed with an S-Corp and Missy is part self-employed. Live in Eagle, CO and Dr. Bettenhausen looks to be in PHCS network. They like to travel internationally such as Nicauraugua. Explained how that works. Wants earliest start date which is May 1st. She will talk with David further and make a decision. They were shocked by SECURE $500/$1000  compared to other options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-04-01 12:09:13', '2021-04-01 12:09:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065849008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000065861001', 'Deanna Hall Bowman', NULL, '4-1-21 Deanna is 56 and husband is 59. Both are W2 employees. However, after many questions Deanna finally revealed she also has a 1099 LLC for residential real estate. She''s an RN in the medical field and does billing and coding and has run across health sharing, but none that work quite like this! She listened to the audio and understands the Concierge practice. They don''t do their annual wellness visits, but she would like to do so. They are healthy, no chronic illness, no meds, no tobacco since 3 years. But, she did get a cortisone shot in her shoulder and had a skin rash. I told her these will be lumped into pre-x. Needs to talk with husband one last time to answer his questions that I just answered for her. Deciding between SECURE $500/$1000 or $420/$2500. Will try to call me tomorrow to finalize decision.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-04-01 10:07:54', '2021-04-01 10:12:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065677008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000065676029', 'Dwan Sloan', NULL, '3-29-21 Dwan is 56 and came to me via Andrea. She lives in Aurora and works for Target. They are dropping her from providing benefits bc they are calculating her hours in a time period where she had 29.94 hours which is just under 30 hrs to make them legally have to provide her benefits. She averages 32 hours but they don''t care. She''s paid $15.86 per hour and annualized it''s $28,421 which gives her a $435 APTC.  DOB 9/5/1964 and no major health issues. Takes meds for hot flashes and for inflammation in knee. Wants to keep Kaiser dr. but open to switching since they aren''t the most affordable. Bright Health looks to be best Silver plan around $180 per month. We will meet on Wed. after she gets into her C4 account.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-29 11:58:24', '2021-03-29 11:58:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065562019', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000065574033', 'Corey Litwin', NULL, '3-25-21 Corey is turning 47 in April and wife is 49 now, kids 11 and 13, live in Boulder. He''s been offered a new job with a Canadian company as a 1099 contract worker. They are giving him a stipend of $1300 to pay for health insurance, dental and vision. He doesn''t believe he''ll get to keep the excess though. He''s considering best Gold plan to use the money or MCS SECURE.  Now has an Aetna plan for about $2054 and he pays only $340 of it. So, he''s used to a decent ins plan for a lot of $ paid by employer. He did have a salivary gland procedure last year where he met his ded, but believes he can''t or won''t have any further problems with it moving forward. Dental is $172 for family which he''s only paying $42 now. Normally they don''t go to the dr. much, healthy, no other pre-x. But, they are going to couples counseling and would like to continue going. He will review all info I send and decide if he wants to take the offer of the new job and get back to me. He was super appreciate of my time and good explanation.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-25 17:26:22', '2021-03-25 17:26:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065515008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000065517001', 'Taryn Stone', NULL, '3-24-21 Taryn is 32, husband is 37 and daughter is 2. Through Covered CA they can get a plan for $425 - $470 with crazy high ded or mop at $16K which shocked them. They didn''t want to pay in $400''s but sounds relieved to have this SECURE option to protect them far better. SECURE is only option in CA for $685/$1000 or $575/$2500. Even at $2500 IUA it''s still far better than $16K ded or mop. Their income is about $90K total but could be more depending on taxes and such. She''s little concerned about pre-cancerous lesions. She had one removed on her ear recently and other things removed over time. She gets checked every year since skin cancer is in their family. I told her to call her doctor and ask how they would consider any further spots, if considered pre-x or new. Told her it''s really per the dr. records. I can''t answer how they deem it. She understood.  Husband is massage therapist with his own biz and she also has a small side biz selling hand-made blankets/comforters I think she said. Will be losing their current insurance. Told her May 1st is earliest start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-24 15:49:54', '2021-03-24 15:49:54'),
