  ('zcrm_1579374000064711011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000064713084', 'Anita Koury', NULL, '3-4-21 Anita is 62 and was sent to me by Doreen Fitzgerald. Her Cobra ends at the end of the month. She''s paying $700 through employer group for $1000 ded / $4000 mop. But, as individual it will be $733 with Oscar Silver for $8500 ded which was eye opening to her! She''s self-employed graphic designed and works in a gallery in Boulder. She does have a chronic possible interstitial cystitis. She''s going to CO Urology soon and doing some PT for these pelvic issues. She doesn''t know what negative repercussions could happen with this down the road. I told her to talk with her doctor about it. Also has some arthritis in neck and lower back. All will be considered pre-x. I don''t think this is a good option for her. But, she still wants to learn more. I explained pre-x clause in detail and IUA''s etc. Next I need to explain virtual healthcare when we talk. But, I don''t believe she will choose this since it puts her at risk!  She''s not on any meds and doesn''t need any surgery for her current medical issues.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-04 15:47:11', '2021-03-04 15:47:11'),
