  ('zcrm_1579374000064230027', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000064247020', 'Conni Bruce', NULL, '2-23-21 Conni has been on Medicaid with her son. He''s going to USC in CA now, so she just needs insurance. She''s been on her employers plan starting in Jan. 2021. However, she fell off a ladder and fractured her hip on Dec. 18th. It miraculously started healing on it''s own to her doctor''s astonishment!  She is nearly recovered and should be 100% by April 1st. Once she experienced the $12K MOP with regular insurance she was horrified and no longer wants to participate in that ever again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-23 15:18:23', '2021-02-23 15:18:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064174051', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000064183040', 'Shantel Carlson', NULL, '2-19-21 Shantel/Shannie is calling for her husband Steven who has MS. They make $85K household income, so too much for APTC. She really wanted him to qualify with his income at $55K but I told her that''s not how it works re IRS. DOB 7-7-70.  Zip 80015. He gets two infusions every year that cost $100K+! She originally thought they cost $5K-$6K until she looked at the bill! We are looking at a Friday Health or Bright Health, either lowest cost is Friday Health or $0 ded for Bright Health with Dr. Jeffrey Tan Sing in Parker, CO. They will likely easily max out MOP. So, also Bright Health HSA might be best. Sent them 3 plans to review.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-22 17:22:15', '2021-02-22 17:22:15'),
