  ('zcrm_1579374000063520011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000063253001', 'Sandrine Moser', NULL, '2-9-21 Explained how it works to Henri this time around and answered their questions. He seems to understand it now and they want to talk with others who are using the membership such as Mary Beth Hassett. Their daughter is seeing a behavioral health specialist that they finally found and really like. They can request her to be in network or find a new one. They are only paying $2.95 for Prozac at this time. They know of the Feb. 19th deadline for March 1st start date.  They will let me know if/when want to move forward. Wouldn''t commit to setting up next appt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-09 12:47:16', '2021-02-09 12:47:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000063244028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000063253020', 'Caroline Scott', NULL, '2-4-21 She will call me next week after determines if she can get kids on CHP+ for a little while as her income is low for a moment. She will enroll ES or EF very soon. Was also worried about strep throat turning into pre-x for having tonsils removed. Told her yes, but if she can be comfortable with 1 year of no sharing then she should be fine. She''s not worried. Just used to get them all the time and then it stopped. Then got it 2x last year but thinks she knows the cause.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-04 15:32:44', '2021-02-04 15:32:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000063244023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000063253020', 'Caroline Scott', NULL, '2-3-21 Caroline is 33, husband 36 and kids 3 and 1. She''s a mental health therapist and can bill some clients as 1099 and has professional license. Doesn''t like ACA bc had to pay back money at end of year when filed taxes bc income fluctuates. No tobacco, no meds. Has tubaligation since had eclempsia with both births. Had gastric surgery in 2015 and no issues since.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-04 14:24:22', '2021-02-04 14:24:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000063244018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000063253001', 'Sandrine Moser', NULL, '2-4-21 Sandrine came via Mary Beth Hassett and has talked with her a lot about how it works. Sandrine comes from France so this is all a big challenge for her. She likes the idea of being part of a healthy group working on living a healthy lifestyle. She felt badly for 30 years. Then she was connected to another person who had similar problems and suggested she stop eating sugar. She stopped on her Birthday, June 19th, 2019 and has felt better and better ever since. It was an immediate change that she felt within a few days! She has way more energy now than ever. She doesn''t drink at all, no tobacco. Super happy. Just her daughter takes mild anti-anxiety med and nothing else for rest of family. Kids are 16 and 18. She owns small business for 1 1/2 years teaching mostly women and some men how to use power tools. Husband left his teaching job with great benefits. They were only paying $400+ and now looking on marketplace qualify for Gold plan to only pay $600+ for her and kids, not husband. But, she will discuss this option with her husband over the weekend. She knows of deadline and will reach out next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-04 13:48:47', '2021-02-04 13:48:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000062988013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000063000037', 'Sharon Greenberg Goren', NULL, '2-1-21 Sharon is 60 and healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco. Her husband is turning 60 this year but he had 3 major heart surgeries. He was labeled as high risk but just had new blood work done which is showing much better levels, lost weight and is doing better. He will stay on his current health ins plan. Sharon wants to keep Dr. Courtney Sinclair in Canton, GA. She is showing up in the network! Sharon is unemployed since lost job due to covid. Husband is self-employed. Sharon only qualifies for CARE+ since unemployed right now. Paying $500 now and also gets dental for about $100 for the two of them. Not sure if that''s included in the $500. They are also looking for Life Insurance for husband at $350-$400K. Was paying $177-$180 for that amount but it just ended and cost is going up to $600+ a month, so shopping around. I will run quote and see if Mara is licensed or if I should get licensed in GA. Zip 30062. She doesn''t want life insurance for herself since has money from estate or death of family member. 
