  ('zcrm_1579374000055918008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000055937001', 'Kim Frodine ?', NULL, '8-21-20 Kim called via referral from Ryan Ashley. Kim is doing a cataract surgery in Oct and will exhaust their IUA. So, she may stay put to do other items such as colonoscopy that''s not included in Medishare. Paying only $288 with a $12,500 max share amt. She is self-employed. We could look at MPB Carez with MEC in future to give her wellness visits she wants. Used to be a member of Nextera with Dr. Flanagan. She will wait a year and call me if/when she wants to revisit the conversation.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-08-21 11:23:13', '2020-08-21 11:23:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000055742052', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000055743018', 'Tonsina Wells', NULL, '8-19-20 Tonsina is the Union Executive Team Member and Negotiator for a Regional Medical Center in Southern Oregon. They have 4000 employees but she''s focused on the 900 nurses at the moment. Their benefits are causing them to leave because families are liable for up to $15K max out of pocket which is crushing for most. There are also 2 networks in the area, one called, Asante and the other Providence. Providence has deductibles that are about half of Asante''s. But, their employees are being forced to use Asante (from my understanding). I could have this confused a bit. Tonsina is representing the employees and working hard to find better solutions. In ideal world, we''d get this going in a month. In realistic world, she realizes this may take 6 months-2 years.  Most nurses are 20-50/60. 80% female and 20% male. Unlikely to have smokers or too unhealthy.  They also want dental and vision. She sent me an overview for 2020-2021 to review.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-08-19 15:21:12', '2020-08-19 15:21:12'),
