  ('zcrm_1579374000046983008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000046985001', 'Alan Morris', NULL, '2-13-20 Alan just turned 60 in Dec., 2019 and his wife is 57. Suggested separate memberships to keep cost down. Quoted $507 and $335 for $842 total. They are paying only $654.58 for Medishare at $8K AUA which includes a $99 fee for her high cholesterol. She refuses to take meds for it bc of all the research she''s done. But, they are charging her extra for it. He''s going to check to see if they include the annual wellness visit or not. I don''t believe they do, hence the price difference. Annie broke her wrist over holidays where they had to pay $8K-$10K for it and hoping to get reimbursed from Aliera but they haven''t yet. They were on Aliera until booted off at end of Jan. Also just paid $120 fee to join Medishare for Feb. 1st.  No other health issues to report. They are both leaving town next week, so will look towards April 1st start date if they choose to switch. Happy to learn of options but may not switch.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-02-13 12:49:42', '2020-02-13 12:49:42'),
