  ('zcrm_1579374000044516023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000044517015', 'Laure Ettlinger', NULL, '12-12-19 Laure is 29 and husband 31 turning 32 soon. They are young and healthy, no pre-x. Also have a child. Asked about maternity. Has an indemnity plan now for $400+. Told her those are quite limited if something bad happens. They see the Dr. about 1x per year per family member. Earn about $90K but want to wait until Feb. or March to enroll to see how income remains. Husband might make a change and they aren''t sure how stable their income will be and don''t want to sign up until they know they can afford this. She definitely wants to keep the annual wellness visit included but I don''t think PSDHC is good idea up there now with challenges in network. She will reach out later after new year if chooses this route.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-12-12 14:23:30', '2019-12-12 14:23:30'),
