  ('zcrm_1579374000043977003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000043976001', 'Stephanie Brooks', NULL, '12-2-19 Stephanie 52, husband, 51, kids 16 and 13. They are paying over $2000 mo. for family of 4 plus 1 employee on UHC HSA plan. Stephanie wants to keep her doctors. She had melanoma 5 years ago. Husband had hip replacement, gout, shoulder surgery and may need another hip replacement. He should remain with trad ins to keep work plan going for him and employee. Diane Olssen mentioned Nextera but Stephanie wants to keep her current doctors, PT and acupuncturist. Mostly sees PT and acupuncturist since she''s been so active and has old injuries and surgeries. It would be idea to put just kids on but not possible. She will look it all over to see if it makes sense or not. Discussed PDHC as possibility.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-12-02 12:59:24', '2019-12-02 12:59:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043517062', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000043548043', 'Ryan Slack', NULL, '11-19-19 Ryan is 37 and wife is 38, son 5 and daughter 3. Healthy, no tobacco, no meds. Has Cobra option for $1000 PPO. Live in Basalt so Provider Directed is best option. Ryan did apply for Medishare already but wants to learn about this. He will have much easier time with this membership since he will be limited by PHCS network on Basalt and not with this membership. He''s super busy and wants to learn. He says to stay on him if I don''t hear from him. Put on calendar to contact him in Dec.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-19 15:04:28', '2019-11-19 15:19:55'),
