  ('zcrm_1579374000042887031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000042886051', 'Leslie Todd', NULL, '11-4-19 Leslie is diabetic but not currently on any meds. Doing the Keto diet now and managing it well.  She has high blood pressure and high cholesterol well managed on meds. Told her exemption will be going away.  She''s 63 and husband is 63. He''s on LHS now and aware of the reimbursement problems.  They are both members of Nextera already. Husband will decide if he wants to stay with LHS or switch. But, he''s turning 64 on Dec. 15th. Told Leslie he needs to join by Dec. 1st and she can join Jan. 1st since can''t join once turns 64. She was surprised by the cost different between Sedera and LHS.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-04 16:26:01', '2019-11-06 10:14:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042887026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000042886034', 'Callie Vardal', NULL, '11-4-19 Callie 36 and kids 2 and 4. Husband is 47 and has hip dysplasia and just had his right hip replacement surgery and will need his left done next, maybe in March 2020. Reached his ded for 2019 and will want to stay on Cobra for 18 months starting in July of 2019. Company paid for family until 10/31/19. Rest of family is healthy, no tobacco, no meds except nuvaring for bc. Looking at Redirect for family with kids since sees dr. 1-2x per person per year. Likes telemedicine and will use that.  Learned of this through Minn Kaess from Nextdoor! $500 IUA is $564 a month! Best option for monthly. They were going to be charged $1800 for Cobra for entire family.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-04 15:55:09', '2019-11-04 15:55:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042887013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000042886017', 'Chesney Midcap', NULL, '11-4-19 Chesney is most worried about her anxiety which has been turning into panic attacks. At $68K they get a $222 APTC with husband and 2 of the 3 kids on her plan. 1 kid is on grandma''s plan. Bright Health Silver is $834. Kaiser Silver is $921.93 with $20 copay for mental health visits. Kaiser Bronze plans don''t have co-pays for mental health. Sounds like she hasn''t been to Dr. since May when lost Medicaid.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-04 11:43:04', '2019-11-04 11:46:53'),
