  ('zcrm_1579374000030203016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000029930001', 'James Stanfill', NULL, '1-31-19  Members are 20''s-40''s. Want nationwide option. Mostly Male, only 6% women. Tend to be fairly healthy since in cycling industry. Most get their healthcare on their own. He thinks 50% get subsidy and 50% do not qualify. About 800-900 Individuals and 300 businesses with some overlap, therefore about 1000 members total. I described the PSDHC and mentioned we have other options for folks with pre-x or chronic issues. Sending site link for TDA to see other Assoc who has joined. He wants to share as much info as he can with the Board members to see if they will want to offer this to their members.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-01-31 14:35:52', '2019-01-31 14:41:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000030076008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000030073015', 'Megan Kinsey', NULL, '1-30-19 Megan is 34 and daughter Maddie is 5 months old living in Sunnyside, WA. She learned of Sedera from Pastor''s wife who uses LHS. She''s going to look into Medishare as well. Told her to check guidelines for maternity and limitations. They don''t cover wellness which she was aware of. They are healthy, no tobacco, no pre-x. Sees Dr. Galbraith who PA shows as in network. Told her to call practice to make sure all Dr. are in the PHCS network since only one showing. Dr. Weaver/Pediatrician is in the network.  She knows deadline and will call me when she''s researched and compared both. Wasn''t sure if she needs to get separate dental as well since doesn''t make sense with her 5 month old but WA mandates anyone under 18 has dental. Told her to ask locally.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-01-30 14:33:19', '2019-01-30 14:33:19'),
