  ('zcrm_1579374000017721003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000015699076', 'Chad Smith', NULL, '5-31-18 Chad is likely going to enroll today to be grandfathered into MPB group HEP plan. He can be referred by Tanya Dueri if need be or Heather Musmanno (not client yet). He will refer Jen Cenedella to get her grandfathered in as well in future. He might have double coverage for July with his current company before he quits.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-31 11:22:59', '2018-05-31 11:22:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000017547013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000017542039', 'Sai Jones Rajopadhye', NULL, '5-25-18 Sai is allergic to fur, seasonal allergies, etc. She needs shots on a monthly basis at $70 each as self-pay. She gets 2 vials 1x per year for $2000! Told her to find the cost as self-pay for that. The co-pay network plan won''t benefit her for allergy shots bc it excludes allergies. They are not planning to have kids at any point. She does have some GI concerns that she hasn''t figured out yet. Maybe co-pay plan good for that instead. Husband is healthy and just has adult ADD. Were just on Medicaid but going to hear $60K moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-25 15:14:53', '2018-05-25 15:14:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000017472003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000017471001', 'Vicky Balderston', NULL, '5-23-18 Presented ACCESS Co-Pay Network Plan! She has a bunch of health issues going on most of which are exempt from pre-x clause. She''s 61 and Rich (Dick) is Medicare age. No tobacco, no drugs, drinks alcohol 10x a year. Works for Dept of Corrections and is looking to retire or resign and perhaps do another PT job. She is almost 5 years cancer free in Feb. of 2019. Had uteran cancer and uterus removed entirely. Therefore that can''t come back. Only possible risk is vaginal cancer. She has Type 2 diabetes, non-insulin version and dr. might be able to take her off of meds soon. Is on Metformin now. Also has well managed high blood pressure and high cholesterol as well as stomach pills for gird. She sees dr. 1-2x per year. She can usually just call in refills. Also see gyno 1x per year to check bc of cancer from past. Also gets sick 1x per year that she thinks is sinus infection but turns out to be allergies. Had knee replacement in Jan. 3rd 2018. Will need the other one and is hoping to wait until on Medicare to do so. Told her it''s pre-x and best to wait ''til 65. Also might want to switch to trad ins. when she can get APTC with income at $57K per household in 2019. Tax credit sounded significant but may not be so since only covering her, not her husband.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-24 16:34:22', '2018-05-24 16:34:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000017406009', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000017402001', 'Donald Smeller', NULL, '4-23-18  Kelly received an inbound sales call from Donald.  I (Ron) returned his call.  He explained he lives in Largo, FL and is just completing his training to become a home inspector.  He said the company that he used for his training, after he became a member, he inquired about health insurance and they provided our company name and said they have a special group rates.  That prompted him to call us.  I explained our program and how it worked but he kept referring to insurance and the way he is comfortable how insurance works.  At that time I told him maybe I''m not aware of this Association but as far a special group rate I was only aware of our standard pricing.  I kept reminding him this is NOT insurance and after a about 30-minute or more I suggested a couple times that our program may not be right for him.  Then he would reply well insurance is so expensive maybe I''ll consider this.  Near the close of our conversation he seemed a little annoyed that the company did not properly explain our plan and he was going to call the up and discuss the situation.  I told him I would email him some information and left it at that.
I went and spoke to John K about the call because prior to the me calling Donald, Kelly,  John and I were briefly talking about the inbound call and John thought that we did have that association set up.  He looked around in the CRM and did discover it was Wendy''s account.  We called up Wendy and John ask her if it was her account and she reply she thinks so.  I told Wendy about the call and she said she would call Donald and handle it from here.   I did not send the information since Wendy took over the customer.', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2018-05-23 21:36:13', '2018-05-23 21:41:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000017403033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000017402001', 'Donald Smeller', NULL, '5-23-18 Spoke with Donald after Ron spent a long time with him. Donald was super frustrated bc he thought ASHI was misinforming him about their relationship with MyAHE. After I explained the program to him and our relationship with ASHI he apologized to me for being difficult at the beginning of the call. He must visit his doctor every 3 months to check on his blood pressure which he takes tennerol for. He doesn''t want to be discouraged from going if he has to pay for it every time. He looked into LHS extensively already but he needs to know they will consider his high blood pressure pre-x and Not exempt it. When I realized he just wants co-pays for his dr. visits, I shared with him our new Co-Pay plan that will cost him $383 at age 55. He wants to read about it first to get comfortable with it. He had swine flu in 2007, fainting/hypertenstion in 2011, never smoked and never drinks, could lose some weight and could exercise more. Just quit his cushy job with great benefits that he''s had his entire life and is struggling to have to pay so much for bad coverage on marketplace that is showing $700-$1500 for him in FL at his age for no coverage. He said he tried to get some info about trad health insurance and submitted his name and number online and has received about 200 calls in the last 2 weeks. He''s very interested in our co-pay plan now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-23 15:56:19', '2018-05-23 15:56:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000017329018', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000018687001', 'Christina L. Davis', NULL, '4-22-18  Kelly gave me a lead from inbound sales today.  I called and spoke to Victory regarding our plan for his wife Christine.  I took him to the MyAHE website and presented our plan.  He ask many good questions.  I sent him the 1st approach letter and HSA Bank info.  He likes it 100% and will discuss with his wife and enroll this week.  I will follow-up in 2 days', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2018-05-22 13:18:03', '2018-05-22 13:18:03'),
