  ('zcrm_1579374000016864010', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000016868014', 'Beth Colbert', NULL, '5-9-18 Bryan looking for wife whose 43 and he''s turning 67 next month and retiring in Aug. He will be on Medicare and looking for her. Both work for school and they force them to get 2 individual plans as a couple. Crazy! Healthy, no tobacco, eat mostly Paleo diet, work out 4x week. Wife is currently on disability for depression bc of bad incident with some students. Explained pre-x clause and not covering mental health bc pre-x but can help with cost of meds. He''s more concerned about if she gets sinus infection or something like that. Currently covered with Anthem. Read about Sedera a little already and has reasonable understanding before I explained it all. Told them the plan will be changing but we can likely grandfather her into the current HEP with MPB if enrolls sooner than later. They are covered through Aug. But, might choose to apply in June or July to ensure gets on plan. He''ll talk it over with her and Mike McGimpsey. He really likes the concept and said I explained it well. Believes in the health assessment''s mission as well.  On board. I sent him email #1 to read through and share with Beth.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-09 14:11:29', '2018-05-09 14:11:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000016618081', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000016633026', 'Patricia McDannell', NULL, '5-4-18 Family with 11 yr old daughter. Karen''s going in for colonoscopy since family history of problem. She''s not yet 50. No meds, no tobacco, self-employed for now or longer if all goes well. Paying $1300 mo since Oct. for Cobra now which includes dental. She did Not like sounds of LHS bc of exclusiong and limitations. Doesn''t like pre-x clause bc is afraid there''s too much room for then to deny new issues. Told her to pull her dr. records and if there''s anything of concern we can run it by Sedera first. That sort of settled her down. She doesn''t want surprises and hates insurance. Apparently her pregnancy was considered pre-existing condition with ins a while back.  She was a bit short but curious enough. She doesn''t like all the different components involved. Sounds too confusing. She does possibly want to see a naturopathic dr. in town that doesn''t accept insurance for gut reasons. Maybe ReDirect would be better for her in the future.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-04 14:32:39', '2018-05-04 14:32:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000016618068', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000016633001', 'Keri Norley', NULL, '5-4-18 No insurance now. From Australia and they don''t have to pay anything for it in Australia so she says they''d go back to Aus in someone had something bad happen. Found some ACA plan for $700 supposedly, but I''m not convinced and found some other option for $400 or so and she had no idea what that was. So, explained HEP and likes the concept and will discuss with husband. I''m not sure they will move forward since she admits she really doesn''t want to pay for this at all but people keep telling her she needs to. Who knows. She''s 40 and had her B-Day this week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-04 12:56:50', '2018-05-04 12:56:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000016577003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000015524001', 'John Cutschall', NULL, '5-3-18 John is enrolling now. Yes health conscious. 54 lives in Louisville. Has macular degenerative eye disease. Uses eye vitamins and eats well and exercises. No tobacco. As of April 6th was getting tested at Kaiser for acid reflux. Assume results were good since is choosing to enroll. Was paying $500 month with Kaiser. Realtor. Enrollment complete - 1:25 pm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-05-03 13:10:25', '2018-05-03 13:28:06'),
