  ('zcrm_1579374000010964026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010954074', 'Mary Huffman', NULL, '11-17-17 She wants to read up on more information and is excited to join. She will likely join in the next 90 days or so. She will contact me around the 10th of the month for the next month''s start, whenever she decides for that to be.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-17 11:13:10', '2017-11-17 11:13:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010964013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010954067', 'Kosta Korres', NULL, '11-17-17 Super healthy, Kosta 37, Amy 35, kids 6 &amp;8. Has HSA from old employer but mostly drained account. He gets $500 from his employer to help pay for health ins.! He also works with folks in TX, NY, CA who need help and may be excited to have this as well. They might try to push it to get a Dec. 1st start once he talks with his wife Amy in next few hours. He will call me.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-17 10:25:58', '2017-11-17 10:25:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010928013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010929011', 'Sarah Ravenscroft', NULL, '11-16-17 Paying $2100 in 2017 but going down to $1800 with a higher ded. Daughter 9 months old has excema and uses steroid cream, 5 yr. old, daugther and husband has 18 yr old as well. He has a 23 yr. old who is insulin dependent and not good candidate for plan. Healthy otherwise, no pre-x, no tobacco or drugs. She''ll show her husband and get back to me in a few days. Wants a Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-16 13:44:46', '2017-11-16 13:45:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010879081', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010896053', 'Matthew Seckinger', NULL, '11-15-17 paying $310 for accident and medical policies but going up to $400 in 2018. Had kidney stones that passed while he was in urgent care. Got lucky but still had to pay for visit. Also got bronchitis and flu this year but that is unusual. Is engaged to Hannah and getting married this Aug. At that point he will likely get on her insurance depending on her job situation at that time. Has an HSA compliant plan but I don''t think he set up the HSA account. Looking for Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-15 17:20:13', '2017-11-15 17:20:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010879066', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010896039', 'Ryan Donahue', NULL, '11-15-17 Ryan is covered through work starting Jan. 1st. But, girlfriend is paying $400 for a high ded plan that sucks. But, has a $250 plan now that covers only 1 doctor visit.  She has dr. appt because she thinks she has a cyst in her breast, so just checking on it. That is Nov. 29th. So, they will wait until after appt to make sure it''s all good. Will do a Jan. 1st start if clear. Otherwise will go on his ins. She isn''t earning any money right now. I''m not sure why. Must not work. Sounds like he''d want the $500 IUA. Have follow up appt schedule on Dec. 4th 10:00 am.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-15 16:30:12', '2017-11-15 16:30:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010879053', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010896022', 'Yael Flusberg', NULL, '11-15-17 Yael (Ya-el) She will contact me Mon. after Thanksgiving at the latest to proceed. Going to share it with her husband and find out the cost for her to stay on BCBS bc of breast cancer 1 1/2 years ago. Just had surgery, no treatment otherwise. Husband was a Dr. in Peru and native to Peru but now practicing more as homeopathic / intergrative doctor here in US. They will likely enroll him for now and add her in a year and a half. Is fine with doing this program that is better than LHS that Laura recommended. But likes Mennonites. ;-)', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-15 14:23:57', '2017-11-15 14:24:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010879035', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010726060', 'Ashley Spriggs', NULL, '11-14 17 They might keep Medicaid for son in Dec. to buy them more time. She''s preferring to chose the most stable, compliant solution, ie. HEP/Sedera, not LHS since exempt, not compliant. Son needs his 9 month shots asap. But, may do that in OH or wait. She wants husband to look over everything and ask me questions since he''s better at this. He''s going to look it over tomorrow. Their life is chaotic right now with the move and job changes etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-15 10:12:36', '2017-11-15 10:12:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010881047', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010880046', 'Janda Steward', NULL, '11-14-17 Wants info to review before our talk on Friday. Works with Matt Ross in Basalt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-14 15:49:31', '2017-11-14 15:49:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010759053', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010760093', 'Bruce Holiday', NULL, '11-10-17 Super nice. Calling about LHS but I explained we have a slightly diff. solution and explained. He''s healthy, 40. I forgot to tell him pre-x clause. Marketplace going to cost him $330. Phone # FL but not sure he''s in FL.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-10 17:46:35', '2017-11-10 17:46:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010759028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010760028', 'Kirsten Atkins', NULL, '11-10-17 Self-employed and rates going up to $1700 as couple. Neighbors going up to $3000! She has a knee surgery this year. I told her the pre-x clause. Likely wanting Jan. 1st start but needs to see when her short-term ends.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-10 15:35:55', '2017-11-10 15:35:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010727044', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010726060', 'Ashley Spriggs', NULL, '11-9-17 They are moving from OH to AZ now. "Our situation is a little unique in that my husband is currently working & is offered insurance through work. However, our goal is to bring him home by December 1st to work freelance with me (starting our own LLC in January/February). We have an 8.5 month old who we want to schedule for his 9 month shots here soon. So we are stuck with not knowing whether we should sign up through my husbands work for the month of November or deny it, and set up insurance with you." She found an option through Freelancers Union for cheap $464 and $2800 Ded but found horrible reviews online so now scared away from that. Jessica mentioned LHS and said she''s paying $299 for her family which has to be a typo bc no possible. Is likely $399 Plus HES $50 for $449. But limits on wellness and vaccines which will not be good for them because they have an 8 1/2 month old who need his next immunization right away. So, this may be a hardship for them to pay the Under 30 price with us at $586/$1000 IUA for U30 Family.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-09 17:23:57', '2017-11-09 17:25:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000010727036', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000010726053', 'Robin Kay', NULL, '11-9-17 Husband is on Medicare. She''s been with Kaiser past 2 years and not eligible for subsidy. Premiums around $675 per year, therefore unaffordable. She''s definitely interested and wants to read more about it. Also wants to share with her Lyons group of about 50 folks to see if they want me to come in person to explain it. Perhaps Thursday afternoon Nov. 16th.  She is very healthy, 58. Has insomnia and pays about $200 for meds per year. Not concerned about that part at all.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-09 15:59:52', '2017-11-09 15:59:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182853177', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012024130', 'Julie Meko', NULL, 'Julie is hoping to increase her IUA to $5000 to bring down the monthly amount much more significantly.  She submitted the Change Form and it will go into effect for May. She was OK with that. That will bring their $774 for Secure HSA to $668 for Care+ and then to the $5000 IUA it will be $442. So, they''ll have a massive monthly savings since they rarely use any services and only want alternative care.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-20 15:58:09', '2026-03-20 15:58:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182853172', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154481297', 'Lisa Rediger', NULL, '3-20-26 Lance is enrolled but wasn''t showing up as enrolled with UHC. Monica with UHC Broker Support put in an escalations ticket for me with TKT # SR20193755. They will make sure to note him as active like he should be. Monica will send me an email when their account is fixed. Then I will be paid the proper missing commissions as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-20 14:45:34', '2026-03-20 14:45:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182845316', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000171886002', 'Sheree Richards', '3/20/2026', 'Sheree asked how to find a provider for colonoscopy I sent her this email: <br><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">I will outline the next steps below to help guide you through the process and ensure you are able to identify a provider that best fits your needs.</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><ol style="list-style-type:decimal;list-style-position:inside;"><li style="list-style-image:none;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><p style=" display:inline;"><a style=" display:inline;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;" target="_blank" href="https://providersearch.multiplan.com/"><u>https://providersearch.multiplan.com/</u></a><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">  (this is our provider link to the list). </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><p style=" display:inline;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">You will (only ever) need to sort it by "PHCS Specific Services" </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><p style=" display:inline;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">From there you can search by zip code, specialty, facility, name </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><p style=" display:inline;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">For you specifically enter your zip and gastroenterology </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><p style=" display:inline;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">It will show you all the providers operating under the network in your area.</span></p></li></ol><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">When making an appointment, please verify with them when you call that the doctor of your choice is still operating under the "PHCS Multi Plan Network." </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">If you need any further assistance, feel free to reach out!...rc</span></p>', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-03-20 14:42:54', '2026-03-20 14:42:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182853167', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152460004', 'Sharon Montini', NULL, '3-20-26 She''s gone from my BOB.  No response.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-20 14:40:52', '2026-03-20 14:40:52'),
