  ('zcrm_1579374000178551143', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '1-12-26 Genevieve and William have decided to put Genevieve and 3 kids under age 26 onto Premium HSA for Feb. 1st start date. Their son with the jaw issue they will pay cash $5K for the surgery on their own. It will be cheaper to pay the cash price than to put him on William''s RMHP. They chose Premium HSA EC $676/$1000 $125/$25. Genevieve is self-employed with their own business and used their EIN to enroll for Feb. 1st, 2026.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 16:39:47', '2026-01-12 16:56:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551103', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000178551098', 'Michelle Bouvard', NULL, '1-12-26 Michelle came to me via Nancy Gentry. They got onto the topic of healthcare while they were hiking together. Michelle lives in CA and Nancy in CO. Michelle is 56 and her husband is 56 as well. Her husband is self-employed. They are 3 kids 23, 19 and 17. They are about to pay $3400 per month for their self-insured plan through work via Cobra with Kaiser! This covers them for everything including ded and mop, except they pay small co-pays for things. This is $40,800 per year!!!  If they choose Secure HSA they will save $28,800 that they can put towards their expenses. Her biggest concern is her husband''s skin since he''s had melanoma removed and a recent large one removed. He goes to the derm 2x per year for checks. I told her he may be best on Covered CA. She will also call derm to obtain his record and find out worst case scenario. She''ll also ask about cash prices as self-pay. Her daughter is having some minor digestion issues which might be gluten intolerance. Daughter is a ski racer and son is a big wave surfer. So, they are super healthy but could get injured. They takes supplements as well. She will watch the video to continue wrapping her head around it all. She''s also excited about the HSA aspect since they can easily pay the max to that and still be ahead of the game. She''ll do her homework and call or email next. She may push off the start date to March if she doesn''t have answers that fast.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 14:43:37', '2026-01-12 14:43:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000177351396', 'Judith Herr', NULL, '1-12-26 David and Jude called back to enroll. They are in Nicaraugua right now and were in a restaurant with native music playing in the background. They enrolled in Secure HSA $1250/$774 and included Nikki Boye on the app. They come home Jan. 31st in time for their start date. All set to go for Feb. 1st. Jude is the primary since she''s a realtor and self-employed. David is retired and 1 year younger than Jude.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 11:24:37', '2026-01-12 11:26:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551001', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000177351396', 'Judith Herr', NULL, '1-12-26 Left vm for Jude for our appt now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 11:03:56', '2026-01-12 11:03:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178302023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170389022', 'Alison Huskie', NULL, '1-7-26 Alison enrolled with Jack Taylor in the background. They are friends. Alison lives in Montrose and Jack lives in Longmont. Jack is friends with Carol Banks and her friend James! Small world. Alison takes gaba pentin and valocyclovir. She was worried about how to access those moving forward. After much conversation I finally understood that she has a DPC membership with Trailhead Clinic in Montrose who prescribes them. She pays $100 per month to access this DPC. Once I understood, I let her know she can keep that and it will work well in conjuction with Premium HSA. She does do a <span style="color:rgb(73, 80, 87);background-color:rgb(248, 249, 250);">BCR-ABL1 Gene Rearrangement, Quantitative, PCR (Quest) every 6 months. Last time it was $800-$1000. I looked it up on Lab Assist and it''s showing $282.97 at Quest in Montrose. She''s thrilled to hear that. Otherwise it''s $678 or so in GJ which is 2 hrs away.  She enrolled in Premium Care bc no self-employment and also has DPC. She chose $299/$1000 and is going to change her payment method from ACH to CC to avoid any problems with banking. All set for Feb. 1st, 2026 start date. Also PARA was going up to $800 per month for her. So, she''ll save a significant amount, $500 per month which is $6K per year simply on her monthly cost.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-07 14:43:19', '2026-01-07 14:53:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178176791', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '1-5-25 Selected me as their broker and will call me soon.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-06 20:25:10', '2026-01-06 20:25:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178176761', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000178176751', 'Celina Allen', NULL, '1-6-26 Celina was referred to me by her friend Shannon whose last name she doesn''t know. She''s 23 and healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. Lives in Montrose CO. She is on her mom''s plan with Aetna but it doesn''t work well since mom is in WA state. So everything is out of network and failing her. She files her own taxes and expects to make $30K this year. She''s also going to go to graduate school with a little help from her family to pay. But, the RMHP looks the best for only $1 since she gets a tax credit to pay for the entire amount. She was shocked and pleased. She''s all set and submitting the initial payment now. She will also call in 7-10 bus days to set up auto pay.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-06 17:14:26', '2026-01-06 17:14:26'),
