  ('zcrm_1579374000178176726', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000178133031', 'Abby Emdur', NULL, '1-6-25 Abby is trying to decide if they keep the entire family together possibly with the Cobra plan with a $3500 family ded and $7000 family mop for $2500 per month. She uses the entire ded and mop for her meds with some special program that pay for the ded while she just has to pay $5. It''s a crazy system that I don''t totally understand. But, she believes they reached the family mop last year simply due to the meds. However, if Josh moves to Premium HSA $1000/$363 or $1500/$336 they will save about $537 per month which is $6444 savings. Even if he has one incident they will be ahead financially by $5444. Josh has his own small business but also works with another small business who is offering IHCRA with a $500 stipend. I told them to find out if he can just choose his own plan. If they are hung up on the tax benefits, perhaps they can give him $400 instead of $500 which still covers the full cost of Premium HSA at the $1000/$363. He''ll be ahead of the game and so will the small business.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-06 14:35:39', '2026-01-06 14:58:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178176698', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000178176693', 'Tyler Scherffius', NULL, '1-5-26 Tyler works as an independent contractor with Mountain Insurance with Gail Longnecker. She introduced us. Tyler used to use Medishare but spent too much time trying to get reimbursed when they had a Need a while back. So, he doesn''t want to go through that again. He is 47 and wife is 50 plus a 12 and 10 year old. They live in BV, CO. They are facing a $2000 plan with Anthem which is ludicrous, in his own words. Angie had a knee replacement last year that is doing very well. Angie had open heart surgery at age 4. She''s been doing perfectly well since. However, she chose to do a heart scan last year just to check on things and they can see a leaky tri cuspid valve. Apparently they aren''t worried and there''s nothing to do at this time. I told her about the pre-x clause and suggest she stays on Anthem and the rest of the family can do health sharing. She also has a thyroid issue treated with meds. They like to do wellness and don''t care about HSA.  They take some basic supplements. They are also considering including Angie for a year or more to get through the pre-x clause while keeping trad ins as primary. They will review it on their own and get back to me. I discussed Premium HSA since the pre-x clause is better, they don''t care about alt care and it''s more affordable. They will also find out the cost to just keep Angie on Anthem and move the rest of the family.  They are eyeing a Feb. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-06 11:46:42', '2026-01-06 11:46:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178133036', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000178133031', 'Abby Emdur', NULL, '1-2-26 Abby 50, husband Josh 48 and kids 15 and 14 live in Boulder, CO and were referred by Julie Boylan. Their Cobra will start Feb. 1st and they would pay $2500 EF with a high ded. Abby has rheumatoid arthritis and 1 kid has a rare eye condition that he or she just had surgery on. He or she has to go back quarterly for check ups. So, C4 is best for Abby and 1 kids while MCS is good to husband and other kid. Abby wants to keep access to UC Health due to working there for 18 years and knowing everyone. She wants Select Health. She will also watch the video with her husband to review that option. Abby takes Orenicia which is a Specialty Medication. She''s on some program where they pay for her ded which is $6K and then she pays $5 co-pay per month to obtain the medication.  However she will lose this deal if/when she changes plans to Select Health. She will have to start over with the ded and co-pay. She will lose the benefit of her Accumulator Program apparently. So, it we discussed putting Abby and one kid onto the C4 Select Health plan and husband and other kid onto MCS.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-02 16:39:31', '2026-01-06 14:13:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178133014', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '1-2-26 William and Genevieve are most concerned about William''s meds, Mounjaro, Repatha and Jardiance. They all say NOT Specialty but ther are Tier 3 or 4. It looks like they would be Preferred or Non-Preferred meaning $50 or $200 per month. One son plays hockey and needs jaw surgery from getting hit. So, he will be best served on the C4 plan with William. If all family members join C4 it will be $3540.09. They are paying $2900 for Cobra right now which is ending Jan. 31st. We will likely put 2 kids or all kids onto Premium HSA. One can double up with ACA RMHP/UHC plan with William until he does his jaw surgery and all is well. They each go to different schools and we don''t know if all schools will accept the MCS/MEC or not. They will discuss all of the options and. We have our next appt on Monday, Jan. 12th at 4:00 pm. She wants William''s help but I let her know I can do the C4 part and talk her through the MCS app. Kids are Olivia 24, William S, 24 soon and Cedric 21.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-02 16:07:42', '2026-01-02 16:07:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000177351401', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000177351396', 'Judith Herr', NULL, '12-18-25 Jude 60 is a realtor in Boulder and was referred by Nikki Boye. Her husband is David and turning 59 in Jan. 2026. They want a Feb. 1st start date. They are facing a $1600 month payment with a high ded. Jude has Hashimoto''s and just takes NP thyroid which she gets super affordably from Costco. Otherwise she manages it with diet and lifestyle changes. David is healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco and no meds. Yes, they do the wellness visits and they have an HSA and HRA. They are deciding between Premium HSA and Secure HSA. They will be in Nicaragua Jan. 3-20. They are trying to decide before they leave but if not will hope to have a US IP address in order to successfully enroll which they are away. They are also about $5K over the threshold of getting an APTC with C4.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-22 23:10:30', '2025-12-22 23:10:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000177351249', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000177351244', 'Richard Hanson', NULL, '12-22-25 Richard (Rick) came referred by Ann Zimmerman. He is 60 his wife is 61. They live in Central Point, OR. His wife is a heart patient with a valve replaced 8 years ago and now has a pace maker 4-5 years ago. She will not qualify for LX and isn''t a good candidate for MCS. They are slated to pay $2800 per month in 2026. He wasn''t open to the idea of splitting them up to even bring their cost down by $1000. They are paying about $600-$800 in 2025. He can''t fathom paying $2800. If she remained, we are guessing it would cost $1400 + with MPB about $450 - $1850. That was not appealing and I haven''t heard from him since. Not sure what he can do to help his wife her her pre-x outside of ACA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-22 15:54:21', '2025-12-22 17:38:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000177351239', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000177351234', 'Andy Clark', NULL, '12-16-25 I left a vm with Andy at 4:45 pm. He was referred by Amy Anderson.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-22 15:42:41', '2025-12-22 15:42:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176653001', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175892049', 'Kurt Leinbach', NULL, '12-16-25 Kurt is not comfortable with MCS at all. He''s interested in LX but had to go talk with someone in the lobby of his business. He said no to the health questions, so he''ll qualify. He will review the document and let me know later today.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-16 12:15:16', '2025-12-16 12:15:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175892057', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175892049', 'Kurt Leinbach', NULL, '12-10-25 Kurt owns an escape room biz in Louisville! It''s near the thai place and Parma. He says it rated the best. I''ll have to check it out. He''s 59 and was referred by Deland Craven. He''s facing $1124.07 per month if he keeps his Kaiser CO Silver plan. It has a $3700 ded and $7000 mop. He watched the video and was very skeptical.  His only pre-x is a torn meniscus. He''s told it won''t heal on its own. It''s frayed with some fragments. He had a meniscus surgery a while back and his favorite dr. that he trusted was out of network. So, the cash price was $7K. He knows if he chooses to do that again it will be his cost. He wants to be able to run but every time he does he pays for it. He seemed to become more open minded as we talked. He doesn''t do the annual wellness screenings really ever. But, he feels like he "should" do a colonoscopy soon. So, I quoted him Secure HSA bc he didn''t want the cheapest plan and he was more interested in whole body care such as holistic and integrateive care. He didn''t know what that was until I explained it. Then it resonated with him. So, he gravitated towards Secure HSA with the higher IUA levels. He wanted $5000 IUA but he might choose $2500/$391. He will review the information I send. He''s been auto renewed in Kaiser. He knows he can cancel that any time and he has until Dec. 18th to chose MCS. He lives in Lafayette.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 20:31:04', '2025-12-10 20:34:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175892044', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175892039', 'Jennifer Kegel', NULL, '12-10-25 Jennifer came to me via Mary Ellen Francescani. She''s been researching health shares for 2-3 months. She''s a medical dr. herself. She''s a diganostic radiologist. However she''s on short-term disability and may get onto long-term disability. She could be covered until Oct. Then she might qualify for Cobra somehow. I thought she said she is 59 but I can''t find that in my notes. She''s facing $1200-$1300 ACA EO plan for 2026. She has a slew of medical conditions. She has significant arthritis in her neck. She''s had 5 surgical spine surgeries on T3-T1. She''s not foreseeing any neuro surgery. She developed some signficant neuropathic something and getting chelation procedure. She has severe osteoporosis. She has abarate esophagus and needs an endoscopy 1x per year. She had breast cancer and no longer has breasts. She had a knee replacement 11 years ago. Her daughter is a gyno so doesn''t need anything on that front. She''s now very open to functional medicine since that''s the only thing that''s helped her with all of her health issues now. She used  to practice acupuncture with her own LLC. She suffers from depression. Then she revealed she has an aneurysm. I finally broke it to her that this is WAY too risky even though she fully understood the pre-x limitations. She really wanted to save $900- $1000 per month.  Finally she revealed she has heavy metal toxic overload! I wonder if she''s exposed to the radiation as a radiologist. She said that was from too many MRIs for her neck and other issues. She''s also seeing a psychiatrist but can get it for $65 per session, which is the cheapest I''ve ever heard. She will look at Donald Kipps site as well to see if that will be helpful at all. She''ll keep my number in case she has questions.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 20:18:03', '2025-12-10 20:18:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175892034', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175939040', 'Oliver Molberg', NULL, '12-10-25 Oliver created his C4 account and selected me as his agent. We reviewed the plans for him at $50K for 2025. This gives him no APTC but does give the $80 CAP. So, for a decent plan the best one looks to be Anthem CO Option Gold Pathway Essentials for $344.37 his cost. He does mental health counseling 1x per week. He also takes sertaline. Generic drugs are $10 but he can get it on GoodRX for $2.  He will also review the MCS video since I can get his price down significantly and his income won''t matter. He hasn''t done a wellness visit but is interested in doing one. Otherwise Care+ is the way to go on that front. I learned he works for Kim Gangwish in her start up. But, it''s not going the way they hoped and there''s no work for him to proceed right now. So, he may need to find another job or create his own soon.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 20:01:40', '2025-12-10 20:01:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175939045', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175939040', 'Oliver Molberg', NULL, '12-10-25 Oliver doens''t know his income. He''s working for a start up but with no pay right now. I sent him instructions to set up C4 account and also to watch the MPB video to determine the best path for him. He''s turning 26 in Jan. and was sent to me by Kim  Gangwish.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 13:30:40', '2025-12-10 19:57:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747343', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175053148', 'Christian Pizzimenti', NULL, '12-9-25 Hi Wendy,<br>Reaching out to give you an update on our health benefits decision.<br>Meeting with you did help with understanding some of our options.  We did explore other local marketplace health insurance options with a broker.<br>We learned that the marketplace insurance option is the better financial choice for us in 2026.  Based on our usage and income, we qualify for options that are significantly lower.<br>Thank you for your help and we will keep you in mind if our needs change in the future.  If we could please cancel our meeting this Thursday.<br>Thanks, <br>Tara and Christian', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 23:25:22', '2025-12-09 23:25:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175412235', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175412230', 'David Hunt', NULL, '12-5-25 David lives in SE MI and came to me via Karen Torsoe when he was researching Zion and health sharing. Karen passed him over to me. He''s self-employed and semi-retired. He''s 60 and wife 61. He owns his own consulting biz. He''s healthy. They both had covid but he endured long covid. He found a dr. in AL that was finally able to treat him with alternative medicine since his reg drs. weren''t able to help him at all. He''s doing prefectly well now. This was back in 2023 or ''23. He can''t take meds for cholesterol bc he''s seriously allergic or reactive to the meds. Instead he maintains a strict diet. He wants me to inquire about a coronary calcium test he chose to do on his own, not for any reason other than knowledge. They found some calcium but he passed all stress tests! We discussed Secure HSA $774/$1250 or $646/$2500. He exercises daily.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-05 22:24:30', '2025-12-05 22:24:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175281227', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175281217', 'Jenny Brav', NULL, '12-4-25 Jenny has a rare and unique condition that Kaiser didn''t want to  even acknowledge exists. <span style="color:rgb(67, 79, 207);">Ehlers-Danlos syndromes</span><span style="color:rgb(70, 70, 73);"> (EDS) are a group of 13 heritable connective tissue disorders caused by genetic changes that affect connective tissue, leading to weakened skin, joints, blood vessels, and internal organs. I told her this will be deemed pre-existing. I read the genetic disorder section from the sharing guidelines. The only thing that has manifested is she dislocated one shoulder a few times now and I let her know that will certainly be deemed pre-x. She''s considering getting reg ins from Covered CA for one year during the initial $0 sharing for pre-x year one. Then she can graduate into $25K sharing and upward from there. She''s not concerned about costs exceeding those dollar amounts. Her cost on Covered CA are too expensive for her to afford without the APTC. She didn''t understand that the APTC she sees now is not going away, it''s only the extended tax credits that are ending. She''s paying $380 now and thought it was going up to $1340. She was paying $88, then $25 and now $380. So, she''s hopeful that she can pay both for one year since that''s still less than the $1300 she thought she was facing for a bad plan.  She has a dr. visit or two coming up. She''s like to make sure all of that checks out just fine before she makes any decisions. So, she might keep Covered CA for Jan. and then possibly join Secure HSA for Feb. 1st while also keeping Covered CA for 2026. She also knows of Radiology Assist which has worked well for her.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-04 22:50:07', '2025-12-04 22:50:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053153', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000175053148', 'Christian Pizzimenti', NULL, '12-2-25 Christian and Tara are both 42 and they have a 4 year old daughter. They were referred by Samantha Midler. They are healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco. Tara takes a birth control and they do their wellness screenings. They are self-employed. We found Dr. Jacqueline Fournier in Dripping Springs, TX showing up in the network. Secure HSA will be best and will be $1250/$819 or $2500/$679. Zip code is 78738 for Austin. Dentist is A Summer Smiles. They want 1Dental info and Secure HSA with a Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 20:29:11', '2025-12-02 20:29:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053087', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129840035', 'Wayne Harrick', NULL, '12-2-25 Wayne is strongly considering Secure HSA for Jan. 1st. He wants to make sure he doesn''t qualify for a reasonable APTC. He doesn''t think so but wants to make sure. I''m not sure which state he claims as his resident state. I''m guessing NM from his phone number, but not sure. He''ll keep me posted.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 14:28:10', '2025-12-02 14:28:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053052', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000129840035', 'Wayne Harrick', NULL, '12-2-25 Wayne is 41 now and solo. Self employed and in better health than before. No meds, no tobacco, no pre-x. He''s self employed. He does his wellness visits. The Secure HSA membership sounds like it fits his desires. ACA is looking like it will be $400-$500 in 2026. He wants to bring the price down. This will be $359/$1250. I need to mention $125/$25. He''s going to the gym now and I can call him between appts later today. He''ll watch the 9 minute video. He called me by accident last week and then realized he needs better options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 12:00:54', '2025-12-02 12:00:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174894021', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000174894016', 'Jim Harvey', NULL, '11-26-25 Jim came to me via Christine Harvey to help take care of his 22 year old daughter, Ashley who is in Spain now. She''ll be coming back to CO and trying to get her visa to go back to Spain in 2026 sometime. She''s healthy. She just graduated from CU in May and is an oper in Spain under the table. Jim got Ashley enrolled in Premium Care since that has the best intl benefits. Chose $1000/$249. Jim is also going to be in Spain for about 6 months but might like to explore Secure HSA for himself and wife Bobbi. He lives in Naples, FL. So, Premium Care isn''t an option. He''ll be going back and forth between CO and Spain in 2026. It''s good that he has ins over there since Secure HSA isn''t quite as comprehensive as Premium Care for intl. He is using Faye for his travel insurance and it''s also good for extreme sports protection alongside the travel insurance.  Looks like a good idea for some. They work with travel agents, not health ins agents though.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-30 19:37:49', '2025-11-30 19:51:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174894006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000174894001', 'William Sardinsky', NULL, '11-24-25 Will, 30 came referred by Mary Sundblom and lives in Carbondale, CO. He has various health issues that his ins and Medicaid is not paying for. He has lower back pain and uses alternative treatments. He had a herniated disc this past year. He understands that will be pre-x. He does rolphing, acu, chiro, PT and osteopathics, supplements and massage. He''s a self-employed photographer. He has had an APTC before. He''s expecting to earn above $62K for 2026. Sees a mental health therapist.He''s most interested in Care+. He doesn''t do wellness, no meds and no tobacco.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-30 19:24:45', '2025-11-30 19:24:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174464037', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000174464032', 'Sara Newman', NULL, '11-24-25 Sara is turning 33 this month. She''s waiting to see if it makes financial sense to be added to her boyfriend''s plan. He just bought more towards an S-Corp. So, they''re doing the math. She wants to most basic, affordable option CARE+ at $1250/$298 or $2500/$216. She''s healthy, no meds, no tobacco, does labs for wellness. She watched the video. She earns too much for an APTC. She''s leaving the country for a trip until Dec. 7th or 9th. She''ll probably deal with it at that point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-24 15:46:10', '2025-11-24 15:46:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174395048', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165741028', 'Steve Winter', NULL, '11-24-25 Steve called me back before I sent him my email response. I explained things to him again. He asked about his old helicopter crash accident from 1997 where he does have a handicap status bc he wears braces in his legs and has hardware in his back. He had an incomplete injury and came back from paralysis! He stabilized by 2000 and hasn''t had any changes since. But, he does have nerve damage in his legs creating leg weakness and has hardware in his back. His C4 plan is going from $800 to $1300 since he earns more than $68K. He does need a colonoscopy in 2026 since it''s been 5 years since his last one. He did the last one in GJ. He knows it would need to be somewhere other than CB to go in network. He''d be fine with all of that assuming his leg situation isn''t deemed pre-x.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-24 12:26:19', '2025-11-24 12:26:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239086', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000174239066', 'Tim Brown', NULL, '11-21-25 If they earn too much or choose MCS in the future they will contact me for sure. They appreciated learning from me that the APTC''s weren''t going away, only the extended covid relief money. They were stressing about it for months. They are super relieved and set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 20:19:06', '2025-11-21 20:19:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239081', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000174239066', 'Tim Brown', NULL, '11-21-25 Tim and Jennie expect to make about $92K in 2026 and fall within the threshold to get a massive APTC still. Their cost will be about $63 if they keep their plan.  This is their information and I recommended they stay with C4 and they already have a broker they are working with. They were very upfront and great people.<br><span><br></span>I''m Tim Brown, Jennie Graz''s husband.  Maria Hennessey referred Jennie to you and you two have been in communication via her work email.  I''ve cc''d her on her personal address above and we should use that moving forward.<br><br>We''d love to meet with you to discuss healthcare options.  Your email to Jennie mentioned that you would tentatively book her at 2 on Thursday.  That will work for one of us, but we would prefer to meet with you together if possible.  <b>Please let us know if you have another time available this week.  Otherwise, we''d like to confirm 11/20 @ 2.  </b><br><br>We have used a local broker in Gunnison to purchase insurance through the marketplace for the past several years, but he has retired and someone else in his office is handling our account now.  We contribute the maximum amount to our HSA each year ($8,300 in 2024) and we''ve been going with the Rocky Mountain HMO plan <b>RMHP Valley Bronze Value HSA </b>(No Referrals).  We received a quote from RMHP/Connect for Health dated 10/29/25 with an <b>estimated monthly premium of $61.63 for 2026</b>. <br><br>Current monthly costs for 2025:<br>Monthly Premium: $2,113.36<br>Tax Credits: -2,108.84<br>Total monthly payment: $4.52<br><br>Estimated monthly costs for 2026:<br>Monthly premium:  $2,959.48<br>tax credits:  $2,730.85<br>Colorado Premium Assistance: -167.00<br>Total monthly payment:  $61.63<br><br>Our birth dates (family of 4):<br>Tim  3/25/1974 (age 51)<br>Jennifer:  12/23/1974 (age 50, 51 before Jan 1, 2026)<br>Josephine:  5/29/2013 (age 12)<br>Sebastian:  6/19/2016 (age 9)<br><br>I don''t have the updated income level we claimed through the marketplace application, but I think it is $90k MAGI.  Our 2023 tax return AGI was $86,609 and our 2024 tax return AGI was $92,093.  We expect to be in that same range for 2026.<br><br>We very rarely use our insurance and we are quite happy with the low premiums we have been paying despite the high deductibles.  We also like the HSA-compatible plan since contributing to the HSA reduces our taxable income, keeps us in a lower tax bracket, and gives us quick, tax-free access to cash for previous medical receipts we''ve accrued.<br><br>Your email to Jennie that "only the extended covid relief subsidies are not getting extended" brought our attention to a potential misunderstanding that we had about the tax credits.  We were under the impression that they were all going away except for the (new?) Colorado Premium Assistance amount unless Congress decides to extend them.  Did we misunderstand this?  If so, the quote above could be very reasonable.  Without them, it would crush us.  <br><br>Do you have additional options on the marketplace that we not have seen?<br><br>Do you know of other options such as a healthshare that might be appropriate for us?  If so, we are interested in hearing about costs, pros and cons of these.  <br><span><br></span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 20:17:52', '2025-11-21 20:17:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174142089', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000152284694', 'Shannon Lamb', NULL, '11-20-25 Shannon removed me as her Agent. Havent heard anything from her. She received my email about open enrollment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-20 19:57:18', '2025-11-20 19:57:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974194', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173974189', 'Luke McConnell', NULL, '11-10-25 Luke is 44, criminal defense and civil rights lawyer living in Lakewood, CO. He came to me via a friend and I need to find out who. He''s self-employed with his own firm. He''s had Kaiser for 18 years and likes it but it''s getting too expensive at $480 in 2026. He watched the video and understands the IUA and pre-x. He''s interested in Secure HSA and wants to know what''s included in the wellness. He''s not all that interested in the HSA but might be as he learns more. His only pre-x is some dermatology issue he didn''t want to share. He understands how it works and I told him to get his records if he''s concerned. Sounds like he''s not on a medication for it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 22:35:06', '2025-11-19 22:35:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974129', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173974112', 'Melinda Baum', NULL, '11-19-25 Melinda is 61 and was referred by Willa Bonzi. She watched the video. She has an LLC and gets paid via a 1099. She does her annual wellness screenings. She''s also a retired teacher and is reviewing her PARA options and wants an HSA. Sounds like PARA is $700+. She gets Comfort Dental already and is fine with that. She newly has tinnitus that she''s trying to get help with. She was a music teacher, so it''s a real problem for her. She also wants to go to a chiro. I suggested she asks about the tinnitus to see if that can help. She will do so. She''s been paying $500. Her new RMHP for 2026 will be $1700!  We discussed Secure HSA $1250/$448 or $2500/$391 and $125/$25.  She will keep me posted on her decision.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 21:41:29', '2025-11-19 21:41:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173933048', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173933043', 'Nicole Morris', NULL, '11-18-25 Nicole is 42, self-employed, no longer qualifies for Medicaid. She''s expecting to earn about $50K. She says C4 is so expensive. She''s pretty healthy, no meds, does wellness visits, pap screening. She goes to a local clinic to get that done and it''s super affordable. She really just wants a catastrophic option. We discussed Care+ and C4 plan comparison. At $50K her APTC is $191.25.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-18 20:08:03', '2025-11-18 20:10:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173915011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173915006', 'Jane Tornatore', NULL, '11-18-25 Jane lives in WA state. Grrr..... She came to me via Summer Deaton. She is eyes wide open about our Western Medicine world. She got cancer last year and treated it metabolically and isn''t worried about it coming back. If it does she will pay for it on her own using alternative medicine, not chemo or any of the toxic ways that are normal. I will pass her off to Karen, so she can join the co-op for this year. She really just wants it for if she gets in an accident and breaks a bone or something. Her plan will be $1000 per month if she goes onto their exchange. She''s done with it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-18 09:20:09', '2025-11-18 09:20:09'),
