  ('zcrm_1579374000173343132', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173343127', 'Laud Vidal', NULL, '11-11-25 Laud is 27 and lives in Philly and works for Finray Solar. His only pre-x is mental health. He take olanzapine 15mg which is an anti-psychotic drug but looks to be affordable still. He''s leaning towards a Jan. 1st start date. Care+ was more appealing at the lower rate. It would be $268/$1250 with Darrel Porter paying $100 towards his plan making it $168 per month for his cost. I explained the virtual mental health in great detail with the $0 mental health counselors per their discretion on visit numbers and the option to upgrade to PHD level for $205 intake and $100 per session. He sounded amenable to this and fine with the virtual aspect. He knows the deadline and will keep me posted. He doesn''t have ins right now but is leaning towards Jan. 1st, 2026 start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-11 21:34:35', '2025-11-11 21:34:35'),
