  ('zcrm_1579374000173241031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173241026', 'Jason Hernstad', NULL, '11-7-25 Jason was referred to me by Mara Simoneau. He works on unincorporated non-profit organizations. UNA takes about 4-6 weeks to set up and 12 months of support but crazy expensive! He''s interested in MCS and possibly Care+. He''s 38 and lives in Boulder. Works with private banking that needs a min balance of $50K! Once over $500K $ earns 8% based in Dominica. Yikes! Anyhow, he''s interested to learn about MCS, healthy, no tobacco, no pre-x.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-08 10:56:19', '2025-11-08 10:56:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173241021', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173241004', 'Loralee Kuntz', NULL, '11-7-25 Loralee is 50 and referred by Elena Bensenoff. No pre-x, no tobacco, takes compunded progesterone. Self-employed. Lives near St. Pete''s or Tampa, FL. She prefers thermography. Works in the healthcare field. She''s interested in Care+ since she won''t use most of the other wellness benefits and doesn''t want or need a colonoscopy any time soon.  Care+ $1250/$381 and $125/$25. Can''t do Premium Care bc in FL.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-08 10:48:33', '2025-11-08 10:48:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079394', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173079389', 'Jessica Martinez', NULL, '11-6-25 Jessica is 39 and Taylor is 36. They were referred to me by Nicole Baker. They are losing their employer benefits soon. They are both in the healthcare world as an PA and NP with PRN roles. She thinks they are both W2 employees even when she drops down to less time.She has a thyroid problem and take NP Thyroid 60 mg and 15 mg. She takes med for insomnia sometimes and has minor exercise induced asthma. Her husband Taylor is healthy, no tobacco, no meds. She needs wellness visits for her thyroid meds to be refilled. She might be able to take care of that via the virtual healthcare app but I''m not certain. We discussed Care+ since can''t qualify for Secure HSA. I shared with math with her to help her see that Secure HSA will be more expensive then just paying for her mammogram on her own. She looked at <a style="display:inline;" target="_blank" href="http://weshare.org/"><u>WeShare.org</u></a> also. I''m not sure about that one.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:54:47', '2025-11-06 22:54:47'),
