  ('zcrm_1579374000173079149', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000173079144', 'Gail Longenecker', NULL, '11-6-25 Gail is a long time referral partner. She''s now doing full service for all insurance types! So, I can refer to her for anything I don''t already refer to Steve Hakes. She is an excellent resource. She was thinking of learning about MCS but realizes it''s too complicated to add to her list at the moment before open enrollment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 20:58:36', '2025-11-06 20:58:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172953042', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000172566034', 'Jennifer Rose', NULL, '<span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">I appreciate you taking the time to speak with me last week at such short notice. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">My partner and I reviewed the plans that their work offered and compared it to the Care+, and we have decided to go with me being on their plan for now.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Things may change in the future, and if it does, I will reach out. I do appreciate this as an option, and appreciate your time.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Thank you,</span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Jen Rose</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-04 22:42:46', '2025-11-04 22:42:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172566039', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000172566034', 'Jennifer Rose', NULL, '10-29-25 Jen talked with me about a year ago. She came to me via Mary Ellen Francescani with Middleway Wellness. She''s 48 and her DOB is in June. Lives in PA. She has her own LLC and is self-employed. Her employer coverage is $350 for her cost with a PPO and it will be going up to $360 with a high ded. She''s considering Care+ $2500/$216. She''s healthy, no pre-x, no meds. She never even used her ins last year at all. She only used Middleway for her wellness visits. She gets supplements as well. She''s looking at Jan. 1st start date. I''ll send her written overview.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-29 15:55:25', '2025-10-29 15:55:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172330009', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000172330004', 'Alexandra Sawyer', NULL, '10-24-25 Alexandra goes by Zan and is 56. Husband Dan is 59 turning 60 very soon. They were referred by Christine Harvey. Dan recently sold his business but it will go through in Jan. 2026. They are looking for a Jan. 1st start date most likely. They live on Juniper Ave in Boulder. They are both healthy. Zan is on 2 meds for her thyroid and 2 for her hormones. Dan is on 1/2 of pill for anti-depressant (I think). They are both self-employed. Zan has been a contractor for 25 years. We discussed Premium HSA and Secure HSA. We focused on Secure HSA in case there are caps on sharing for Premium HSA. The price is nearly identical. We discussed the nuances of a colonoscopy for preventive vs diagnostic. We checked to see if BCHand BMC takes Multi-Plan/PHCS. Looks like yes but I told them to check with their doctor to be certain. Zan loves full scripts but it sounds like she already gets it wholesale price or better than 30% discounts. They also have a 22 year old daughter who might be well served to join their family membership. She has mild autism and that''s it. They were reviewing the 2025 prices and I''m not sure if I gave them 2026 prices because they were asking questions and I forgot.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-24 21:10:49', '2025-10-24 21:15:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172038006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000172038001', 'Patrick Dee', NULL, '10-17-25 Patrick is 57 and lives in PA. He''s self-employed. He''s owns rental properties and has investment income. He has an LLC with an EIN. He wants access to annual wellness screenings including colonoscopy. He had kidney stones but in 2021. So, no longer relevant. The only new problem he''s working to resolve is tingling in his fingers. He''s working with his PCP to see what''s going on for that. Once he knows then he can make a decision about joining or not. He used to have Medishare with a $10K AUA. Then he switched to First Health Network which he says is garbage ins. He did blood work and they just helped him get 25%-30% discount which he felt he could have done on his own. They don''t cover any wellness visit, labs or anything. He also has slightly elevated cholesterol and blood pressure well managed. I read the exemption clause in Guidelines for Secure HSA. He''ll sort out his current concerns and let me know if/when he''s ready to join. I gave him both 2025 and 2026 pricing. He might choose the $2500 IUA level.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-17 10:08:19', '2025-10-17 10:08:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171948066', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000171948061', 'Courtney Fields', NULL, '10-16-25 Courtney lives in Austin, TX and came to me via Samantha Midler.She''s looking at this for her and possibly for her employees. She''s a hari stylist and doesn''t currently offer benefits but is open to offering something. Their ins is really expensive right now and will be going up. She''s 33 and husband is 36. They are both super healthy, no meds, no tobacco. Her employees are W2. She has 4 employees. 2 are all set with spouse and parents. 2 might need help. 1 is 32 and the other is 26. She''s looking for Spring <span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">2026</span> most likely. I quoted her Care+ and Secure HSA and need to send them both via email.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-16 17:49:54', '2025-10-16 17:49:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171948051', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000171948046', 'Kelly Larson', NULL, '9-25-25 Kelly came to me via Mara Simoneau. She''s 47 and her son is 4. Her company is based in CA. She might live in Iowa, CO, but I''m not sure if that''s connected to the client above her in my notes. She needs it to be compliant in CA. She had a heath share years ago and then went onto Medicaid. She no longer qualifies for Medicaid and now has Anthem with her son. She pays $126 per paycheck and company pays $379 per paycheck. However, the total cost she believes is around $900 mo.  Yes, she wants to do wellness visits. She must choose Secure HSA for CA, $1000/$578. She has perimenopause and does her pap screenings 2-3 x per year. Only med is acyclovir on occasion for cold sores. She wants proof that she will not be penalized for non-compliance in CA. Reba will send a note stating that she will receive the 1095-C form for tax filing in 2026 for 2025.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-16 16:19:13', '2025-10-16 16:19:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171948031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000171948026', 'Kim Dilling', NULL, '10-15-25 Kim watched the video. She came to me via Suzy Martinek. She won''t need benefits until spring of 2026, perhaps around May. She''s 59 and very confused as to how this works. I helped her understand. She has asthma and allergies but otherwise healthy. She went to ER for asthma a long time ago and not since. She will be working winters and not summers now. She does the annual wellness screenings. She wants to speak further in Nov. when she has more time. We only had 5 min. today.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-15 22:21:39', '2025-10-15 22:21:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171948021', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000171948016', 'Bill Schmid', NULL, '10-14-25 Bill is with WWSRA and lives in CA with his wife. His wife had cancer 8 years ago and it''s been well managed ever since. However, she takes medication to manage it. So, I don''t recommend MCS at this time. He and their 16 yr old daughter could join and wife could go onto ACA. But, she''s ending her job and benefits Nov. 1st. That will bring their income down to $80K-$100K which means they might get a significant APTC witH Covered CA. We don''t know the prices and how that will shake out. Bill has an S-Corp. They can join Secure HSA to remain compliant in CA. Also, his wife is used to having a high paying position with group benefits. But, she may choose to go out on her own and consult. But it''s TBD.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-15 22:15:05', '2025-10-15 22:15:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171391192', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170389022', 'Alison Huskie', NULL, '10-1-25 Alison sent an email asking me to call her. I just left her a vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-01 16:16:52', '2025-10-01 16:16:52'),
