  ('zcrm_1579374000170990016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170990011', 'Brian Anthony', NULL, '9-19-25 Brian is 50 and his wife is 53. He''s a WWSRA member and was sent by Rachel Holden. He works in the Pacific NW and lives in OR. He''s hitting his big travel season now. He''s been on the ACA the last 4-5 years and is planning ahead. He and his wife are healthy. No pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. He''s not sure if his wife does a mammo. He doesn''t think so. He does the colonoscopy. I described Premium Care $1000/$603, $1500/$532 and Premium HSA $1000/$720, $1500/$655 with $125/$25 and $100 waived as WWSRA member. He will review it with his wife but will get back to me once they are able to talk about it. It''s tough for him this time of year to focus on this stuff.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-19 11:33:54', '2025-09-19 11:33:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170863031', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '9-17-25 Genevieve asked a few more questions and shared they will remain on their ins plan until Feb. 1st, 2026. We will meet on Jan.2nd at 3:00 to discuss C4 Ins for William and MCS for Genevieve and the kids. They will do all of their wellness visits now and anything else they need. They''ve maxed out their MOP for 2025. So, it''s best to stay put until their renewal Feb. 1st. William is afraid their plan is not as good as his but she''s been explaining how it works and why it should be good for them.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-17 15:30:47', '2025-09-17 15:30:47'),
