  ('zcrm_1579374000170661063', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170661058', 'Katelyn Cooper', NULL, '9-12-25 Katelyn has been very flexible with the changes in schedule due to Venteur/Sabrina being very difficult to work with this far. We have an extension and an on-boarding meeting on Monday, Sept. 15th for Jennifer, Katelyn and Ashley Coburn. Working towards an Oct. 1st effective date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-12 15:13:58', '2025-09-12 15:13:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170642003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000134214005', 'William Choi', NULL, '9-10-25 After a long conversation with Genevieve, she thinking of doing Premium HSA for her and kids who are 21, 22 and 23. Their 26 year old is on his own now. Premium HSA is $1000/$676. Genevieve only has high blood pressure medication nebivolol. She gets is from GoodRX but can get it from pharmacy checker for even cheaper. She can get 30 tablets for $10.80 as of today when sort by price. Wiliam takes too many meds for MCS to be  a good idea. His meds are <span style="">Repatha 140 mg, Jardiance 25 mg, Rosuvastatin 20 mg and Mounjaro 5 mg. Willing to take generic versions. They get them every 90 days and 4 x year refills. Daughter Olivia has IBS problems and takes Ibsrela. I found Ibsrela for about $92 a month which she''s fine with. I gave her Pharmacy Checker to see and order on her own. We will wait for Nov. to see the prices and options for William. The best carrier now is RMHP/UHC to include all of his meds. It does not include his Dr. but she says that''s ok. Their Cobra runs out Feb. 1st. They are paying about $2500 per month. She could move off now and save them probably $1000 per month. Her 23 year old daughter has some digestion issues.  I''ll share the video and she will talk it over with William. They earn about $1M per year, so they won''t qualify for any APTC. She''s super nice and thankful for my patience.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-10 14:21:10', '2025-09-10 14:21:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170541006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170541001', 'Stephanie Bertz', NULL, '9-8-25 Stephanie is 30 and engaged to her fiance who is 33. She''s exploring using Middleway Wellness for screenings such as pap screening and primary care. She takes meds for depression/anxiety and PTSD. She believes she can get her meds affodably on her own and pay for therapy herself as well. She''s more concerned about major hospitalization type scenarios. Fiance had a traumatic brain injury at some point so he gets migraines. He''s going to the PCP next week to make sure everything checks out ok. That will determine if this is a good idea or not. Middleway can help him with the migraines, etc. according to Stephanie. Her fiance recently lost his job but will have his ins until the end of Sept. Care+ is the best choice for them to pair with Middleway since they don''t need the high cost wellness items and don''t care about the HSA. She''s also wanting to start a family in about 2 years, no sooner than Dec. of 2026. So, she''s fine with the 6 month waiting period. Her current deductible is $7K which is terrible. She uses Care Credit with gives her time to pay off medical bills with no interest accruing. She pays the full amount to the dr. or hospital and then pays of the bill to Care Credit over the course of time, like  acc but w/o the interest.  She really likes the idea of health sharing because it actually helps other people in their time of need. She works in the healthcare realm or managing benefits, so she understands how it works... or doesn''t work.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-08 11:32:37', '2025-09-08 11:32:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170458050', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000169948001', 'Tiffany Exstrom', NULL, '9-4-25 Now she''s saying they don''t need MCS until Nov. 1st bc current insurance runs through end of Oct. They are most available Monday and Friday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-04 16:35:30', '2025-09-04 16:35:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170389042', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170389037', 'Stephen Nilsen', NULL, '9-3-25 Stephen just turned 56 and his girlfriend is 50.  They live in Evergreen and travel a lot. Stephen came to me via Patty Nilsen. They are not married anymore but they have two twins who are going to Pepperdyne that we tried to get approved for ins for school but failed to do so. Stephen had a full knee replacement in May or 2023 or 2022. He can''t remember but says is great and he''s had no problems at all! He''s in MN right now and will be back in CO soon. He just lost his brand new job at a start up unexpectedly. They lost their funding or didn''t get the funding they expected. He''s never been at a job for less than 5 years. But, he''s used to making $270K or so and now it''s $0. So, he''s looking to do consulting work if he can''t find a FT job with benefits. He already has his own LLC for his self-employment. He''s used to having the best and most comprehensive plans through work His dad used to work on the hospital system and started to how how terrible the system was. He also encourage Stephen to never go without ins.   They are both healthy. No pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. His GF does have celiac disease but she just has to be careful what she cooks and eats. He wants the best, most comprehensive membership which is Premium HSA for his age. $1000/$363 or $720 if considered domestic partners. He also wants dental and vision. He wants to keep Dr. Jeffrey Sorensen <span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 42);">at Evergreen Internal And Family Medicine At Arapahoe Peak. The multiplan site isn''t working and the dr. practice doesn''t seem to have a website to search for who they accept. He will call and ask them.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-03 15:45:06', '2025-09-03 15:45:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170389027', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170389022', 'Alison Huskie', NULL, '9-3-25 Alison watched the video minus the last minute. She''s turning 61 soon. She''s a retired school teacher and gets PARA now. She''s also working as W2 for a non-profit org. She''s paying around $500-$600 per month. She gets her mental health counseling for $40 co-pay and goes 2x per month. She will find out the cash pay rate for Catherine Anderson. She is 8-9 years cancer free from leukemia. She gets some blood tests every 6 months to make sure all is well. She gets the BCR ABL1 from Quest which shows up as $287.97 in Montrose and CBC is $6 and CMP is $7. She would have to pay cash for her pap screening. Premium Care $1000/$299 or $1500/$267 is best option with her retirement and W2 status. She will get some more information for us to determine if it makes sense or not.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-03 12:55:45', '2025-09-03 12:55:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170327011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000170327006', 'Adair Taylor', NULL, '8-2-25 Adair is 63 and watched the video. She likes some alternative care. She has bone spurs in her knees and needs to decide if she will has surgery on one now and the other once on Medicare. She''s not sure what''s involved and she will find out what it will cost with her ins now vs if pays the cash price w/o ins. Her ins is about $600+ with a $200+ APTC. It has  a$6K ded, then 80/20. MOP is $12K in-network and $16K out of network for Individual / $32K for family. Yikes! She''s having a finger surgery tomorrow for the contraction of the tendon that makes her finger curl on its own. Then she will need hand therapy for a month. She understands the pre-x clause which is why she will do her due diligence first and call me back after she has some answers. She also has fair skin and had melanoma and basal cells removed last year. She sees the derm for skin check 2-3x per year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-02 12:42:03', '2025-09-02 12:42:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948588', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000169732011', 'Jeffrey Cohen', NULL, '8-20-25 Jeffrey is very interested but also nervous because of his type 2 diabetes. He can get the meds and insulin cheap enough.He''s just concerned about if something more serious goes wrong. He will call his endocrinologist to see what serious ailments could come from this. I let him know I''d inquire with 2 doctor groups as well and see what they say. He is VERY nice and appreciative of my help and honest opinion. He''s from GA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 13:29:38', '2025-08-20 13:29:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948009', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000169948001', 'Tiffany Exstrom', NULL, '8-19-25 Tiffany is 52 and Dudley is 61 and live in Golden. They were referred to me by Ben DiSalle who is not a member. They have a sole proprietorship and LLC but mostly retired otherwise. Cobra with Cigna will be $1560 which includes dental and vision. They both see eye doctors. Dudley has seen his eye Dr. for 50 years but nothing to worry about. Tiffany gets eye injections for $170 for each injection every 3 months. Her ins wasn''t covering it. They take some supplements and can make use of the 30% discounts. Tiffany take alopurinol which is affordable. I priced it out as well as estradiol and progesterone. Only one was significant cost of $55 per month but I only checked goodrx. She can probably get it cheaper with Concierge support of the drug list through the  MEC.  They want an Oct. 1st start date. They will call their doctors and find out the cash price discount per visit. <br>As for a dentist, they go to the CO Dental Spa with two brothers. I can''t find any network or insurance that they bill. Dudley will find out. I sent them VSP to review as well. We will revisit it all on Sept. 3rd at 10:00.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-19 14:26:03', '2025-08-19 14:26:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169732016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000169732011', 'Jeffrey Cohen', NULL, '8-15-25 Jeffrey Cohen was referred by Florie and Dan Glusman. Jeffrey is 59 and engaged to a woman who is 52 and in Mexico. They spend a good amount of time in Mexico City.  Premium Care will be best since it''s the most inclusive for international care and the pre-x clause is better moving forward bc he has insulin dependent diabetes. He takes several meds of which he gave me most names and I looked up on Pharmacy Checker. They were probably no more than $200 plus $100 for insulin totaling $300 plus $299/$1000 = around $600 per month instead of $1000 per month with his current ins plan with an $8K ded. He''s been having to come back to the US to get his meds which has been a burden. He''s willing to buy his c-pap machine and diabetes supplies as self pay. He''s been paying about $25K per year for his insurance, meds and accessories! He''s going to read the sharing guidelines and make sure he''s 100% comfortable.  His meds are <span style="color:rgb(45, 45, 45);">Omeprazole </span>, rosuvastatin, topimerate, <span style="color:rgb(45, 45, 45);">olmesartan-hydrochlorothiazide and 1 he already knows the price and didn''t share with me. Some or most can be shipped worldwide and one needs to be in person for best price. He also sees a retinologist bc he had diabetic retinopathy and just has regular check-ups 1x per year. He will pay the cash price for those. He had his screening colonoscopy in Dec. 2024 and had no problems. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(45, 45, 45);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(45, 45, 45);">He''s VERY interested in doing what I do, educating people about these memberships. He works in the garbage/recycling industry. He''s also a singer. He sang outside Andrea Bocelli''s home and was invited in and now gets lifetime free tix to his concerts bc Andrea likes his voice so much!!!</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-15 14:15:21', '2025-08-15 14:16:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169732006', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000169732001', 'James Saunders', NULL, '8-5-25 James is working with Finray Solar and wants a Sept. 1st start date. He watched the video and said it is incredibly informative. He totally understands how and why it all works. He is 33, wife is 31 and all girls 7, 5 and 13 months.  He lives in MA so they need the MEC. Secure HSA is by far the best price at $780 at $1000 IUA. That''s the one he wants. The only thing that happened in the past 2 years was that he had a grade 4 laceration of his spleen while playing duck, duck, goose with his kids and he slipped on a rock and hit it just at the wrong spot. He got a life flight to the hospital, lost 3/4 of blood. He was monitored for a while with his blood and hasn''t had any problems whatsoever since. He got a clean bill of health and absolutely no issues. He''s all set as well as his family. He''s ready to enroll on Monday. I just need to ask Darrell Porter about payment, since I forget. James will have all kids SS ready and his wife will be available when we do the enrollment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-15 11:50:59', '2025-08-15 11:50:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169447040', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000144114236', 'Sara Cadwell', NULL, '8-11-25 Sara removed me as her broker and won''t speak with me. Mike tried to give her my call and she wouldn''t take it. So, who knows what''s up with her. Nothing I can do.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-11 16:22:14', '2025-08-11 16:22:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169006143', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000168965031', 'Chris Sullivan', NULL, '7-31-25 Left vm for Chris at our scheduled time to talk to help them enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-31 14:34:43', '2025-07-31 14:34:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168965036', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000168965031', 'Chris Sullivan', NULL, '7-30-25  Chris 50 and Katie 54 have 3 kids 21, 19, 17. The youngest needs ins for football soon but might be able to get something through the school. They missed their SEP bc he lost his ins May 31st. Cobra was going to be $2500 so they opted out. He''s most interested and excited for Premium HSA. They have two EIN''s for two different businesses/non-profits. Chris is looking for new employment but really likes what I explained re Premium HSA.Katie had a hip surgery about 2 1/2 years ago and no further problems. Chris had a deviated septum surgery w/in the last 36 months and no further issues. They both have hypothyroid and take levothyroxine and lyothyronine (sp?). I explained the pre-x clause to them and they understand. They are also psyched to fund a HSA which they''ve never been able to do so before. They were referred by Dave Loomis who learned of this through his brother in law. I don''t know who that is. Chris tried to connect with me perhaps twice through the Naturally Inspired link I have and it didn''t work! I''m working to get that resolved. Chris and Katie scheduled to meet again tomorrow to complete the enrollment for Sept. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-30 16:27:36', '2025-07-30 16:27:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168715066', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000158933001', 'Cheryl Branson', NULL, '7-24-25 Cheryl removed me as her agent on C4 today. I just left her a vm to see if she needs help still.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-24 17:29:07', '2025-07-24 17:29:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168591034', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000164437143', 'Ximena Lizama', NULL, '7-22-25 Ximena opted out of all THIA benefits. She is getting them through her husband or other means. She already has life ins and doesn''t want the dental discount plan that includes vision either. So, nothing for her at this time.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-22 12:29:32', '2025-07-22 12:29:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168298157', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000167659045', 'Iris Gartner', NULL, '7-17-25 Iris has a few potential jobs that offer benefits. So, she wants to hold off until that all plays out. She''s all set for now! Very appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-17 10:05:30', '2025-07-17 10:05:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000167659067', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000167357054', 'Andrew Pemberton', NULL, '7-2-25 I left him a vm now in case I didn''t previously. He came to me via Cory Nickerson.  It looks like I answered his first call but I don''t have any notes...', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-02 16:13:49', '2025-07-02 16:13:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000167659062', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000167357054', 'Andrew Pemberton', NULL, '6-26-25 I believe I left him a vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-02 16:13:07', '2025-07-02 16:13:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000167659050', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000167659045', 'Iris Gartner', NULL, '7-2-25 Iris came to me via Amy Walker. Iris is 24 and just moved here from NY. She''s looking for a job right now. She might get a job at the Botanical Gardens but they don''t offer benefits since it''s seasonal and PT.  She thinks she wants to see a PT and endocrinologist. So, C4 will be best for now. We are talking in 2 weeks when her work situation may be sorted out.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-02 11:12:29', '2025-07-02 11:12:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166637159', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000158933001', 'Cheryl Branson', NULL, '6-16-25 It looks like her income will be $20K. So, I believe she qualified for Medicaid. But, system is showing $1000+ APTC and wanting more verification info. But, she should be on Medicaid and therefore nothing to do with C4.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-06-16 13:16:22', '2025-06-16 13:16:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166475041', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000166475033', 'Francini Eufemia', NULL, '6-10-25 Francini is 62 and is retiring from BVSD in July. Her husband is turning 63 in a week. He''s on Cobra for $900 right now but he uses tobacco. He''s not a good candidate. Francini agrees. She was referred by Tracy Dunnuck who gave her my information but Tracy hasn''t enrolled and I don''t think I''ve talk with her yet. She knows Stephanie Watson as a parent of one of kids also and knows she has a membership but isn''t the one to connect us. Francini had a good understanding of MCS just from talking with so many different people she knows. She''s super healthy, no pre-x other than takes Crestor bc of family history of high cholesterol. She gets her annual wellness screenings. Premium HSA is the best fit for wellness and her age. I quoted $363/$1000, $1500/$336 plus $125/$25. She doesn''t take supplements so that''s not really a benefit. She wants an Aug. 1st start date and will call me when she''s ready.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-06-10 18:23:22', '2025-06-10 18:23:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165907014', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000165907001', 'Christian Childs', NULL, '5-29-25 For meds - We usually can source Mounjaro, Wegovy and Ozempic, however there is fear that the Canadian Postal workers are about to go on strike, so our Canadian pharmacies are not shipping to the US until this strike stuff is over. We can currently source the Nurtec though.I have both prices below.
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000143225003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131707093', 'Isaiah Taylor', NULL, '7-17-24 Tim Taylor and wife Jane Taylor called inquiring for their son, Isaiah 28 and his wife Mady Taylor who is turning 26 in Aug. 2024. Tim is an ASHI member and plans to pay for their membership from his business. Isaiah works for Tim.  Isaiah currently has Solidarity for $225 a month with a $6K "deductible." Jane isn''t sure if they do their wellness visits. She doesn''t believe he has any pre-x and doesn''t know about Mady. They don''t use tobacco. CARE+ is best due to age and not needing most of the ACA wellness visits.  They might be interested in HAB but doesn''t sound like it will benefit them enough.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-17 16:26:55', '2024-07-17 16:26:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141297023', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000141306001', 'Bonny Roberts', NULL, '6-18-24 Bonny and Neal found me on C4 site!  They''ve been back in CO for 14 years and their kids are now 18 and 20. OMG! Bonny is looking for a new job and Neal is still working as self-employed. They moved back and live in Superior. They stopped playing soccer 5-6 years ago. Bonny kept trying to play but she kept injuring her back. They do their wellness visits, dental cleaning, Skin checks, vision screenings, gym, possible nutrition, and yes for mental health, especially for Zoe. She deals with anxiety, depression, ADHD type of stuff and takes some meds.  I explained the pre-x clause is for 36 months. Other than the mental health they don''t have any pre-x other than son getting some moles removed now. They are best served by Premium Care and HAB. I quoted $1000, $1500 and $2500 IUA''s and $250 HAB. She wasn''t sure which IUA she wanted yet. She will discuss it with Neal and we set a time on Thursday at 11:00 to enroll for July 1st start date bc her ins end June 30th.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-18 13:45:43', '2024-06-18 13:45:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141214003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000131407031', 'Haley White', NULL, '6-17-24 Haley should have had her baby in early June. I just left her a vm for our appt now. She probably forgot about it. Hopefully she''ll call back when she''s free.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-17 11:04:18', '2024-06-17 11:04:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000140546170', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000140470156', 'Krystle Mulnix', NULL, '6-10-24 I sent this to her regarding the list of meds she can use.
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000092438029', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000092487001', 'Noreen Johnson', NULL, '5-5-22 Noreen is a member at Dr. Drostan Baker''s DPC. She''s 61 and has no other ins at the moment and realizes it would be a good idea. She lives in Liberty Lake, WA, so membership is not available at this moment as Zion works through the gov regs to get approval. She''s willing to wait. I asked her to put on her calendar to call me in July and she will. I will also try to remember if we get the thumbs up sooner. But, Zion said it will likely be a few more months. She will need the DIRECT membership since she has a DPC. I have NOT talked through everything with her yet or ask about pre-x or employment status, etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-05-05 11:44:12', '2022-05-05 11:45:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091633013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000091642011', 'Charity Roberts', NULL, '4-25-22 Charity is turning 46 on 8/5/1976. She''s super healthy, massage therapist, active, etc. But, she did have  a knee replacement in Dec (or Sept 2021). Not sure I heard her correctly. But, it''s super strong now she says and she''s aware of the pre-x clause related to that. She also takes meds for her face (I assume she means skin) Spironolactone for about $17 and Adderrall for ADHD which is showing at $13-$20.  She''s self-employed and does her wellness visits. I also explained the her annual skin check is not part of ACA compliant annual wellness, so she will pay that cash on her own without reimbursement. Both of her drs. are in PHCS network, Dr. Whitney Kennedy (she sees the PA under Dr. Whitney) and Dr. Cristee Offerdahl. I still told her to double check by showing card with network before she goes and pulling card if needs to see dr. beyond the wellness visit at a later date. She understands. She''s also interested in HMA for IUA, dental and meds. Plus wants VSP for next eye visit, but may wait until she''s close to needing it which could be in about year or less.  SECURE $300/$1000 for June 1st. She had a divorce finalized on April 15th and she''s hoping she can stay on x-husband''s plan for May since she missed the deadline for May 1st start date. So, looking to June 1st start date and will check on Cobra for May if necessary.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-25 15:46:00', '2022-04-25 15:47:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091200016', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000091124115', 'Rebecca Webster', NULL, '4-20-22 Becky is Mike McGimpsey''s sister. She''s turning 60 soon and has a number of health issues, primarily with back issues. She gets injections about every 3 months. Her discs are going bad. She takes gabapentin, motrin for pain and sdhe has a thyroid issue too. Her BMI is not ideal either she said. Also has some ankle issues that she''s getting cortisone shots for now. Likely this will Not work for her. But, I asked her to find out the cost of her injections and the name of it. The more she talked, the more health issues she mentioned. She says the ACA is about $800 a month for something or $0 for basically no coverage with the worst plans. I thought maybe a DPC could help her but sounds like she needs a specialist called an IR (Interventional Radiologist) to do the injections.  There are 3 DPC''s in Prescott, AZ and closest one is a Dr. Nancy Blum, DO. But again, likely she needs to stay on ACA with all of her health issues that have cropped up. She even mentioned she walks around with a walker now and things are getting worse. I told her it''s a small chance I can help her. She will call me back with cash price of injections. Mike said she didn''t have any pre-x. She even mentioned that he should know better.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-20 17:04:01', '2022-04-20 17:04:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091200011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000091124105', 'Colin Fogerty', NULL, '3-23-22 Colin is on medicaid. He''s 27, healthy, no meds, no tobacco.  Looks like will earn $21K. I can''t tell from my notes. But, looks like he''s been working on own biz which will be live in Nov. 2022. I think he''s still on Medicaid for now until they kick him off.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-20 15:21:49', '2022-04-20 15:21:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091093026', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000051560009', 'Cathy Gavette', NULL, '4-20-22 Cathy called for final questions and she will decide if this is the route they want to go. She thinks she has a better grasp of it all now. Husband does have asthma but never hospitalized, just uses inhaler on occasion. He also had a sinus surgery this year to correct a deviated septum to clear the passage way. Their PCP is Dr. Susan Jacobs and she is in the PHCS network in zip 46077. Husband is also looking to start his own LLC and they have the SRAM shares to show proof of self employment. Full cost is $915/$1000 SECURE with 2 boys, 1 will age out in Dec. of 2022. She knows price will remain the same and likely not increase since this is the new pricing already. Super nice and will let me know if they want to move forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-20 13:21:36', '2022-04-20 13:21:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091052013', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000090393001', 'Jaunius Geleziunas', NULL, '4-18-22 Jaun called about his employee Robby Nelson who takes meds. This was the quote from World MedRX 
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000050667011', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000050680001', 'Paul Noto', NULL, '5-5-20 Paul Noto with firm called Waterlaw wants to set this up for his entire firm. They are currently paying full cost of all family members who are in the firm. They are paying for 8 now. 1 is paid purely in health insurance, another is leaving in a few months. 1 is 67 or 68 and he will encourage him to get onto Medicare. He''s not sure why he''s not on is already. This is good incentive to remove him. So, it will be safest to join as Individuals and do a list bill. Paul will gladly pay for employees on list bill. Paul is also friends with Attorney General (AG) of CO and says if we ever have problems with legal issues he will gladly get AG on board with MCS. Paul believes AG will totally "get it." Paul had a craniotomy in 2015 and last treatment of any kind in 2016, no meds, no symptoms, no treatment, nothing since 2016. One partner has a hear condition with thinning of the walls. He used to be an endurance athlete. He now has to be checked every year or every 6 months and is on a med. I mentioned this partner may want to stay on traditional insurance and needs to 100% understand risks if he chooses this. Other partners have had joint replacements but he''s not sure how recently. He suspects they were more than 3 years ago. He''s not certain. I will talk with each of them to make sure they know pre-x clause and it''s not too risky.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-05 13:17:14', '2020-05-05 13:17:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050667003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000050647001', 'Andrew Martinek', NULL, '5-5-20 Andrew is Suzy Martinek''s son. Suzy speaks very highly of her membership which Andrew realizes is very rare. Andrew is 26 bumped off parent''s plan and now on employer plan. He thinks he''s paying $300 per paycheck every two weeks. Sounds a bit too high since company is also contributing. This includes dental and vision. Has a $7K ded with Anthem. He''s healthy but just had a ranula which is a swollen salivary gland under his tongue. They are keeping an eye on it to make sure surgery is not necessary. He knows all costs related will be his responsibility if he joins MPB. He''s also a mtn biker and wants to protect himself in case of an accident. He does his annual wellness but didn''t do it last year. He''s willing to pay cash for it since price of SDHC is significantly better. $203/$500 best option in my opinion. Lives in Richmond, VA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-05 11:02:06', '2020-05-05 11:03:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050602008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000050601020', 'Alice Madsen', NULL, '5-4-20 Alice is 44 and turning 45 in Nov, 2020. She was laid off in Oct. 2019 and is entering the real estate world which is now the worst time to be doing so. Therefore, has no income at the moment and no insurance. Knows she can join Medicaid but is resisting that. She wants to contact me once she has her first closing, ie. has income again. She''s going to listen to the audio. She has celiac disease and I explained pre-x clause to her. Super nice and spoke a ton with Sarah Price who also explained the membership to her at length.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-04 12:17:40', '2020-05-04 12:17:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050602003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000050601001', 'Machiko Christiansen', NULL, '5-4-20 Machiko uses an interprative call line bc her husband is deaf, so there''s often a delay and another person involved in transferring the calls. Machiko called in on 4-30-20 and wants start dates on 5-1-20. She had little time before had to leave for work and then unavailable until 6:30. I didn''t hear from her again after sending plans, instructions, timelines and everything else. I left two more vm to see where they landed. Husband is getting $680 a week in severance for 10 weeks which is $6800 total from May 1st-July 10th. Machiko''s income is $45K and annualizing husbands brings his to $35,360. She then later said their entire income was $45K which I don''t believe sounds accurate from what she told me. But, she''s not responding either way. I sent them Cigna and Bright Health plans to review. Husbands income may come back when furlough over, plus he had 3 sources of income, 1 furlough, 1 laid off and 1 church.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-05-04 11:11:17', '2020-05-04 11:11:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050538022', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000050473002', 'Barrie Pressly', NULL, '4-29-20 Barrie is 53, healthy, no tobacco. She has coaching biz and nursing biz. She doesn''t have ins now but had LHS last year for 6 months and dropped it once heard people were having trouble getting reimbursed. Discussed PDHC bc of age. Lives in FL and needs glaucoma screening and skin screening but knows those aren''t shared unless has new diagnosis. They aren''t included in ACA preventive services. She has an accident policy that is around $63 a month that she will see if she can cancel or lower the amounts. Was going to enroll today and then tomorrow. But, now is waiting until 5/11/20 to enroll so she has funds ready to be used.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-04-30 13:08:23', '2020-12-08 16:20:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000050538008', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000036488131', 'Heidi Huisjen', NULL, '4-30-20 Heidi is 55 and I talked a year ago. She''s now looking to possibly stop working at Children''s Hospital this summer or may lose job.  She has autoimmune issues and Epstein Barr. Hasn''t had issues with it in the past 36 months. Warren is 62 and has gout and joint issues. They take meds but couldn''t remember them right now. She wants to keep her PCP, Dr. Annie Anderson Moore, Internal Medicine Dr. There''s another Annie Moore who is a pediatrician and not the right Dr. PDHC is best bc of age. Told her to split membership and cost is $842 total at the $1500 IUA level. Trad ins with Dr. Annie Moore is only Anthem starting at $1400 a month with $8150 ded and mop! 
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000027197033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000027220001', 'Stephanie Campbell', NULL, '11-27-18 She had breast cancer in 2007 and had reconstructive surgery. Has to have it done again but Dr. will pay for it bc he messed up. Had 2 foot surgeries last year and still not sure if it''s good or not, although Dr. says it''s healing well.  She was also in rehab for a month for alcohol and then something about 2 more months I think outpatient to cont dealing with the problem. She says she''s done with it all now and is fine. Divorce just went through and wants a Jan. 1st start date. She also can have ins through USAA for around same price. I will encourage her to go with the USAA plan since pre-x isn''t relevant. She will get her colonoscopy and other visits done now on her UHC ins before she switches. Quoted her $1500 / $368 for the Co-Pay Network plan. She sees foot Dr. 2x per year, derm 1x and PCP 1-2x and says done with mental health...if that''s possible.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-27 09:06:17', '2018-11-27 09:06:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026980003', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000026966019', 'Sabrina Lombardi', NULL, '11-20-18 Excellence health, 38 and 7 yr old daughter. Was hoping to include her significant other but they are not married so he''d need his own membership. He''s a naturopath. She likes the annual wellness visits included. She''s also looking at Aliera for under $500 also. I told her the challenges some folks are having to get reimbursed. She might enroll today to fund HSA for 2018 but more likely to wait for Jan. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-20 10:16:08', '2018-11-20 10:16:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026908033', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000026910048', 'Rachel Fleit', NULL, '11-19-18 Rachel is with Oscar Ins through Marketplace in NY now and paying $387 a month.  She even gets $100-$120 APTC. She has No pre-x, no tobacco, drugs or anything. She''s 37 and likes the $1500 / $269 option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-19 16:14:16', '2018-11-19 16:14:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026908028', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000026910028', 'Hope Glazener', NULL, '11-19-18 Wants a Jan. 1st start date and prefers the Association membership, NOT MPB Group. Already has an HSA, has 2 9 yr old twins and going through divorce right now. Paying $1600 for entire family, self-employed. Send her PSDHC email #1 and enrollment instructions for new platform.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-19 15:43:17', '2018-11-19 15:43:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026810043', 'lead', 'zcrm_1579374000026794047', 'Kim Unknown', NULL, '11-16-18 "Hi Wendy,
