  ('zcrm_1579374000182481046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000182412135', 'Thomas Sigman', NULL, '3-13-26 Thomas is also 58 and has 3RX that he takes for high blood pressure - olmesartan, high cholesterol - atorvastatin and uric acid - allopurinol to prevent gout. They are all under $15 on GoodRX. He does a colonscopy every 3 years due to polyp removal. I let him know that might be coded as diagnostic and he''d have to pay his chosen IUA, if so and then costs likely shared above that point. He doesn''t need another colonoscopy for another year or so. He''s a bit scattered. He didn''t eat all day today. He''s a W2 employee for the same company for 25 years. They don''t offer health benefits. There are now only 5 people there and 2 are on Medicaid. He earns dividends from a commercial real estate investment which he gets  a K1 from. I searched a K1 and it says it''s not considered as self-employment. So, Premium Care will be best and is the most affordable anyhow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-13 15:16:37', '2026-03-13 15:18:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182481041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000182412135', 'Thomas Sigman', NULL, '3-13-26 Thomas called C4 yesterday and asked for them to give him his $1100 back and they can''t. So, he shut down his auto pay so he won''t be billed again. I shared with him the new amount is $421.21 not the $683 I quoted him accidentally yesterday. Either way, it''s too expensive. He was paying under $200 last year and was hoping for that again. The cheapest and best option is Premium Care $299/$1000, $267/$1500 and I just left a vm letting him know of the price change to $324/$1000, $293/$1500. I also told him I am willing to waive the $100 of the $125!  I know he''s strapped for cash and it will be very helpful to him. We are meeting again on Thursday, March 19th at 2:00.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-13 15:12:33', '2026-03-13 15:12:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182481033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000182412135', 'Thomas Sigman', NULL, '3-12-26 Thomas missed all emails and notiication to update his C4 account with updated income so they billed him at the full amount which broke his bank. I updated it and this is what would be moving forward:<br><br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Disenrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Thomas Sigman</span></p><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Cigna Connect Flex Silver 2750 Rx Copay</b></span></p><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$2,750</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$10,100</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span><br><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span><br><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 03/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>$421.21 /month </b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">after $683.63 financial help</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Exchange policy number:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 4007608549</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Coverage dates:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 01/01/26 - 03/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Last updated:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 03/12/26</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-13 15:05:32', '2026-03-13 15:05:46'),
