  ('zcrm_1579374000182462013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165196002', 'Paul DiCicco', '03/13/2026', '<span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Paul writes to express ongoing frustration with accessing </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>preventive care</b></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> through the PHCS Specific Services network. Despite successfully scheduling and processing preventive visits for his two sons, Paul himself was later denied a physical by the same provider, who claimed the plan wasn’t contracted—creating confusion and inconsistency.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">He explains that multiple in‑network providers listed under Multiplan/PHCS have refused to accept the plan once they realize it’s the </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i>PHCS Specific Services</i></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> version. This has resulted in hours of phone calls, delays in basic preventive care, and the need to consider switching primary care providers.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Given that he lives in Massachusetts, where Minimum Creditable Coverage requirements apply, Paul notes that MPB’s Secure HSA plan is the only compliant option—but that it relies on the problematic PHCS network. He asks whether there are any other options or workarounds to avoid switching healthshare organizations.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">My reply acknowledges the frustration, clarifies a practical alternative (using out‑of‑network providers and submitting for reimbursement), and informs him that MPB is transitioning to a </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>no‑network MEC</b></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> within about three months, which should simplify preventive care.</span>', 'Tupac Manzanarez', 'Tupac Manzanarez', '2026-03-13 09:16:20', '2026-03-13 09:16:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000182462008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176946015', 'Julie Alley', '3/13/2026', 'Emailed Julie back in regard to her needing to cancel the appointment for today and she went ahead and rescheduled the welcome call for the 19th @1pm...rc', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-03-13 09:06:18', '2026-03-13 09:06:18'),
