  ('zcrm_1579374000181774078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155863360', 'Paula Jessen', NULL, '3-3-26 Paula and husband just had a baby on Jan. 13th. They are in a bind with their employer plan not allowing them to add their newborn. If they don''t allow him to be added, they will choose an Anthem Gold plan for about $310 or Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $0 for $339. Otherwise if they can get the employer plan then they''ll choose the cheapest plan such as Select Bronze $6900 for around $234 (?). With a newborn you have 60 days to add the baby and to backdate to the DOB. She will let me know what they learn from the employer and how they plan to proceed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-03 15:22:45', '2026-03-03 15:25:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181748280', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000159492001', 'Nina Itin', '03/03/2026', 'cancellation - left a vm', 'Tupac Manzanarez', 'Tupac Manzanarez', '2026-03-03 15:01:28', '2026-03-03 15:01:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181774068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148917016', 'Herman Kirby', NULL, '3-3-26 The kids are on and off of Medicaid and CHP+. This is the reason for wacky commissions. They are currently on Medicaid for now. Herman has disability due to kidney failure. Brianna was concerned about what to do for herself since they don''t qualify for ACA with the above parameters with Medicare and Disability. She''s super healthy and no pre-x in the past 36 months.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-03 14:41:20', '2026-03-03 14:41:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181740130', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176146001', 'Sarah Starr', '3/3/2026', 'Stanton got a fax number for the telehealth provider to send referral orders, transferred to lyric so he could relay it ...rc', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-03-03 14:27:34', '2026-03-03 14:27:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181757188', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118543002', 'Kelcey Nichols', NULL, 'Sent Change Form out to update spouses email', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2026-03-03 14:26:47', '2026-03-03 14:26:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181739301', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175820002', 'Michael Carpenter', NULL, 'Member submitted his cancellation form today, due to Aging into Medicare eff 05/26. Member will age into Medicare on 04/01/26 as his DOB is 05/01/26.  Therefore I did not send Member the 1st Primary Member Turning 65 Notice.', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2026-03-03 14:26:00', '2026-03-03 14:28:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181786008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176472047', 'Gopal Krishnan', NULL, '03/03/2026 - Responded to Gopal''s questions  regarding Pryia''s well woman visit.  SW', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-03-03 14:21:40', '2026-03-03 14:21:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181774063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148917016', 'Herman Kirby', NULL, '3-3-26 Brianna called to find out what happens when they show that Herman has disability with Part A and B Medicare. I wasn''t sure. This is what a search says:<br><span style="color:rgb(70, 70, 73);">Yes, you can have Medicare Part A and Part B and still be eligible for an ACA premium subsidy under certain conditions. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(70, 70, 73);">However, you are not eligible for ACA premium subsidies if you are enrolled in premium-free Medicare Part A (which is the case for most SSDI recipients after the 24-month waiting period).  Once your Medicare Part A and Part B coverage begins, your eligibility for Marketplace subsidies ends. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(70, 70, 73);">Key points:</span><br><ul style="list-style-type:disc;list-style-position:inside;"><li style="list-style-image:none;"><p style="display:inline;"><span style="margin-inline-start:24px;color:rgb(51, 51, 51);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">If you are receiving SSDI and have not yet reached the 24-month waiting period for Medicare, you are eligible to enroll in a Marketplace plan and receive premium tax credits if your income is at least 100% of the federal poverty level. </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;"><p style="display:inline;"><span style="margin-inline-start:24px;color:rgb(51, 51, 51);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">Once your Medicare coverage starts (after 24 months of SSDI), you lose eligibility for ACA subsidies. </span></p></li><li style="list-style-image:none;"><p style="display:inline;"><span style="margin-inline-start:24px;color:rgb(51, 51, 51);font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;">If you keep both Medicare and Marketplace coverage, Medicare is the primary payer, and you will have to pay the full price for Marketplace premiums unless you drop the Marketplace plan. </span></p></li></ul><span style="color:rgb(70, 70, 73);">Important: Your SSDI payments are not counted as income for ACA subsidy eligibility, but your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) — which includes other income sources — determines your subsidy eligibility.  If you are still in the 24-month waiting period for Medicare, you may qualify for subsidies. </span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-03-03 14:17:05', '2026-03-03 14:17:05'),
