  ('zcrm_1579374000181649001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129391002', 'Robert Columbo', '3/2/2026', 'I followed up on Roberts voicemail, he had general membership questions: Preventive v. Diagnostic, Telehealth, Dermatology, PHCS Network. Answered all of his questions...rc', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-03-02 07:23:42', '2026-03-02 07:23:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181646017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178425035', 'Molly Kopan', NULL, 'Member updated payment method via website portal', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2026-03-02 07:22:59', '2026-03-02 07:22:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181646012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000159874001', 'Gavin Goff', NULL, 'Member updated payment method via website portal', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2026-03-02 07:21:41', '2026-03-02 07:21:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181630006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165196002', 'Paul DiCicco', 'Reverted back to previous membership', 'Member &amp; Fam $1250 Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2026-02-28 09:49:30', '2026-02-28 09:49:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181630001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165196002', 'Paul DiCicco', NULL, 'Tupac requested that this member be reverted back to the Secure since he lives in MA (an Ind Mandate State).  I told him I would make an exception since it could involve a tax penalty.  I will charge the member the difference of $44 for the MEC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2026-02-28 09:48:29', '2026-02-28 09:48:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181572036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169950023', 'Michelle Maziar', NULL, '2-23-26 After speaking with Rachelle once she looked into Michelle''s case, Rachelle''s best recommendation is for the client to send a note back to the Needs Determination Team asking if she got a doctor prescription for the Need if they would then share in the cost? I called Michelle and let her know this was their best recommendation. She has no desire to spend more money on a Dr. visit to possible get reimbursed for the need. She believes Zion keeps moving the goal post. Bottom line Zion now has in their Sharing Guidelines that members are not allowed to self-refer for situations like this. They must have an open need prescribed by a medical professional and then properly approved for sharing. I see both sides and there''s no way for either side to come together. Michelle has chosen to cancel wants to pursue getting her money back for a bunch of months. I let her know that the determination is up to Zion and I sent her the Sharing Guidelines to review. She will review the contracts she signed when joining as well. She stopped seeking care for her hip now that sharing has been denied. Patti cancelled her before she was billed again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-27 16:26:33', '2026-02-27 16:26:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000181572031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169950023', 'Michelle Maziar', NULL, '2-27-26 Michelle is looking to get money back since Zion took so long to provide a denial for a Needs Request for her hip pain. She spent $1100 on PT in 2025 with a PT prescription to also include acupuncture. Here''s what I sent to Zion when Michelle called to find out about the denial.<br><span><br></span><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">I just got off the phone with Michelle Maziar who is quite frustrated with Zon''s Needs process. She has submitted for cancellation due to her frustration. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Michelle submitted a Needs Request including the treatment plan on November 7th. She said Zion''s portal was having trouble that day. So, she then had to submit her documentation via email. She had a bike accident which caused hip pain. She used a Board Certified Physical Therapist to prescribe a treatment plan. It took until Dec. 7</span><sup style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);display:inline;">th</sup><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> for Zion to request her records which she signed the HIPAA form on the 8th. It sounds like there were additional communications that further delayed the process. Then it took until Jan. 27</span><sup style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);display:inline;">th</sup><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> for her request to be denied. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">She had $1100 in costs by Dec. 31st. She halted all care when the process wasn''t moving forward. She still has hip pain and no relief with her member sharing request. Per the below Needs Determination, if a </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Board Certified Physical Therapist isn''t sufficient to prescribe the treatment plan, why wasn''t this conveyed to her immediately upon submission of the treatment plan on Nov. 7th? It</span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> took 3 months while she''s been in pain for her to learn that nothing will be shared. This is such a small request.</span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Can you please take a look at why this was such a struggle for her? It would be super helpful if Zion could approve the Sharing Request. They will keep the member happy and active for a very small Need. Otherwise she will proceed  with her cancelation. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-27 16:20:27', '2026-02-27 16:20:27'),
