  ('zcrm_1579374000181050051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148811391', 'Kellylyn Gaffney', '2/20/2026', 'Kellylyn emailed about how to get labs done, i sent her: <br><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">For </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>preventive </b></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">labs (no symptoms, routine) under your Secure HSA plan you can walk into a local LabCorp or Quest etc.. And hand over your physical card or digital card with the "Submit Claims To" address on the back of it to ALT Risk for billing on your behalf. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Now, </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>diagnostic</b></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> labs (Labs ordered due to symptoms) work is a little different that will become your responsibility; you can get your lab order and send it to us, and we can find you the best pricing. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">The only thing you need to do is speak to your provider and find out if they are preventive routine labs or diagnostic and then move forward accordingly. </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">RC</span></p>', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-02-20 07:43:35', '2026-02-20 07:43:35'),
