  ('zcrm_1579374000180474001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000180451002', 'Alicia Swaby', 'Member & Sp $1000 IUA Premium Care + Tobacco', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2026-02-11 06:48:15', '2026-02-11 06:48:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000180431170', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000180451002', 'Alicia Swaby', NULL, '2-10-26 Alicia found me through Jason Barnicoat and Todd (?). She chose to give the referral to Jason knowing he gets paid $100. She is 44 and husband is 41. They live in Glenwood Springs and work for Glenwood Canyon Brewery. She prefers to get check up every 6 months for her Adderall meds. She wasn''t ever diagnosed with ADHD but might be and prefers sticking with adderall. They don''t have any ins at the moment. She had a preventive colonoscopy which cost her $11K! They removed a few polyps and drastically inflated the bill with every new bill that came in with each aspect of the visit. By the end it cost $11K at Valley View Hospital. She''s paid it off. Colon cancer runs in her family she is overly cautious. She doesn''t need another colonoscopy for 5 years. She''s willing to drive to the Front Range to get it done. I found it for $1300 in Wheatridge or $1595-$1795 in Denver, Greeley, etc. She does want a mammo as well. I told her about the 6 month waiting period for both and the $600 and $2500 for each. They are both W2 workers and no self-employment. So, Premium Care is best. They are both tobacco users and now willing to quit. It''s a great incentive for them to quit with the $75 additonal amount and limits once they turn 50. She''s eager to quit! They chose Premium Care $1000/$603 + $75 = $678 and might pay with CC simply bc it''s the easiest way to deal with their finances. Total cost will be about $698.34. All set for March 1st start date!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-10 21:44:44', '2026-02-10 21:44:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000180431112', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000180427019', 'William Llewelyn', NULL, '2-10-26 Reed''s official name is William but he goes by Reed. He''s 59 and lives in Glenwood Springs, CO. He works for Rebel Bikes', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-10 21:31:23', '2026-02-10 21:31:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000180431073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000132943002', 'Wallace Reid', NULL, '2-10-26 1Dental - <a style="display:inline;" target="_blank" href="http://trayreid4@yahoo.com/"><u>trayreid4@yahoo.com</u></a> just purchased a plan from your link! You will earn commission once the member is active beyond the 30-day trial period.<br>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-10 20:37:17', '2026-02-10 20:37:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000180431060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122226002', 'Karin Nance', NULL, '2-10-26 Karin called to understand why she hasn''t received the link to cancel yet. I let her know I was waiting for Zion to figure out the best process to keep her membership showing as active since Aug. 2023. I spoke with Rachelle and they weren''t even finding her in their system. Rachelle is reaching out again and she''s going to let me know the best way to re-enroll her and keep her connected to me via MPB, if she wants. Karin is a little frustrated by the computer age and how it makes things difficult. But, she will be patient.  <br>Update, I called her back thinking that Premium Care could be good for her. But, she''s getting Zion at $777 at the $1250 IUA level. Premium Care is $777 at the $1500 level and the price will likely change for June 1st, 2026. So, she wants to stick with Zion. She''s an alternative practitioner and doesn''t do the mammos or colonoscopies ever.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-10 15:15:07', '2026-02-10 15:21:50'),
