  ('zcrm_1579374000180209011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000182477018', 'Gene Greene', NULL, '2-4-26 It looks like the hardest part might be to find diabetic supplies for her son. He needs a Dexacom, glucose monitor, insulin and something about infusion sites. <br><br>This is what they are getting for his needs with insurance - <br>Here are Jett''s needs:<br><br>Baqsimi 3Mg Spray, Non Aerosol - he will need a few of these per year<br><br>Dexcom G7 Sensor 1 every 10 days, for 9 on our current plan for a base price of 1611.36, insurance pays 1062.78, savings of 458.58 and we pay 90.00<br>Through MPower per Wendy: $121 each - $364 per month<br><br>Novolog 100 ml vials - 4 vials per month - $410.83, Insurance covered $250.29, Savings of 135.54, we pay $25 for 4 vials.<br><span><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">We pay $25 for 2 nose spray bottles.</span><br>Thanks again!<br>Sara', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-02-05 13:44:25', '2026-02-05 14:09:50'),
