, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">02/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"> $0.00 </span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Exchange policy number:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 3774801850</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Coverage dates:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 02/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Last updated:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 01/30/26</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-30 12:46:12', '2026-01-30 12:46:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179870021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000177130015', 'Noelle Orr', '01/30/2026', 'Welcome Call Complete.', 'Tupac Manzanarez', 'Tupac Manzanarez', '2026-01-30 12:38:23', '2026-01-30 12:38:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179868006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000179868021', 'Tyler Penson', NULL, '1-30-26 Ty came to me via Suzy Martinek. Ty left his job in Nov. 2025 and his benefits ended Nov. 30th. If he chooses Cobra it will be $3500 per month and he hasn''t paid yet. So, he needs a Feb. 1st start date to avoid Cobra. He is very interessted in Secure HSA at $1250/$817. Not sure if I mentioned $125/$25.  He is planning to be self-employed. His wife is just finished getting her nurse practitioner license and might get a part-time job. He thinks she could get benfits that way possibly in the future. She might not be given benefits as part-time. He''s planning to remain self-employed. He been doing accounting but he''s deciding what to do next away from accounting. They are both 32 with a 2 and almost 1 year old. They prefer traditional healthcare. He is on blood pressure medication for 2 years and that''s it for any pre-x for the entire family. He takes losartan which is super affordable and likely on the drug list. <br>Since he needs something for Feb. 1st, we looked at C4 for the one month until he can start Secure HSA. He chose the Cigna Connect Flex 7200 for $1434.20. He will upload his Cobra letter and update his son Harvey''s SS# since C4 is asking for it. He must have typed it in wrong.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-30 12:37:42', '2026-01-30 12:37:42'),
