  ('zcrm_1579374000179831021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000177748019', 'Mike Phillips', NULL, 'Member submitted Cancellation eff prior to start due to the fact that he did not know what he enrolled in.  Since he went through HSA for America he did not get any information or presentation on the membership.  He ended up going "another way".  I will refund him all monies back &amp; cancel membership prior to start.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2026-01-30 09:02:31', '2026-01-30 09:02:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179832026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165196002', 'Paul DiCicco', '1/30/2026', 'I also have another question for you. Up until this point, I have been self-employed and contracting through a company that is looking to bring me on as a W-2 employee. They don''t currently offer health insurance, so I''m looking to stay with MPB Health. However, I noticed that the Secure HSA plan I''m currently on is designed for those who are self-employed or business owners. Would we need to switch to a different plan if I become a W-2 employee? If so, it looks like your Direct plan for individuals and families would be most comparable. Can you help me understand the difference between this plan and the Secure HSA plan?<br><span><br></span><span><br></span>Paul emailed with this question, trying to set up a time to speak and let him know the options..&gt;RC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-30 09:00:10', '2026-01-30 09:00:10'),
